+[{"u": "/", "t": "Home [en]", "l": "en", "x": "Nexus Scalp Engine documentation homepage what's new capabilities architecture research"}, {"u": "/releases/", "t": "Releases [en]", "l": "en", "x": "releases v9.0.8 changelog what's new history 959d7d9"}, {"u": "/architecture/code-navigation/", "t": "Code Navigation Map — Nexus Scalp Engine [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Architecture  /  code navigation  \n Code Navigation Map — Nexus Scalp Engine \n  Where to find things, for a developer (or agent) landing fresh in this repo.  This map is an INDEX. Detailed truth lives in:  -  agents/skill.md  — authoritative architecture map + repo contract (READ FIRST)  -  docs/architecture/dependency-map.md  — subsystem edges + contracts  -  docs/architecture/comment-style.md  — comment/doc conventions  -  docs/RELEASE.md  — CLI exit codes, update protocol, release verification  -  agents/bugs.md  — bug ledger (append-only; grep  ^## BUG-  tail for next free id)  \n Startup &amp; lifecycle \n  \n   Concern  Where    \n  Primary launcher (bootstrap sys.path, adapter bind, engine + web)   NexusTradingForexBot.py   \n  CLI entry ( nexus  /  nse , Typer)   src/nexus_scalp/cli/main.py   \n  Engine construction + async tick loop   src/nexus_scalp/application/live_engine.py  ( ru"}, {"u": "/architecture/comment-style/", "t": "Comment Style Guide — Nexus Scalp Engine [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Architecture  /  comment style  \n Comment Style Guide — Nexus Scalp Engine \n  Applies to all Python source in  src/ ,  tests/ , and  scripts/ .  Repo rule of thumb:  the repository should not contain more comments — it should contain better comments.   \n The one test \n  Could a competent developer derive this from the code itself?  \n If YES → do not comment. If NO → the comment may be valuable; then ask: \n \"Will this still be true and useful six months from now?\" If NO → do not write it. \n What comments are FOR \n A comment must be one of: \n  \n   Category  Documents  Example    \n  INVARIANT  a rule the code must keep but does not enforce visibly  \"Resume-safe hash: the hasher must cover the already-downloaded bytes too.\"  \n  SAFETY  fail-closed / fail-safe semantics  \"Fail closed: no inference must never yield a trade decision.\"  \n  CONCURRENCY  lock ownership, ordering, atomicity  \"Hol"}, {"u": "/architecture/control-center-ui/", "t": "Control Center UI Architecture (CHG-0043, TASK-CONTROL-CENTER) [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Architecture  /  control center ui  \n Control Center UI Architecture (CHG-0043, TASK-CONTROL-CENTER) \n  Operator-facing architecture of the NEXUS Control Center. UI-owned doc;  backend architecture lives in  docs/architecture/  elsewhere. Status  semantics here are the CONTRACT for every future CC view.  \n Purpose \n One coherent surface where an operator answers, without reading logs: \n WHAT is happening → WHY → WHAT changed → WHAT is blocked → WHAT is healthy → \n WHAT is serving → WHY did/didn't a trade happen → WHAT is safe to do next. \n Observation model: OBSERVE → UNDERSTAND → INVESTIGATE → ACT → VERIFY. \n Navigation &amp; Screens \n  \n   Tab (nav id)  Screen  Data sources (all read-only)    \n  Control Center ( tab-control-center )  Overview: mode banner, 6-tile status strip (Runtime/Data/Model/Inference/Database/MT5), runtime truth, market snapshot, latest decision, active warnings"}, {"u": "/architecture/crash-safety/", "t": "Crash-Safety Architecture (NSE) [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Architecture  /  crash safety  \n Crash-Safety Architecture (NSE) \n  Status: HARDENED_WITH_GAPS baseline documented 2026-09-01 (rev 2 — checker  regex fix + 381-site silent-handler backlog tracked as P1 violations).  Owner: Nexus-Main (crash-containment master pass).  Scope: the failure contract of every major execution boundary, from process  startup through model tensor execution, trading execution, Web/API, updater,  release pipeline, and shutdown.  Companion documents:  failure-recovery-matrix.md  (per-subsystem failure  matrix),  artifacts/forensics/crash-safety-audit.json  (machine audit).  \n \n 1. Governing principle \n The requirement is NOT \"the application must never crash\". The requirement is: \n  ⧉   NO SILENT CRASH      NO SILENT EXCEPTION      NO FALSE SUCCESS\nNO FAKE HEALTH       NO FABRICATED MODEL OUTPUT\nNO UNSAFE TRADING AFTER CRITICAL FAILURE\nNO CORRUPTED STATE AFTER FAI"}, {"u": "/architecture/data-flow/", "t": "Data Flow — Tick to Decision [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Architecture  /  Data Flow  \n Data Flow — from tick to decision \n This is the canonical path (from  agents/skill.md  §4). Every arrow is a \n contract boundary. \n  ⧉   TickData (MT5 / paper / gateway)\n  → ScalpFeatureEngine.to_tensor_input()\n      50D base (scalp_v1 · FEATURE_NAMES · [-3,+3] · finite)\n  → assemble_70d / build_70d_vector()\n      70D canonical: Base 0..49 | News 10D 50..59 | Liquidity 10D 60..69\n  → InferenceContractValidator\n      scaler dim == feature dim · schema hash · finite · bounds\n  → ScalpNet → 4 logits (NO_TRADE / BUY / SELL / WAIT) → confidence gate 0.35\n  → regime_classifier (Regime Guardian)\n  → signals/policy + rule_matrix (~30 rules, TTL 5s cache)\n  → RiskEngine.calculate_dynamic_volume() + evaluate_proposal()\n      free-margin 20% clamp · tier caps · HARD_MAX_LOTS\n  → OrderManager (60-scenario router · 11 position states ·\n      MAX_TOTAL_EXPOSURE=1 · 30s "}, {"u": "/architecture/database/", "t": "Database Architecture [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Architecture  /  Database  \n Database Architecture \n Canonical stores \n  \n   DB  Contents  Notes    \n   artifacts/audit.db   trading ledger, experience outcomes, accounting, research registry, strategy lifecycle, incidents, hygiene  one canonical ledger; SQLite  WAL   \n   artifacts/news.db   news ingestion, analysis, consensus, impacts  lazy schema on first save  \n   candle_intel.db   candle intelligence  versioned schema  \n  settings DB  secrets + user intent (Telegram creds via  settings_service )  never in YAML (INV-010)  \n   \n Write path \n  AuditRepository  queues writes to a  background worker thread  — the tick \n hot path never performs synchronous DB work (INV-001). Historical \n experience/outcome/ledger rows are  immutable  (INV-007); corrections go \n through evidence → reconstruction → derived records with provenance, never row \n rewrites. \n Migrations \n  src/nexus_scalp/datab"}, {"u": "/architecture/dependency-map/", "t": "Architecture Dependency Map — Nexus Scalp Engine (NSE) [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Architecture  /  dependency map  \n Architecture Dependency Map — Nexus Scalp Engine (NSE) \n  Maintained per the MASTER MULTI-AGENT CONTRACT §9 (see  agents/multi-agent-git-contract.md ).  Describes actual subsystem relationships (verified against executable code; see agents/skill.md for the full inventory).  Every edge documents: contract, direction, expected data, safety guarantees.  \n Canonical high-level flow \n  ⧉   MT5\n  │  (tick/order/position/account events)\n  ▼\nMT5 Adapter / Providers            [ports: IMT5Port; adapters: mt5/, paper/, remote]\n  │  (normalized events)\n  ▼\nLiveEngine (async event loop)      [src/nexus_scalp/application/live_engine.py]\n  ├─ Feature Engine                [features/scalp_features.py → FEATURE_VECTOR_50D]\n  ├─ Model Runtime                 [models/scalp_net.py → MODEL_MANIFEST; Champion/Challenger]\n  ├─ News Context                  [news/ → NEWS_CO"}, {"u": "/architecture/execution-pipeline/", "t": "Execution Pipeline [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Architecture  /  Execution Pipeline  \n Execution Pipeline \n  execution/order_manager.py  is the single dispatch authority (INV-004). It is \n large by design (convention-locked hot path) and is being decomposed \n surgically, seam by seam, with golden tests. \n Path of an order \n  ⧉   TradeProposal (frozen domain contract, execution_id trace)\n  → policy/confluence checks (SMC matrix, Regime Guardian, confidence gate)\n  → RiskEngine.evaluate_proposal() → dynamic volume (fractional Kelly)\n  → OrderManager router (60 scenarios: fills, rejections, partials, errors)\n  → IMT5Port adapter (Win32 IPC / ZMQ / paper)\n  → position lifecycle (11 states with hysteresis)\n  → protective exits (SL/TP first-touch, breakeven lock, profit giveback,\n      adaptive exit protection)\n  → broker reconciliation (broker truth wins — INV-011)\n  → accounting + autopsy (immutable ledger)   \n Hard clamps (never bypass"}, {"u": "/architecture/failure-recovery-matrix/", "t": "Failure-Recovery Matrix (NSE crash-containment pass) [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Architecture  /  failure recovery matrix  \n Failure-Recovery Matrix (NSE crash-containment pass) \n  Status: baseline 2026-09-01. Companion to  crash-safety.md  and   artifacts/forensics/crash-safety-audit.json .  Every row = subsystem × failure → expected console log, state, recovery,  exit, and the test that proves it. GREEN means failure-injected → detected →  logged → safe behavior → regression exists (never \"a try/except exists\").  \n Legend — State: truthful runtime state after the failure. Log: minimum \n console/file record. Rec: recovery policy. Exit: CLI/process exit contract. \n Test: primary regression evidence. \n  \n   #  Subsystem  Failure  Log (console)  State  Rec  Exit  Test    \n  1  startup  missing/invalid config at launch  red panel  cfg_detail=Parse error…  + doctor FAIL  NOT READY  halt  1 / EXIT_RUNTIME  launcher doctor contract; BUG-149/156 lineage  \n  2  startup   _"}, {"u": "/architecture/model-pipeline/", "t": "Model Pipeline [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Architecture  /  Model Pipeline  \n Model Pipeline \n Lifecycle \n  ⧉   DATASET (versioned artifact + quality gates + fingerprint)\n  → EXPERIMENT (equal budgets/seeds/splits; dataset-fairness gate)\n  → CANDIDATE MODEL (+ manifest: schema hash · scaler · dataset ID · git commit)\n  → VALIDATION (walk-forward · OOS gate · robustness · calibration)\n  → REGISTRY (content-addressed; challenger only)\n  → LOAD GATE (10 gates, enforced at every attach)\n  → SHADOW PARITY (zero order authority)\n  → OPERATOR PROMOTION (READY_FOR_REVIEW → APPROVED → CHAMPION; atomic transaction)\n  → ROLLBACK PREVIEW / EMERGENCY FREEZE   \n Artifact-first Model Factory ( model_generation/ ) \n Datasets, experiments and models are **versioned filesystem artifacts with \n manifests** — inference needs no database. The manifest carries \n  feature_schema_hash ,  training_dataset_id , scaler identity and git commit. \n ScalpNet"}, {"u": "/architecture/observability-log-contract/", "t": "Observability Log Contract — frozen 2026-09-01 (Agent 2) [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Architecture  /  observability log contract  \n Observability Log Contract — frozen 2026-09-01 (Agent 2) \n Authoritative in-repo reference for the log-noise contracts proven in the \n operational-observability sprint and pinned by \n  tests/unit/test_operational_log_hygiene.py  + \n  tests/unit/test_observability_contract_freeze.py  + \n  tests/unit/test_logging_redaction.py . \n Any future change to these behaviors MUST update those tests in the same \n commit (test-first rule: a new repetitive runtime event needs an \n aggregation/transition/rate-limit test before merge). \n Companion tooling:  src/nexus_scalp/observability/event_aggregator.py  \n (EventBatchAggregator — bounded, thread-safe, first-occurrence-immediate). \n \n Core invariants (all events) \n \n SEVERITY ladder: DEBUG = diagnostic detail; INFO = normal state / bounded \n \n informational transitions; WARNING = first failure or action"}, {"u": "/architecture/observability-map/", "t": "Observability Map — Nexus Scalp Engine (NSE) [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Architecture  /  observability map  \n Observability Map — Nexus Scalp Engine (NSE) \n  TASK-OBS-AUDIT (2026-08-31, HEAD baseline 1f60832; delivered at dcc80d7).  Agent: Hermes-ObsForensic. AUDIT-ONLY: zero runtime code changed.  Machine-readable companion:  artifacts/forensics/observability-audit.json .  Method: black-box reconstruction from runtime evidence (logs / DBs / artifacts /  live API / CLI) FIRST, then targeted read-only code sweeps for every claim.  Evidence markers: [L]=live-probed today, [DB]=DB census, [LOG]=log sample, [C]=code file:line.  \n 1. What the system actually produces today \n  \n   Channel  Reality (verified)    \n  Logs  severity-split  logs/{critical,error,warning,info}/YYYY/MM/*.log , ISO-8601  +03:30 , 10 MB part rotation, retention 30/30/90/365 d [C observability/logging.py:388-394]. Only 08-29 + 08-31 exist; 08-30 absent. ~190 MB on 08-31 (131 MB error).  \n "}, {"u": "/architecture/observability/", "t": "Observability [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Architecture  /  Observability  \n Observability \n NSE treats observability as a subsystem with contracts, not a logging afterthought. \n If the engine cannot show  why  it did something, its behavior is indistinguishable \n from a bug — so showing why is engineered, not hoped for. \n Structured logging ( observability/logging.py ) \n \n Severity-split, date-organized storage:  logs/&lt;sev&gt;/YYYY/MM/YYYY-MM-DD.log . \n ISO-8601 timestamps (broker-local offset aware), event/component/category/ \n \n error-code fields, correlation context. \n \n Daily + size rotation with zero-loss part files; per-severity retention. \n Key + high-entropy redaction; ANSI-free stacks. \n \n Incident response ( incidents/ ) \n Canonical incident model ( INC-YYYY-hex8 , 8 statuses, 5 severities), \n fingerprint correlation, causal-chain timeline reconstruction, value lineage \n with first-divergence location, WHY workflo"}, {"u": "/architecture/order_manager_architecture/", "t": "ORDER_MANAGER.PY — Architectural Map (Agent-5, Phase A) [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Architecture  /  order manager architecture  \n ORDER_MANAGER.PY — Architectural Map (Agent-5, Phase A) \n Evidence base: forensic inventory at HEAD  0015608  (post Agent-4 winner-protection \n sprint  0839da3 ). No edits made during this phase. This document precedes any \n extraction (task brief §24). \n 1. Current shape \n 6372 LOC, 1 god class + 6 support types \n  \n   Item  Span  Notes    \n  Module constants (18)  L60-155  exposure caps, BE/giveback/trailing geometry  \n  ExitMechanism (Enum)  L158  exit taxonomy  \n  PositionState (Enum)  L172  11 in-trade lifecycles  \n  PositionEvaluationStep  L190  trajectory step record  \n  LSFTicketState  L209  LSF per-ticket state  \n  PositionProtectionState  L226  per-ticket protection facts (dataclass)  \n  SmartPositionMetrics  L281  57 derived metrics (dataclass)  \n  OrderLifecycleManager  L348-6372  81 methods, 99 distinct  self.*  state attrs  \n"}, {"u": "/architecture/overview/", "t": "Architecture Overview [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Architecture  /  Overview  \n Architecture Overview \n NSE is  hexagonal (ports-and-adapters) and event-driven . Broker platforms, \n models and network adapters are isolated behind port contracts \n ( IMT5Port ,  IGatewayPort ), so the domain never knows which broker — or \n whether a broker — is attached. \n  ⧉           ┌────────────────────────  ports (contracts)  ───────────────────────┐\n        │                                                                    │\n Market │  ┌──────────┐   ┌──────────┐   ┌─────────┐   ┌────────┐            │\n data ──┼─►│ features │──►│  model   │──►│ signals │──►│  risk  │            │\n (MT5 / │  │ 50D/70D  │   │ ScalpNet │   │ policy  │   │ engine │            │\n paper) │  └──────────┘   └──────────┘   └─────────┘   └───┬────┘            │\n        │                                                  ▼                 │\n        │                         "}, {"u": "/architecture/qa-assurance-contract/", "t": "QA ASSURANCE CONTRACT — Deep Assurance Layer (CHG-0045) [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Architecture  /  qa assurance contract  \n QA ASSURANCE CONTRACT — Deep Assurance Layer (CHG-0045) \n  Owner: Nexus-Main (TASK-QA-DEEP-ASSURANCE). This document is the contract  for the OSS-grade adversarial QA layer: lanes, markers, budgets, the JSON  result schema, and the governance rules for flaky/open-defect tests.  \n 1. Position in the gate hierarchy \n  \n   Lane  Command  When  Budget    \n  Pre-push critical gate (existing, NOT replaced)   beforePush.sh  /  check_local.py   every push  ~2.5 min  \n   Deep assurance — fast    python scripts/qa/deep_assurance.py --fast   PR / push lane in CI  &lt; 60 s  \n   Deep assurance — full    python scripts/qa/deep_assurance.py   main / scheduled / dispatch  &lt; 5 min  \n  Mutation proof   python scripts/qa/run_mutations.py   scheduled / dispatch (weekly)  &lt; 15 min  \n   \n The deep-assurance layer NEVER replaces the runtime gate; it adds \n ind"}, {"u": "/architecture/QA_BLIND_SPOT_MATRIX/", "t": "QA BLIND-SPOT MATRIX — Nexus Scalp Engine [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Architecture  /  QA BLIND SPOT MATRIX  \n QA BLIND-SPOT MATRIX — Nexus Scalp Engine \n  CHG-0045 / TASK-QA-DEEP-ASSURANCE (Nexus-Main, 2026-09-02).  Required first milestone of the OSS-grade adversarial QA brief: prove which  gaps matter BEFORE building test mass. Derived from  agents/bugs.md   (BUG-001..BUG-208) and  agents/change_control.md  (CHG-0001..CHG-0050).  \n 1. Method \n \n  Defect-history mining  — every BUG/CHG row classified by subsystem, \n \n severity (P0 money/execution · P1 decision-path/trust · P2 operator \n trust/diagnostics · P3 robustness), and named regression test. \n \n  Detection-quality audit  — does the named regression test the ROOT \n \n CAUSE or only the incident's symptom path? \n \n  Re-entry analysis  — can the same class return through another door? \n  Verdict  — KEEP / IMPROVE / MERGE / DELETE / MISSING per test family. \n \n 2. Matrix — defect history → detection "}, {"u": "/architecture/repository-hygiene/", "t": "Repository Hygiene Audit — Nexus Scalp Engine [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Architecture  /  repository hygiene  \n Repository Hygiene Audit — Nexus Scalp Engine \n   Date:  2026-08-31 ·  HEAD:   1f60832  (main) ·  Working tree:  UNCHANGED (0 modifications)   Mode:  READ-ONLY forensic librarian pass. Nothing was fixed, moved, deleted, or refactored.   Machine-readable twin:   artifacts/forensics/repository-hygiene-audit.json    2026-08-31 repair pass:  CLEANUP-001/002/003/004/005/006 repaired — networkx declared as runtime dep, psycopg declared via new  postgres  extra, requirements ranges reconciled to pyproject, skill.md runner path fixed, tick_storage.py removed, 32 e2e_cc files archived to  scratch/e2e_cc_archive/ , .pyproj.bak removed.   Scope guard:  excludes all active-agent work (BUG-166..174, anti-crash, decomposition, release).  \n 1. What was analyzed \n \n 1,621 tracked files (724 py / 625 md / 80 json / 22 js / 16 mjs / 15 ps1 / 10 yml) \n 351 Python so"}, {"u": "/architecture/research-stack/", "t": "Research Stack [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Architecture  /  Research Stack  \n Research Stack \n The research side answers one question with evidence: **is this candidate good \n enough to trust — and can we prove it on data it never saw?** \n Pipeline \n  ⧉   DATA (canonical tick/bar datasets, provenance-fingerprinted)\n  → FEATURES (same causal contract as live: 50D base, governed 70D assembly)\n  → LABELING (triple-barrier, purged + embargoed)\n  → TRAINING (deterministic seeds, walk-forward)\n  → BACKTEST (friction-aware: spread / slippage / latency)\n  → WALK-FORWARD VALIDATION\n  → OOS GATE (hard: failure ⇒ REJECTED)\n  → ROBUSTNESS STRESS\n  → COUNTERFACTUAL / STRATIFICATION EVIDENCE\n  → CANDIDATE REGISTRY (content-addressed)\n  → SHADOW COMPARISON (zero order authority)\n  → OPERATOR-GATED PROMOTION   \n Key guarantees \n \n  Leakage prevention (INV-008):  purged + embargoed walk-forward \n \n (Lopez de Prado); broker history REPLACE+ALIGN"}, {"u": "/architecture/runtime-certification-gate/", "t": "Runtime Certification Gate — canonical pre-push contract [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Architecture  /  runtime certification gate  \n Runtime Certification Gate — canonical pre-push contract \n   CHANGE-ID:  CHG-0051 ·  TASK-ID:  TASK-RUNTIME-GATE ·  Status:  ACTIVE   One command. One answer.   python scripts/ci/runtime_gate.py   \n 1. Purpose \n The repository has many test families (runtime, features, 50D/70D, models, \n database, execution, providers, research, CLI, observability, installer, \n integration). The problem was never test count — it was the absence of ONE \n strong, trustworthy, repeatable command answering: \n  \"Is the composed runtime safe, coherent, loadable, and operational enough  for an agent to push its change?\"  \n The Runtime Certification Gate is that command. It is a **curated, layered \n certification of the REAL composed runtime** — not \"run all pytest\". It \n exercises the actual boot path (config → adapter →  LiveEngine  service \n graph → decision pi"}, {"u": "/architecture/runtime/", "t": "Runtime — the LiveEngine Loop [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Architecture  /  Runtime  \n Runtime — the LiveEngine loop \n  application/live_engine.py  is the orchestrator: a single async event loop \n that drives the tick pipeline and coordinates background workers. \n Startup sequence \n \n Launcher binds an adapter ( DirectMT5Adapter  /  RemoteMT5GatewayAdapter  / \n \n paper) behind  IMT5Port . \n \n Pre-flight  doctor gate : MT5 terminal present? config valid? platform \n \n supported? — otherwise the engine refuses to start. \n \n Migration gate: canonical DB migration engine runs (additive, checksummed). \n Model load: Champion bundle validated by the  10-gate load gate  (manifest \n \n hash, scaler dim, schema family, width contract…). \n \n Mode select:  PAPER (default)  / SHADOW / LIVE (interactive confirmation). \n Web server: FastAPI Control Center + SSE + WebSocket. \n Workers start (audit writer, research, hygiene, incidents, Telegram). \n \n Tick pipeli"}, {"u": "/architecture/system-map/", "t": "System Map [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Architecture  /  System Map  \n System Map \n Package inventory ( src/nexus_scalp/ ) \n  ⧉   nexus_scalp/\n├── domain/            frozen Pydantic contracts (TickData, TradeProposal, …)\n├── ports/             IMT5Port · IGatewayPort        ← the hexagon seam\n├── adapters/          mt5/ (Win32 IPC) · gateway (ZMQ) · paper/ · database/ (AuditRepository, WAL)\n├── features/          scalp_features (50D) · schema registry · schema_contract (70D SSoT)\n│                      liquidity_engine · regime_classifier · temporal (research)\n├── models/            ScalpNet (dual-path TCN + self-attention)\n├── training/          walk_forward_trainer · labeling/ (triple-barrier)\n├── signals/           policy · rule matrix (~30 SMC rules)\n├── strategies/        factory (+ provider_gate for LLM/AI services)\n├── risk/              RiskEngine (Kelly sizing, clamps, kill switch)\n├── execution/         order_manag"}, {"u": "/contributing/add-language/", "t": "Adding a Language [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Contributing  /  Adding a Language  \n Adding a Language \n The multilingual architecture is data-driven: adding Turkish, French, Russian, \n Chinese or Japanese is a directory + registry entry — no code changes. \n Recipe \n \n  Create the language tree  \n \n  ⧉      site/content/&lt;lang&gt;/            # translated site content (mirror of en tree)\n   docs/&lt;lang&gt;/index.md            # optional docs-root landing page   \n \n  Register the language  in  scripts/docs/site_config.py : \n \n  ⧉      LANGUAGES = {\n       &quot;en&quot;: {&quot;name&quot;: &quot;English&quot;, &quot;dir&quot;: &quot;ltr&quot;},\n       &quot;fa&quot;: {&quot;name&quot;: &quot;فارسی&quot;,   &quot;dir&quot;: &quot;rtl&quot;},\n       ...\n       &quot;tr&quot;: {&quot;name&quot;: &quot;Türkçe&quot;,  &quot;dir&quot;: &quot;ltr&quot;},   # ← new\n   }   \n \n  Translate core pages first  (in priority order): \n \n  index "}, {"u": "/contributing/contribution-guide/", "t": "Contribution Guide [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Contributing  /  Contribution Guide  \n Contribution Guide \n 0. Read the engineering memory first \n This repository is developed by multiple coordinated AI agents under a strict \n contract. A human contributor benefits from the same discipline: \n \n  \">https://github.com/Opselon/NexusTradingForexBot/blob/main/agents/skill.md\">  agents/skill.md   — authoritative architecture map \n  \">https://github.com/Opselon/NexusTradingForexBot/blob/main/agents/multi-agent-git-contract.md\">  agents/multi-agent-git-contract.md   — the collaboration contract \n  \">https://github.com/Opselon/NexusTradingForexBot/blob/main/agents/contracts.md\">  agents/contracts.md   +  \">https://github.com/Opselon/NexusTradingForexBot/blob/main/agents/runtime_invariants.md\">  agents/runtime_invariants.md   — contracts &amp; invariants \n  \">https://github.com/Opselon/NexusTradingForexBot/blob/main/agents/bugs.md\">  agents/b"}, {"u": "/contributing/documentation/", "t": "Documentation Workflow [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Contributing  /  Documentation Workflow  \n Documentation Workflow \n Ownership \n Documentation is owned by the  Nexus-Docs  role \n (registry:  docs/agent_handoffs/DOCS_REGISTRY.md ). The boundary is hard: \n docs changes never touch runtime code, and code owners never need to fix docs \n tooling. If documentation exposes a suspected code defect, it is recorded in \n the registry with subsystem attribution — the implementation stays untouched. \n Information architecture \n  ⧉   docs/            engineering documentation (markdown, this IA tree)\nsite/            GitHub Pages source (builds docs/ + translations into a static site)\nscripts/docs/    validation tooling (check_docs.py, check_translations.py, build_site.py)\n.github/workflows/docs.yml    docs CI + Pages deploy   \n Source of truth \n \n  English  is the source language; every other language is a translation \n \n with status metadata ( c"}, {"u": "/engineering/ci/", "t": "CI Architecture [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Engineering  /  CI Architecture  \n CI Architecture \n Workflows \n  \n   Workflow  Trigger  Purpose    \n   ci.yml   push (main/develop/ci-tests), PR, weekly drift scan  ruff · format · mypy · pytest (critical; matrix arms for integration/e2e/research/model on demand)  \n   tests-os.yml   matrix OS runs  cross-platform unit sanity  \n   security.yml   PR + weekly schedule  CodeQL + Trivy  \n   osv-scanner.yml   schedule  dependency vulnerabilities  \n   lockfile-diff.yml   dependency file changes  lockfile drift  \n   js-tests.yml   Web/ changes   node --check  + JS tests  \n   release.yml    v*  tags  only   build + verify + publish release artifacts  \n   docker.yml   Docker surface changes  image build gates  \n   docs.yml   docs/site/README changes  documentation validation + Pages deploy (this platform)  \n   \n Trigger policy (CI_TRIGGER_POLICY v1): tags never fire CI (release-only), main \n pu"}, {"u": "/engineering/quality/", "t": "Quality & Testing [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Engineering  /  Quality &amp; Testing  \n Quality &amp; Testing \n The quality gate \n Every push passes  beforePush.sh  /  beforePush.ps1  (5 stages): \n \n  ruff check  (lint) \n  ruff format  check \n  mypy src  \n  CRITICAL suite  pytest run ( tests/critical_suite.txt , ~779 tests, \n \n RAM-aware xdist workers, coverage) \n \n Forensic  deploy gate  writing  artifacts/forensics/deploy_gate_result.json  \n \n  -FullSuite  runs the whole ~1931-test unit corpus. CI mirrors the gate \n ( .github/workflows/ci.yml ) and adds CodeQL, Trivy, OSV, lockfile-diff and JS \n tests on separate workflows. \n Test architecture \n  \n   Suite  Location  Character    \n  Unit   tests/unit/   ~1900 tests; critical subset in  critical_suite.txt   \n  Integration   tests/integration/   API + engine-level, run standalone/sequential in CI  \n  Golden   tests/golden/  +  test_*_golden.py   byte/behavior-identical extraction g"}, {"u": "/engineering/release-process/", "t": "Release Process [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Engineering  /  Release Process  \n Release Process \n Versioning \n Semver, single canonical source:  pyproject.toml  ( version = \"9.0.6\" ) \n stamped into every build artifact. The README never hard-codes a conflicting \n version — it defers to  nexus version  / the release metadata. \n Pipeline ( .github/workflows/release.yml ) \n Tag-triggered  only  ( v* ). Stages: \n \n Validate tag vs version metadata \n Run the critical test suite (a release run that fails the suite does not \n \n publish — see the v9.0.6 re-cut history in the taskboard) \n \n Build Windows x64 artifacts:  NexusScalpEngine-&lt;version&gt;-win-x64-setup.exe  \n \n + portable  .zip  (PyInstaller) \n \n Generate SHA-256 digests, release manifest, SBOM; embed manifest in the \n \n portable bundle \n \n Publish GitHub Release \n  Post-publish verification  ( release/verify.py ): checksums, manifest \n \n paths, embedded layout (BUG-160 line"}, {"u": "/engineering/security/", "t": "Security [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Engineering  /  Security  \n Security \n Secrets \n \n Secrets live in the  settings DB  / secret store — never in  live.yaml , \n \n never committed (INV-010). Provider URLs/keys are redacted in health \n endpoints and logs ( [REDACTED_SECRET] ). \n \n  scripts/ci/scan_secrets.py  fails CI on secret-shaped strings in \n \n source/config/docs. \n \n Diagnostics export ( nexus export-diagnostics ) is sanitized by contract — \n \n never contains secrets. \n Scanning (CI) \n CodeQL (SAST), Trivy (containers/FS), OSV dependency scanning, lockfile-diff, \n secret scan — see  CI architecture . \n Trust boundaries \n  \n   Boundary  Rule    \n  broker ↔ engine   IMT5Port  adapters only; account-identity fail-safe at connect  \n  research/learning ↔ execution  zero order authority (INV-002); shadow never mutates execution  \n  observability ↔ trading  incidents/forensics are diagnostic-only  \n  Telegram  read-only ou"}, {"u": "/getting-started/configuration/", "t": "Configuration [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Getting Started  /  Configuration  \n Configuration \n Configuration has three layers with different authorities. Mixing them up is a \n classic failure mode — read this page before editing YAML by hand. \n 1.  AppConfig  (bootstrap / import / export) \n  src/nexus_scalp/configuration/config.py  — loads the YAML contract \n ( configs/base.yaml  is the canonical base;  configs/live.yaml.example  is the \n live-shaped example). Used for bootstrap/import/export only. \n 2. Runtime configuration (authoritative live state) \n  RuntimeConfiguration  via  RuntimeConfigStore.get_snapshot()  is the \n  authoritative live state  — versioned, hot-reloadable. Consumers must read \n through  get_snapshot() , never cached constructor values. Scope tags decide \n when a change applies ( LIVE_IMMEDIATE  vs  NEXT_DECISION ). \n 3. Settings DB (secrets + user intent) \n Credentials (e.g. Telegram) live in the setting"}, {"u": "/getting-started/first-run/", "t": "First-Run Safety [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Getting Started  /  First Run  \n First-Run Safety (Demo → Shadow → Live) \n This engine executes on a real broker. The repository's own first-run guidance \n is a strict ladder — do not skip steps. \n  \n   Step  Action  Why    \n  1️⃣  Log into a  DEMO account  in MT5 ( File → Open an Account → Practice/Demo ), confirm the account number/label before touching the bot  LIVE and demo accounts can look identical in MT5's login window  \n  2️⃣  MT5:  Tools → Options → Expert Advisors → tick \"Allow Algo Trading\"   Without this, orders are rejected  \n  3️⃣  Copy  configs/live.yaml  →  configs/demo.yaml ; set demo credentials; confirm  risk.max_concurrent_positions: 1 ,  risk.risk_per_trade_pct  (e.g. 0.5),  risk.max_account_drawdown_pct   Never touch a live config while real money can be reached  \n  4️⃣  Run  SHADOW  first ( nexus start --mode shadow ) for days; review the dashboard + Telegram re"}, {"u": "/getting-started/installation/", "t": "Installation [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Getting Started  /  Installation  \n Installation \n Three supported paths. Pick one — they do not mix. \n Path 1 — End users: packaged Windows release (no Python) \n Download  NexusScalpEngine-&lt;version&gt;-win-x64-setup.exe  (or the portable ZIP \n  NexusScalpEngine-&lt;version&gt;-win-x64.zip ) from \n  GitHub\">https://github.com/Opselon/NexusTradingForexBot/releases\">GitHub  Releases . \n The installer bundles the full Python runtime (PyInstaller) — you never touch \n Python, pip or PyTorch. \n \n Run the installer (per-user,  no admin ) or unpack the portable ZIP. \n First run opens the  setup wizard  ( nexus setup ): compatibility report → \n \n mode ( default: PAPER , never silently LIVE) → symbol → health check. \n \n User data (config/logs/databases/models) lives in \n \n  %LOCALAPPDATA%\\NexusScalpEngine  and survives upgrades, repairs and \n uninstalls. \n  NOTE  Release pipeline:  .github/wo"}, {"u": "/getting-started/quickstart/", "t": "Quickstart [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Getting Started  /  Quickstart  \n Quickstart \n The shortest safe path. Every command below is part of the verified CLI surface \n ( nexus help  shows the authoritative list). \n  ⧉   # 1. Install (developers, from source)\ngit clone https://github.com/Opselon/NexusTradingForexBot.git\ncd NexusTradingForexBot\npython -m venv .venv &amp;&amp; source .venv/bin/activate   # Windows: .\\.venv\\Scripts\\Activate.ps1\npip install -e .[dev]\n\n# 2. Verify your system\nnexus doctor          # read-only diagnostics, 19 categories + suggested fixes\nnexus health          # READY / DEGRADED / NOT READY\n\n# 3. Run — PAPER mode is the default, never LIVE silently\nnexus start           # paper simulation, Control Center at http://127.0.0.1:8080\n\n# 4. Evaluate on real data with zero order authority\nnexus start --mode shadow\n\n# 5. Stop\nnexus stop            # for --daemon runs; Ctrl+C in the foreground   \n Mode sema"}, {"u": "/guides/api/", "t": "API Reference [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Guides  /  API Reference  \n API Reference \n The Control Center backend is a FastAPI application exposing * 203  /api/   \n endpoints across 22 groups** (verified by scanning the route modules in \n  src/nexus_scalp/web/ ), plus Server-Sent Events for ticks and WebSocket for \n the dashboard. Everything the UI does, the API does — the UI is a consumer of \n the same surface. \n  NOTE  Endpoint counts are generated from the repository's actual route decorators —  they drift with the code, and the docs doctor flags stale counts.  \n Discovery \n \n  Health / readiness:   GET /health  →  200  with  READY / DEGRADED ,  503  when NOT READY. \n  Engine state:   GET /api/status  and  GET /api/live/state  (the dashboard heart, includes the effective serving contract). \n  OpenAPI:  the FastAPI app serves its schema at  /openapi.json  and Swagger UI at  /docs  on the same port as the UI (  http://127.0.0."}, {"u": "/guides/cli/", "t": "CLI Guide [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Guides  /  CLI Guide  \n CLI Guide \n  nexus  is the application command (installation lifecycle lives in \n  install.ps1 ; everything you  operate  lives in  nexus ). From source: \n  python -m nexus_scalp.cli.main  (alias  nse ). \n Commands \n  ⧉   nexus help            # same authoritative surface as --help (+ &#x27;nexus help start&#x27;)\nnexus version         # build identity (--json / --plain)\nnexus doctor          # read-only diagnostics (19 categories) + suggested fixes\nnexus status          # health + environment + version\nnexus health          # quick health summary (READY / DEGRADED / NOT READY)\nnexus config          # inspect/validate active configuration (secrets masked)\nnexus start           # PAPER mode by default — never LIVE silently\nnexus stop / restart  # control the background engine (honest dead-pid reporting)\nnexus logs [--tail N] [--errors]\nnexus test --mode quick|uni"}, {"u": "/guides/common-workflows/", "t": "Common Workflows [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Guides  /  Common Workflows  \n Common Workflows \n 1. Daily development loop \n  ⧉   git pull &amp;&amp; .venv/Scripts/Activate.ps1        # Windows dev\nnexus test --mode quick                        # fast sanity\n# ... edit ...\npytest tests/unit -q -k &quot;70 or schema&quot;         # targeted suite\n./beforePush.ps1 -SkipPush                     # full gate before pushing   \n 2. Evaluate the engine on real data (risk-free) \n  ⧉   nexus start --mode shadow      # live feed, zero order authority\n# observe Control Center → SHADOW section: disagreement analysis, drift, health\nnexus stop   \n 3. Research a candidate \n  ⧉   nexus model-dataset-build      # canonical dataset (fingerprinted)\nnexus model-experiment-create  # fair A/B/C protocol\nnexus model-train              # deterministic, seeded\nnexus model-validate           # walk-forward + OOS gate + robustness\nnexus model-replay          "}, {"u": "/guides/troubleshooting/", "t": "Troubleshooting [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Guides  /  Troubleshooting  \n Troubleshooting \n  Rule of thumb:  nexus doctor  first — it reports 19 diagnostic categories  with suggested fixes and is the same gate the engine runs pre-launch.  \n Engine refuses to start \n  \n   Symptom  Likely cause  Action    \n  \"MT5 terminal missing/not running\"  terminal closed / not installed  start MT5, log in (demo first), retry  \n  config validation error  YAML contract violation   nexus config --validate &lt;path&gt; ; fix the named key  \n  environment blocked (exit 3)  Windows ARM64  unsupported by dependency stack; use x64  \n  migration gate failure  schema drift   nexus db migrate ; check  nexus db hygiene status   \n   \n UI / dashboard \n  \n   Symptom  Likely cause  Action    \n  dashboard unreachable  port drift (dev UI/API ports can move)  check  nexus status  output / launcher log for the bound port  \n  \"Cannot GET /\" on some port  wrong po"}, {"u": "/project/capabilities/", "t": "Capability Matrix [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Project  /  Capability Matrix  \n Capability Matrix \n Legend: ✅ Certified · 🟢 Implemented · 🟡 Experimental · 🔵 Research · 🚧 In \n progress · 📌 Planned · ⚪ Not verified \n  \n   Capability  Status  Evidence (repository)  Notes    \n  Causal 50D feature engine ( scalp_v1 )  ✅ Certified   features/scalp_features.py , schema registry, golden/parity tests  live contract; NaN/Inf deterministic fallback  \n  70D canonical contract ( scalp_v3 )  🟢 Implemented (research)   features/schema_contract.py  SSoT, hash, inference validator (10 rejection codes)  candidate-only; negative OOS evidence so far  \n  Liquidity intelligence (10D block)  🟡 Experimental   features/liquidity_engine.py , INV-019 causality rules  research series; governed by  liquidity_features_enabled   \n  News intelligence 10D + bounded gate  🟡 Experimental   news/ , gate bounds boost ≤0.05 / penalty ≤0.10  opt-in, disabled by default;"}, {"u": "/project/milestones/", "t": "Milestones & Project Story [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Project  /  Milestones  \n Milestones — the project story \n This is a factual history reconstructed from the repository's own records \n (taskboard, decision records, forensic reports). No invented narrative. \n Phase I — Engine core (single-agent era) \n The original engine: hexagonal architecture, MT5 adapters, 50D causal features, \n ScalpNet, policy matrix, risk engine, order manager, SQLite WAL ledger, \n FastAPI Control Center. Foundation invariants established: no sync DB on the \n tick path, no order authority for learning components. \n Phase II — Multi-agent forensic era \n Development moved to a  multi-agent model  (up to 56+ parallel AI agents) with \n a strict engineering contract: taskboard, locks, bug ledger, runtime invariants, \n change control. The bug ledger (BUG-001…) and forensic acceptance reports date \n from this era. Key products: database hygiene, migrations, incident res"}, {"u": "/project/roadmap/", "t": "Roadmap [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Project  /  Roadmap  \n Roadmap \n  NOTE  Wording discipline: items are  Planned ,  Under Evaluation ,   Research Direction  or  Completed  — never \"coming soon\" and never  guaranteed. Every item lists its completion gate.  \n NOW (active workstreams) \n  \n   Stream  Item  Status  Objective  Completion criteria    \n  VALIDATION  Rebuild 70D candidate evidence  Under Evaluation  fair A/B/C benchmark on real data with the corrected confidence semantics (CHG-0042)  validated candidate with reproducible walk-forward + OOS artifacts, or a documented stop  \n  RESEARCH  Counterfactual evidence deepening  In progress  NO_TRADE decision walk on canonical tick datasets (CHG-0041, 2095 decisions)  stratified evidence merged into policy review  \n  RUNTIME  Record-builder contract hardening  Completed (2026-09)  single canonical retrain-record builder; width-from-bundle resolution (BUG-185)  launch-gat"}, {"u": "/project/scope/", "t": "Scope [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Project  /  Scope  \n Scope \n In scope \n \n A complete quantitative trading  pipeline : data adapters (MT5/paper/gateway), \n \n causal feature engineering (50D active contract; 60D/70D research family), \n deep model inference (ScalpNet TCN + self-attention), SMC policy matrix, \n invariant risk engine, execution with 60-scenario router, SQLite WAL \n accounting ledger, experience/autopsy intelligence, research &amp; validation \n (walk-forward, OOS gate, robustness), replay and shadow runtimes, model \n governance, observability (structured logs, incidents, forensics, Telegram), \n FastAPI Control Center UI, packaged Windows release + installer + update/rollback. \n \n  Multi-agent engineering memory : architecture map, bug ledger, runtime \n \n invariants, contracts, taskboard, decision records — treated as first-class \n repository artifacts. \n Out of scope (by design) \n \n Multi-broker support be"}, {"u": "/project/status/", "t": "Project Status [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Project  /  Project Status  \n Project Status \n  IMPORTANT  Status labels are evidence-graded. \"Implemented\" means the capability exists  and is covered by tests in this repository. \"Certified\" is reserved for  capabilities that additionally carry a formal forensic acceptance record.  Nothing here claims guaranteed profitability.  \n Snapshot \n  \n   Dimension  Status  Evidence    \n  Version   9.0.8  (semver, single source  pyproject.toml )  release pipeline stamps every artifact  \n  Release   Published  (v9.0.0 → v9.0.8 tags; hardened pipeline: SHA-256, manifests, SBOM)  GitHub Releases  \n  Runtime  Production-hardened; PAPER default; LIVE behind explicit confirmation  CLI contract + pre-flight doctor  \n  Live execution  Working (MT5 Win32 IPC + ZMQ gateway) with account-identity fail-safe  BUG-142 regression suite  \n  Research loop  Working end-to-end (datasets → walk-forward → OOS gate"}, {"u": "/project/vision/", "t": "Vision & Why [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Project  /  Vision &amp; Why  \n Vision — why Nexus exists \n The problem \n Retail-grade algorithmic trading projects usually fail in one of two ways: \n \n  They hide the truth.  Metrics are fabricated or optimistic, failures are \n \n silent, and the gap between backtest and runtime is never measured — so the \n system's own reporting cannot be trusted. A platform that lies to you about \n yesterday cannot be trusted about today. \n \n  They leak the future.  Feature engineering, labeling or \"research\" uses \n \n information that would not have been available at decision time, so results \n are structurally invalid no matter how good they look. The backtest is a \n work of fiction. \n Nexus Scalp Engine (NSE) was built specifically against both failure modes. It \n is an attempt to construct a  complete, auditable pipeline  — market data → \n features → model → policy → risk → execution → accounting "}, {"u": "/reference/cli-reference/", "t": "CLI Reference [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Reference  /  CLI Reference  \n CLI Reference \n The authoritative surface is always  nexus help  /  nexus &lt;command&gt; --help  \n (this page documents the verified contract; the CLI is golden-tested by 66 \n end-to-end tests). \n Global flags \n  \n   Flag  Effect    \n   --json   machine-readable output (parity-tested keys)  \n   --plain   no color, no formatting  \n   --no-color   disable color only  \n   \n Command groups \n  \n   Command  Purpose  Notes    \n  `nexus start [--mode paper\\  shadow\\  live] [--port N] [--daemon]`  run engine  paper default; live needs interactive  --yes /confirmation; port default 8080  \n   nexus stop  /  nexus restart   daemon control  pidfile-based; dead-pid reported honestly (BUG-172)  \n   nexus doctor   19-category diagnostics + suggested fixes   --json  for tooling  \n   nexus status  /  nexus health   environment + health  READY / DEGRADED / NOT READY  \n   n"}, {"u": "/reference/faq/", "t": "FAQ [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Reference  /  FAQ  \n FAQ \n  What is Nexus?  \n A research-driven quantitative trading platform: a hexagonal, event-driven \n scalping engine for MetaTrader 5 (primary: XAUUSD M1) with causal features, \n deep models, an invariant risk engine, deterministic research tooling and \n forensic observability. See  Vision . \n  Is this a live trading bot?  \n It  can  execute live trades on MT5 — but PAPER is the default mode, SHADOW \n carries zero order authority, and LIVE requires explicit interactive \n confirmation. The repository's own evidence shows rejected candidates; this is \n a research platform with a runtime, not a money printer. \n  Can I run it without MT5?  \n Yes — PAPER mode and the full test suite run without a broker. Docker works \n out of the box in PAPER mode. SHADOW and LIVE need an MT5 terminal (Windows \n x64). \n  What is 70D?  \n The canonical research feature contract: 50 base "}, {"u": "/reference/glossary/", "t": "Glossary [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Reference  /  Glossary  \n Glossary \n Project-specific terms. Product/module names (Nexus, ScalpNet, OrderManager, \n MT5, 70D, 50D) are canonical and never translated in code; each language's \n  terminology file  defines how they are presented. \n  \n   Term  Meaning in NSE    \n   50D / scalp_v1   the 50-dimensional causal base feature contract — the ACTIVE live feature schema  \n   70D / scalp_v3   the canonical research feature contract: Base 50 (0..49) + News 10 (50..59) + Liquidity 10 (60..69); candidate-only, not live  \n   scalp_v4   a candidate 70D-family contract (integration-era); classified LEGACY/semantically-different vs v3  \n   Schema hash   SHA-256 over canonical JSON of feature (index, name, family) — reordering invalidates models  \n   ScalpNet   dual-path model: 2D MLP for single-tick snapshots, 3D TCN + self-attention for sequences; 4-logit head  \n   Champion / Challenger  "}, {"u": "/reference/terminology/", "t": "Terminology & Translations [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Reference  /  Terminology &amp; Translations  \n Terminology &amp; Translations \n Untranslatable canon \n These stay in English/Latin script in every language (identifiers, contracts, \n product names): \n `Nexus · ScalpNet · OrderManager · RiskEngine · LiveEngine · IMT5Port · \n AuditRepository · MT5 · ZMQ · SQLite · FastAPI · 50D · 70D · scalp_v1 · \n scalp_v3 · NO_TRADE · BUY · SELL · WAIT · Champion · Challenger · Shadow · \n OOS · walk-forward · O(1) · MFE · MAE` \n Canonical term translations \n The authoritative per-language table lives in \n  site/terminology/&lt;lang&gt;.json  (consumed by the translation audit). Core \n entries: \n  \n   EN  FA (فارسی)  ES  AR (العربية)  DE    \n  Feature Vector  بردار ویژگی  Vector de características  متجه السمات  Merkmalsvektor  \n  Feature Contract  قرارداد ویژگی  Contrato de características  عقد السمات  Merkmalsvertrag  \n  Model Registry  ثبت مدل  Regis"}, {"u": "/research/backtesting/", "t": "Backtesting [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Research  /  Backtesting  \n Backtesting \n Determinism \n Backtests ( research/backtest.py ) are deterministic: fixed seeds, frozen \n datasets, no wall-clock dependence. Same inputs ⇒ same results. \n Friction model \n Spread, slippage and latency are modeled, not ignored: \n \n fills on historical bid/ask (direction-aware), \n tick-level SL/TP first-touch resolution, \n logical latency applied to the decision path, \n robustness stress re-runs under degraded friction (spread/slippage/latency \n \n shocks) — a strategy that only works under ideal fills does not pass. \n Boundary honesty \n \n Backtests produce evidence, not promises. Results feed the validation \n \n pipeline; they never bypass the OOS gate. \n \n Fees/commissions follow the configured friction profile; metrics without the \n \n underlying evidence render  n/a  — never fabricated zeros. \n \n Streaming replay ( research/streaming_replay.py "}, {"u": "/research/counterfactuals/", "t": "Counterfactuals [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Research  /  Counterfactuals  \n Counterfactuals (CHG-0041) \n The question \n Backtests score trades that happened. The counterfactual engine asks the \n other question: **what would have happened on the decisions the engine did NOT \n take?** If the engine abstains (NO_TRADE), was the abstention valuable? \n How it works \n  research/counterfactual.py : \n \n Loads canonical tick datasets (fingerprinted, offline) and decision \n \n snapshots from  audit_signals . \n \n Joins each NO_TRADE decision to the tick window at decision time. \n Applies  certified fill semantics  hypothetically at time T. \n Walks ticks forward to compute MFE / MAE / R / cost / time-to-target. \n Classifies each abstention using  documented rules  (never ad-hoc). \n Stratifies evidence by gate, regime, confidence, session, direction. \n \n First evidence run (2026-09-01) \n 2095 NO_TRADE decisions (2026-08-24 → 09-01) walked ove"}, {"u": "/research/datasets/", "t": "Datasets [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Research  /  Datasets  \n Datasets \n Bar datasets \n Built by  research/dataset.py  +  model_generation/  with quality gates \n (coverage, ordering, duplicates, horizon boundaries). Each dataset is a \n versioned artifact with a fingerprint ( ds_*  id) used in manifests and run \n snapshots. \n Tick datasets (CHG-0041 / TICK_DATASET_META v2) \n  research/mt5_tick_dataset.py  acquires ticks from the **certified adapter \n surface** ( copy_ticks_range ,  COPY_TICKS_ALL ), with: \n \n bounded, deduplicated acquisition (post BUG-188 semantics), \n immutable parquet store with  content fingerprints , \n provenance metadata v2 (symbol, window, source, acquisition identity), \n cache-hit idempotence — re-running acquisition never duplicates. \n \n After acquisition the dataset is fully  offline : research needs no broker. \n Rules \n \n A dataset is immutable once fingerprinted — corrections produce a new \n \n "}, {"u": "/research/methodology/", "t": "Research Methodology [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Research  /  Methodology  \n Research Methodology \n Principle \n Research exists to produce  falsifiable evidence . A candidate that cannot be \n falsified (no OOS, no replay parity, no provenance) is not a candidate — it is \n an opinion, and opinions do not touch the live path. \n The pipeline \n Full detail in  Research Stack . Stages: \n DATA → FEATURES → LABELING → TRAINING → BACKTEST → WALK-FORWARD → OOS GATE → \n ROBUSTNESS → COUNTERFACTUAL → REGISTRY → SHADOW → OPERATOR PROMOTION. \n Every stage writes provenance (dataset ID, schema hash, git commit, effective \n purge/embargo) into run snapshots.  NOT_RECORDED  is written when truthfully \n unknown — never backfilled. \n Evidence grading \n Claims are graded CODE / TEST / INTEGRATION / LIVE / RELEASE VERIFIED. \n Documentation and reports must carry the grade, not just the claim. A \n \"LIVE VERIFIED\" claim means the behavior was observed on "}, {"u": "/research/out-of-sample/", "t": "Out-of-Sample Gate [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Research  /  Out-of-Sample Gate  \n Out-of-Sample (OOS) Gate \n Contract \n  research/oos.py  is a  hard gate : out-of-sample failure ⇒ candidate \n REJECTED, regardless of in-sample performance. There is no override path in \n the pipeline. \n Floors (model lifecycle validation) \n  \n   Metric  Floor    \n  macro-F1 (OOS)  ≥ 0.34  \n  balanced accuracy  ≥ 0.34  \n  calibration error (ECE)  ≤ 0.15  \n  minimum evidence  ≥ 100 rows  \n   \n Evidence the gate bites \n The 70D liquidity candidate — the most heavily engineered research series in \n the repository — was rejected by this exact gate (OOS NOT_ELIGIBLE) after \n real-data walk-forward and shadow benchmarks came back negative/inconclusive. \n A gate that rejects nothing is decoration; this one has a public rejection on \n its record. See  Project Status  and \n  docs/TASK-05-70D-SHADOW-FINAL.md . \n Temporal OOS protocol \n Temporal splits only ( ti"}, {"u": "/research/replay/", "t": "Replay [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Research  /  Replay  \n Replay \n What replay is \n Replay re-runs the engine's decision logic over historical data and proves it \n produces  the same decisions  the live/training pipeline produced on that \n data. It is the execution-fidelity check between research and runtime. \n Two engines \n  \n   Engine  Module  Character    \n  Dataset replay   model_generation/replay.py  +  replay_70d_vector    bit-exact : replay vector must equal the dataset's stored vector (anti-leakage tests)  \n  Streaming replay   research/streaming_replay.py  (CHG-0035)  shared  LiveEngine  over a logical clock (zero sleeps): incremental bar aggregation, causal 50D + news + liquidity at time T, frozen policy + RiskEngine, direction-aware simulated fills on historical bid/ask, tick SL/TP first-touch, ledger MFE/MAE —  NO  order_send  (test-enforced)   \n   \n Anti-leakage \n Features at time T may consume only informa"}, {"u": "/research/reproducibility/", "t": "Reproducibility [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Research  /  Reproducibility  \n Reproducibility \n Identity chain \n Every research artifact carries the chain that produced it: \n  ⧉   dataset fingerprint → feature schema hash → model manifest (scaler, weights)\n→ git commit → effective config (seeds, splits, purge/embargo)   \n Run snapshots ( research_run_snapshots ) store these at run time; provenance \n fields may be  NOT_RECORDED  (honest) but are never invented or backfilled. \n Determinism sources \n \n seeded training (seed-before-model construction — BUG-101 regression), \n frozen datasets (immutable, fingerprinted), \n logical-clock streaming replay (zero sleeps), \n freeze capture at forward-test cutoff +  post-run re-verification  of the \n \n freeze ( research/forward_test.py ). \n What breaks reproducibility (and is therefore guarded) \n  \n   Threat  Guard    \n  dataset mutation  immutable fingerprinted artifacts  \n  feature reorderin"}, {"u": "/research/validation/", "t": "Validation [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Research  /  Validation  \n Validation \n Philosophy \n Validation is the reason the platform exists. Every layer has its own gates, \n and  a failure at any gate is terminal for that candidate  — no averaging, \n no \"close enough\". \n The gate chain \n  \n   Layer  Gates    \n  Dataset  quality gates, fingerprinting, provenance  \n  Features  schema hash, dimension, bounds, ordering  \n  Model  10-gate load gate, calibration, min-evidence  \n  Research  purge/embargo walk-forward, OOS floors, robustness stress  \n  Governance  14-gate candidate verification, promotion preview + transaction  \n  Runtime  deploy gate ( nexus forensic --deploy-gate ) before any release  \n  Release  SHA-256 digests, manifests, SBOM, post-publish verification  \n   \n The 12 validation gates (candidate lifecycle) \n The candidate validation path runs 12 gates over a candidate (manifest \n integrity, schema family, scaler id"}, {"u": "/research/walk-forward/", "t": "Walk-Forward [en]", "l": "en", "x": "  Research  /  Walk-Forward  \n Walk-Forward \n Method \n  training/walk_forward_trainer.py  +  research/walkforward.py  implement \n  purged, embargoed walk-forward  (Lopez de Prado): training folds are \n separated from test folds by a purge gap (label horizon) and an embargo gap \n (serial-correlation buffer), evaluated across temporally ordered folds. \n Defaults that matter (BUG-183) \n The production research path once ran with purge/embargo silently disabled — \n the constants existed but weren't wired. This is recorded as BUG-183 and fixed \n with regression tests:  DEFAULT_PURGE_SECONDS = 300 , `DEFAULT_EMBARGO_SECONDS \n = 60  are now wired into  ResearchPipeline.validate_candidate`, \n  OOSGate.evaluate ,  WalkForwardEngine.validate  and  BacktestEngine.run , and \n the  effective  purge/embargo values are recorded in every run's config. \n Why it is non-negotiable \n A walk-forward without "}, {"u": "/getting-started/", "t": "Getting Started [en]", "l": "en", "x": "Install, run and configure the engine. PAPER mode is the default; SHADOW gives you live data with zero order authority."}, {"u": "/project/", "t": "Project [en]", "l": "en", "x": "What Nexus is, what is certified vs experimental, where it is going — all evidence-graded."}, {"u": "/architecture/", "t": "Architecture [en]", "l": "en", "x": "How the engine is built: hexagonal layers, the tick-to-decision path, model governance, and the intelligence loop."}, {"u": "/research/", "t": "Research [en]", "l": "en", "x": "How historical data becomes falsifiable evidence — datasets, backtests, walk-forward, OOS, replay, counterfactuals."}, {"u": "/engineering/", "t": "Engineering [en]", "l": "en", "x": "Quality gates, CI architecture, the release process, and the security posture."}, {"u": "/guides/", "t": "Guides [en]", "l": "en", "x": "Operating the engine day to day: CLI, REST API, troubleshooting, common workflows."}, {"u": "/contributing/", "t": "Contributing [en]", "l": "en", "x": "The engineering contract, documentation ownership, and how to add a language."}, {"u": "/reference/", "t": "Reference [en]", "l": "en", "x": "CLI reference, glossary, terminology, and honest answers in the FAQ."}, {"u": "/fa/", "t": "Home [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "Nexus Scalp Engine documentation homepage what's new capabilities architecture research"}, {"u": "/fa/releases/", "t": "انتشارها [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "releases v9.0.8 changelog what's new history 959d7d9"}, {"u": "/fa/architecture/code-navigation/", "t": "Code Navigation Map — Nexus Scalp Engine [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  معماری  /  code navigation  \n Code Navigation Map — Nexus Scalp Engine \n  Where to find things, for a developer (or agent) landing fresh in this repo.  This map is an INDEX. Detailed truth lives in:  -  agents/skill.md  — authoritative architecture map + repo contract (READ FIRST)  -  docs/architecture/dependency-map.md  — subsystem edges + contracts  -  docs/architecture/comment-style.md  — comment/doc conventions  -  docs/RELEASE.md  — CLI exit codes, update protocol, release verification  -  agents/bugs.md  — bug ledger (append-only; grep  ^## BUG-  tail for next free id)  \n Startup &amp; lifecycle \n  \n   Concern  Where    \n  Primary launcher (bootstrap sys.path, adapter bind, engine + web)   NexusTradingForexBot.py   \n  CLI entry ( nexus  /  nse , Typer)   src/nexus_scalp/cli/main.py   \n  Engine construction + async tick loop   src/nexus_scalp/application/live_engine.py  ( run_loop"}, {"u": "/fa/architecture/comment-style/", "t": "Comment Style Guide — Nexus Scalp Engine [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  معماری  /  comment style  \n Comment Style Guide — Nexus Scalp Engine \n  Applies to all Python source in  src/ ,  tests/ , and  scripts/ .  Repo rule of thumb:  the repository should not contain more comments — it should contain better comments.   \n The one test \n  Could a competent developer derive this from the code itself?  \n If YES → do not comment. If NO → the comment may be valuable; then ask: \n \"Will this still be true and useful six months from now?\" If NO → do not write it. \n What comments are FOR \n A comment must be one of: \n  \n   Category  Documents  Example    \n  INVARIANT  a rule the code must keep but does not enforce visibly  \"Resume-safe hash: the hasher must cover the already-downloaded bytes too.\"  \n  SAFETY  fail-closed / fail-safe semantics  \"Fail closed: no inference must never yield a trade decision.\"  \n  CONCURRENCY  lock ownership, ordering, atomicity  \"Hold the "}, {"u": "/fa/architecture/control-center-ui/", "t": "Control Center UI Architecture (CHG-0043, TASK-CONTROL-CENTER) [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  معماری  /  control center ui  \n Control Center UI Architecture (CHG-0043, TASK-CONTROL-CENTER) \n  Operator-facing architecture of the NEXUS Control Center. UI-owned doc;  backend architecture lives in  docs/architecture/  elsewhere. Status  semantics here are the CONTRACT for every future CC view.  \n Purpose \n One coherent surface where an operator answers, without reading logs: \n WHAT is happening → WHY → WHAT changed → WHAT is blocked → WHAT is healthy → \n WHAT is serving → WHY did/didn't a trade happen → WHAT is safe to do next. \n Observation model: OBSERVE → UNDERSTAND → INVESTIGATE → ACT → VERIFY. \n Navigation &amp; Screens \n  \n   Tab (nav id)  Screen  Data sources (all read-only)    \n  Control Center ( tab-control-center )  Overview: mode banner, 6-tile status strip (Runtime/Data/Model/Inference/Database/MT5), runtime truth, market snapshot, latest decision, active warnings   /ap"}, {"u": "/fa/architecture/crash-safety/", "t": "Crash-Safety Architecture (NSE) [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  معماری  /  crash safety  \n Crash-Safety Architecture (NSE) \n  Status: HARDENED_WITH_GAPS baseline documented 2026-09-01 (rev 2 — checker  regex fix + 381-site silent-handler backlog tracked as P1 violations).  Owner: Nexus-Main (crash-containment master pass).  Scope: the failure contract of every major execution boundary, from process  startup through model tensor execution, trading execution, Web/API, updater,  release pipeline, and shutdown.  Companion documents:  failure-recovery-matrix.md  (per-subsystem failure  matrix),  artifacts/forensics/crash-safety-audit.json  (machine audit).  \n \n 1. Governing principle \n The requirement is NOT \"the application must never crash\". The requirement is: \n  ⧉   NO SILENT CRASH      NO SILENT EXCEPTION      NO FALSE SUCCESS\nNO FAKE HEALTH       NO FABRICATED MODEL OUTPUT\nNO UNSAFE TRADING AFTER CRITICAL FAILURE\nNO CORRUPTED STATE AFTER FAILURE  "}, {"u": "/fa/architecture/data-flow/", "t": "Data Flow — Tick to Decision [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  معماری  /  جریان داده  \n Data Flow — from tick to decision \n This is the canonical path (from  agents/skill.md  §4). Every arrow is a \n contract boundary. \n  ⧉   TickData (MT5 / paper / gateway)\n  → ScalpFeatureEngine.to_tensor_input()\n      50D base (scalp_v1 · FEATURE_NAMES · [-3,+3] · finite)\n  → assemble_70d / build_70d_vector()\n      70D canonical: Base 0..49 | News 10D 50..59 | Liquidity 10D 60..69\n  → InferenceContractValidator\n      scaler dim == feature dim · schema hash · finite · bounds\n  → ScalpNet → 4 logits (NO_TRADE / BUY / SELL / WAIT) → confidence gate 0.35\n  → regime_classifier (Regime Guardian)\n  → signals/policy + rule_matrix (~30 rules, TTL 5s cache)\n  → RiskEngine.calculate_dynamic_volume() + evaluate_proposal()\n      free-margin 20% clamp · tier caps · HARD_MAX_LOTS\n  → OrderManager (60-scenario router · 11 position states ·\n      MAX_TOTAL_EXPOSURE=1 · 30s re-qu"}, {"u": "/fa/architecture/database/", "t": "Database Architecture [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  معماری  /  پایگاه داده  \n Database Architecture \n Canonical stores \n  \n   DB  Contents  Notes    \n   artifacts/audit.db   trading ledger, experience outcomes, accounting, research registry, strategy lifecycle, incidents, hygiene  one canonical ledger; SQLite  WAL   \n   artifacts/news.db   news ingestion, analysis, consensus, impacts  lazy schema on first save  \n   candle_intel.db   candle intelligence  versioned schema  \n  settings DB  secrets + user intent (Telegram creds via  settings_service )  never in YAML (INV-010)  \n   \n Write path \n  AuditRepository  queues writes to a  background worker thread  — the tick \n hot path never performs synchronous DB work (INV-001). Historical \n experience/outcome/ledger rows are  immutable  (INV-007); corrections go \n through evidence → reconstruction → derived records with provenance, never row \n rewrites. \n Migrations \n  src/nexus_scalp/database"}, {"u": "/fa/architecture/dependency-map/", "t": "Architecture Dependency Map — Nexus Scalp Engine (NSE) [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  معماری  /  dependency map  \n Architecture Dependency Map — Nexus Scalp Engine (NSE) \n  Maintained per the MASTER MULTI-AGENT CONTRACT §9 (see  agents/multi-agent-git-contract.md ).  Describes actual subsystem relationships (verified against executable code; see agents/skill.md for the full inventory).  Every edge documents: contract, direction, expected data, safety guarantees.  \n Canonical high-level flow \n  ⧉   MT5\n  │  (tick/order/position/account events)\n  ▼\nMT5 Adapter / Providers            [ports: IMT5Port; adapters: mt5/, paper/, remote]\n  │  (normalized events)\n  ▼\nLiveEngine (async event loop)      [src/nexus_scalp/application/live_engine.py]\n  ├─ Feature Engine                [features/scalp_features.py → FEATURE_VECTOR_50D]\n  ├─ Model Runtime                 [models/scalp_net.py → MODEL_MANIFEST; Champion/Challenger]\n  ├─ News Context                  [news/ → NEWS_CONTEXT]"}, {"u": "/fa/architecture/execution-pipeline/", "t": "Execution Pipeline [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  معماری  /  خط لوله اجرا  \n Execution Pipeline \n  execution/order_manager.py  is the single dispatch authority (INV-004). It is \n large by design (convention-locked hot path) and is being decomposed \n surgically, seam by seam, with golden tests. \n Path of an order \n  ⧉   TradeProposal (frozen domain contract, execution_id trace)\n  → policy/confluence checks (SMC matrix, Regime Guardian, confidence gate)\n  → RiskEngine.evaluate_proposal() → dynamic volume (fractional Kelly)\n  → OrderManager router (60 scenarios: fills, rejections, partials, errors)\n  → IMT5Port adapter (Win32 IPC / ZMQ / paper)\n  → position lifecycle (11 states with hysteresis)\n  → protective exits (SL/TP first-touch, breakeven lock, profit giveback,\n      adaptive exit protection)\n  → broker reconciliation (broker truth wins — INV-011)\n  → accounting + autopsy (immutable ledger)   \n Hard clamps (never bypassed) \n  \n   C"}, {"u": "/fa/architecture/failure-recovery-matrix/", "t": "Failure-Recovery Matrix (NSE crash-containment pass) [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  معماری  /  failure recovery matrix  \n Failure-Recovery Matrix (NSE crash-containment pass) \n  Status: baseline 2026-09-01. Companion to  crash-safety.md  and   artifacts/forensics/crash-safety-audit.json .  Every row = subsystem × failure → expected console log, state, recovery,  exit, and the test that proves it. GREEN means failure-injected → detected →  logged → safe behavior → regression exists (never \"a try/except exists\").  \n Legend — State: truthful runtime state after the failure. Log: minimum \n console/file record. Rec: recovery policy. Exit: CLI/process exit contract. \n Test: primary regression evidence. \n  \n   #  Subsystem  Failure  Log (console)  State  Rec  Exit  Test    \n  1  startup  missing/invalid config at launch  red panel  cfg_detail=Parse error…  + doctor FAIL  NOT READY  halt  1 / EXIT_RUNTIME  launcher doctor contract; BUG-149/156 lineage  \n  2  startup   _prefli"}, {"u": "/fa/architecture/model-pipeline/", "t": "Model Pipeline [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  معماری  /  خط لوله مدل  \n Model Pipeline \n Lifecycle \n  ⧉   DATASET (versioned artifact + quality gates + fingerprint)\n  → EXPERIMENT (equal budgets/seeds/splits; dataset-fairness gate)\n  → CANDIDATE MODEL (+ manifest: schema hash · scaler · dataset ID · git commit)\n  → VALIDATION (walk-forward · OOS gate · robustness · calibration)\n  → REGISTRY (content-addressed; challenger only)\n  → LOAD GATE (10 gates, enforced at every attach)\n  → SHADOW PARITY (zero order authority)\n  → OPERATOR PROMOTION (READY_FOR_REVIEW → APPROVED → CHAMPION; atomic transaction)\n  → ROLLBACK PREVIEW / EMERGENCY FREEZE   \n Artifact-first Model Factory ( model_generation/ ) \n Datasets, experiments and models are **versioned filesystem artifacts with \n manifests** — inference needs no database. The manifest carries \n  feature_schema_hash ,  training_dataset_id , scaler identity and git commit. \n ScalpNet remains "}, {"u": "/fa/architecture/observability-log-contract/", "t": "Observability Log Contract — frozen 2026-09-01 (Agent 2) [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  معماری  /  observability log contract  \n Observability Log Contract — frozen 2026-09-01 (Agent 2) \n Authoritative in-repo reference for the log-noise contracts proven in the \n operational-observability sprint and pinned by \n  tests/unit/test_operational_log_hygiene.py  + \n  tests/unit/test_observability_contract_freeze.py  + \n  tests/unit/test_logging_redaction.py . \n Any future change to these behaviors MUST update those tests in the same \n commit (test-first rule: a new repetitive runtime event needs an \n aggregation/transition/rate-limit test before merge). \n Companion tooling:  src/nexus_scalp/observability/event_aggregator.py  \n (EventBatchAggregator — bounded, thread-safe, first-occurrence-immediate). \n \n Core invariants (all events) \n \n SEVERITY ladder: DEBUG = diagnostic detail; INFO = normal state / bounded \n \n informational transitions; WARNING = first failure or actionable \n"}, {"u": "/fa/architecture/observability-map/", "t": "Observability Map — Nexus Scalp Engine (NSE) [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  معماری  /  observability map  \n Observability Map — Nexus Scalp Engine (NSE) \n  TASK-OBS-AUDIT (2026-08-31, HEAD baseline 1f60832; delivered at dcc80d7).  Agent: Hermes-ObsForensic. AUDIT-ONLY: zero runtime code changed.  Machine-readable companion:  artifacts/forensics/observability-audit.json .  Method: black-box reconstruction from runtime evidence (logs / DBs / artifacts /  live API / CLI) FIRST, then targeted read-only code sweeps for every claim.  Evidence markers: [L]=live-probed today, [DB]=DB census, [LOG]=log sample, [C]=code file:line.  \n 1. What the system actually produces today \n  \n   Channel  Reality (verified)    \n  Logs  severity-split  logs/{critical,error,warning,info}/YYYY/MM/*.log , ISO-8601  +03:30 , 10 MB part rotation, retention 30/30/90/365 d [C observability/logging.py:388-394]. Only 08-29 + 08-31 exist; 08-30 absent. ~190 MB on 08-31 (131 MB error).  \n  Log r"}, {"u": "/fa/architecture/observability/", "t": "Observability [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  معماری  /  مشاهده‌پذیری  \n Observability \n NSE treats observability as a subsystem with contracts, not a logging afterthought. \n If the engine cannot show  why  it did something, its behavior is indistinguishable \n from a bug — so showing why is engineered, not hoped for. \n Structured logging ( observability/logging.py ) \n \n Severity-split, date-organized storage:  logs/&lt;sev&gt;/YYYY/MM/YYYY-MM-DD.log . \n ISO-8601 timestamps (broker-local offset aware), event/component/category/ \n \n error-code fields, correlation context. \n \n Daily + size rotation with zero-loss part files; per-severity retention. \n Key + high-entropy redaction; ANSI-free stacks. \n \n Incident response ( incidents/ ) \n Canonical incident model ( INC-YYYY-hex8 , 8 statuses, 5 severities), \n fingerprint correlation, causal-chain timeline reconstruction, value lineage \n with first-divergence location, WHY workflows, MT5"}, {"u": "/fa/architecture/order_manager_architecture/", "t": "ORDER_MANAGER.PY — Architectural Map (Agent-5, Phase A) [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  معماری  /  order manager architecture  \n ORDER_MANAGER.PY — Architectural Map (Agent-5, Phase A) \n Evidence base: forensic inventory at HEAD  0015608  (post Agent-4 winner-protection \n sprint  0839da3 ). No edits made during this phase. This document precedes any \n extraction (task brief §24). \n 1. Current shape \n 6372 LOC, 1 god class + 6 support types \n  \n   Item  Span  Notes    \n  Module constants (18)  L60-155  exposure caps, BE/giveback/trailing geometry  \n  ExitMechanism (Enum)  L158  exit taxonomy  \n  PositionState (Enum)  L172  11 in-trade lifecycles  \n  PositionEvaluationStep  L190  trajectory step record  \n  LSFTicketState  L209  LSF per-ticket state  \n  PositionProtectionState  L226  per-ticket protection facts (dataclass)  \n  SmartPositionMetrics  L281  57 derived metrics (dataclass)  \n  OrderLifecycleManager  L348-6372  81 methods, 99 distinct  self.*  state attrs  \n   \n 2"}, {"u": "/fa/architecture/overview/", "t": "Architecture Overview [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  معماری  /  نمای کلی  \n نمای معماری \n NSE  شش‌ضلعی (ports-and-adapters) و رویدادمحور  است. پلتفرم بروکر، مدل‌ها و \n آداپتورهای شبکه پشت قراردادهای port ایزوله شده‌اند ( IMT5Port ,  IGatewayPort )؛ \n دامنه (domain) نمی‌داند کدام بروکر — یا اصلاً بروکری — متصل است. \n  ⧉   داده بازار (MT5 / paper / gateway)\n        │\n        ▼\nویژگی‌های علّی ── 50D scalp_v1 (قرارداد زنده) ── 70D scalp_v3 (پژوهشی)\n        │\n        ▼\nاعتبارسنج استنتاج ──► ScalpNet (TCN + خودتوجهی، ۴-لاگیتی)\n        │\n        ▼\nطبقه‌بان رژیم ──► ماتریس سیاست SMC ──► موتور ریسک (سایزینگ کلی، کلمپ‌ها)\n        │\n        ▼\nOrderManager (روتر ۶۰-سناریویی · ۱۱ وضعیت پوزیشن · HARD_MAX_LOTS=10)\n        │\n        ▼\nآداپتور IMT5Port ──► بروکر / paper        (اختیار سفارش اینجا تمام می‌شود)\n        │\n        ├──► دفتر کل حسابداری (SQLite WAL، تغییرناپذیر)\n        ├──► هوش تجربه / کالبدشکافی معاملات\n        ├──► پژوهش: بک‌تست ← walk-for"}, {"u": "/fa/architecture/qa-assurance-contract/", "t": "QA ASSURANCE CONTRACT — Deep Assurance Layer (CHG-0045) [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  معماری  /  qa assurance contract  \n QA ASSURANCE CONTRACT — Deep Assurance Layer (CHG-0045) \n  Owner: Nexus-Main (TASK-QA-DEEP-ASSURANCE). This document is the contract  for the OSS-grade adversarial QA layer: lanes, markers, budgets, the JSON  result schema, and the governance rules for flaky/open-defect tests.  \n 1. Position in the gate hierarchy \n  \n   Lane  Command  When  Budget    \n  Pre-push critical gate (existing, NOT replaced)   beforePush.sh  /  check_local.py   every push  ~2.5 min  \n   Deep assurance — fast    python scripts/qa/deep_assurance.py --fast   PR / push lane in CI  &lt; 60 s  \n   Deep assurance — full    python scripts/qa/deep_assurance.py   main / scheduled / dispatch  &lt; 5 min  \n  Mutation proof   python scripts/qa/run_mutations.py   scheduled / dispatch (weekly)  &lt; 15 min  \n   \n The deep-assurance layer NEVER replaces the runtime gate; it adds \n independe"}, {"u": "/fa/architecture/QA_BLIND_SPOT_MATRIX/", "t": "QA BLIND-SPOT MATRIX — Nexus Scalp Engine [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  معماری  /  QA BLIND SPOT MATRIX  \n QA BLIND-SPOT MATRIX — Nexus Scalp Engine \n  CHG-0045 / TASK-QA-DEEP-ASSURANCE (Nexus-Main, 2026-09-02).  Required first milestone of the OSS-grade adversarial QA brief: prove which  gaps matter BEFORE building test mass. Derived from  agents/bugs.md   (BUG-001..BUG-208) and  agents/change_control.md  (CHG-0001..CHG-0050).  \n 1. Method \n \n  Defect-history mining  — every BUG/CHG row classified by subsystem, \n \n severity (P0 money/execution · P1 decision-path/trust · P2 operator \n trust/diagnostics · P3 robustness), and named regression test. \n \n  Detection-quality audit  — does the named regression test the ROOT \n \n CAUSE or only the incident's symptom path? \n \n  Re-entry analysis  — can the same class return through another door? \n  Verdict  — KEEP / IMPROVE / MERGE / DELETE / MISSING per test family. \n \n 2. Matrix — defect history → detection → gap "}, {"u": "/fa/architecture/repository-hygiene/", "t": "Repository Hygiene Audit — Nexus Scalp Engine [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  معماری  /  repository hygiene  \n Repository Hygiene Audit — Nexus Scalp Engine \n   Date:  2026-08-31 ·  HEAD:   1f60832  (main) ·  Working tree:  UNCHANGED (0 modifications)   Mode:  READ-ONLY forensic librarian pass. Nothing was fixed, moved, deleted, or refactored.   Machine-readable twin:   artifacts/forensics/repository-hygiene-audit.json    2026-08-31 repair pass:  CLEANUP-001/002/003/004/005/006 repaired — networkx declared as runtime dep, psycopg declared via new  postgres  extra, requirements ranges reconciled to pyproject, skill.md runner path fixed, tick_storage.py removed, 32 e2e_cc files archived to  scratch/e2e_cc_archive/ , .pyproj.bak removed.   Scope guard:  excludes all active-agent work (BUG-166..174, anti-crash, decomposition, release).  \n 1. What was analyzed \n \n 1,621 tracked files (724 py / 625 md / 80 json / 22 js / 16 mjs / 15 ps1 / 10 yml) \n 351 Python source f"}, {"u": "/fa/architecture/research-stack/", "t": "Research Stack [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  معماری  /  پشته پژوهش  \n Research Stack \n The research side answers one question with evidence: **is this candidate good \n enough to trust — and can we prove it on data it never saw?** \n Pipeline \n  ⧉   DATA (canonical tick/bar datasets, provenance-fingerprinted)\n  → FEATURES (same causal contract as live: 50D base, governed 70D assembly)\n  → LABELING (triple-barrier, purged + embargoed)\n  → TRAINING (deterministic seeds, walk-forward)\n  → BACKTEST (friction-aware: spread / slippage / latency)\n  → WALK-FORWARD VALIDATION\n  → OOS GATE (hard: failure ⇒ REJECTED)\n  → ROBUSTNESS STRESS\n  → COUNTERFACTUAL / STRATIFICATION EVIDENCE\n  → CANDIDATE REGISTRY (content-addressed)\n  → SHADOW COMPARISON (zero order authority)\n  → OPERATOR-GATED PROMOTION   \n Key guarantees \n \n  Leakage prevention (INV-008):  purged + embargoed walk-forward \n \n (Lopez de Prado); broker history REPLACE+ALIGN; liquidit"}, {"u": "/fa/architecture/runtime-certification-gate/", "t": "Runtime Certification Gate — canonical pre-push contract [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  معماری  /  runtime certification gate  \n Runtime Certification Gate — canonical pre-push contract \n   CHANGE-ID:  CHG-0051 ·  TASK-ID:  TASK-RUNTIME-GATE ·  Status:  ACTIVE   One command. One answer.   python scripts/ci/runtime_gate.py   \n 1. Purpose \n The repository has many test families (runtime, features, 50D/70D, models, \n database, execution, providers, research, CLI, observability, installer, \n integration). The problem was never test count — it was the absence of ONE \n strong, trustworthy, repeatable command answering: \n  \"Is the composed runtime safe, coherent, loadable, and operational enough  for an agent to push its change?\"  \n The Runtime Certification Gate is that command. It is a **curated, layered \n certification of the REAL composed runtime** — not \"run all pytest\". It \n exercises the actual boot path (config → adapter →  LiveEngine  service \n graph → decision pipeline"}, {"u": "/fa/architecture/runtime/", "t": "Runtime — the LiveEngine Loop [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  معماری  /  زمان اجرا  \n Runtime — the LiveEngine loop \n  application/live_engine.py  is the orchestrator: a single async event loop \n that drives the tick pipeline and coordinates background workers. \n Startup sequence \n \n Launcher binds an adapter ( DirectMT5Adapter  /  RemoteMT5GatewayAdapter  / \n \n paper) behind  IMT5Port . \n \n Pre-flight  doctor gate : MT5 terminal present? config valid? platform \n \n supported? — otherwise the engine refuses to start. \n \n Migration gate: canonical DB migration engine runs (additive, checksummed). \n Model load: Champion bundle validated by the  10-gate load gate  (manifest \n \n hash, scaler dim, schema family, width contract…). \n \n Mode select:  PAPER (default)  / SHADOW / LIVE (interactive confirmation). \n Web server: FastAPI Control Center + SSE + WebSocket. \n Workers start (audit writer, research, hygiene, incidents, Telegram). \n \n Tick pipeline ("}, {"u": "/fa/architecture/system-map/", "t": "System Map [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  معماری  /  نقشه سیستم  \n System Map \n Package inventory ( src/nexus_scalp/ ) \n  ⧉   nexus_scalp/\n├── domain/            frozen Pydantic contracts (TickData, TradeProposal, …)\n├── ports/             IMT5Port · IGatewayPort        ← the hexagon seam\n├── adapters/          mt5/ (Win32 IPC) · gateway (ZMQ) · paper/ · database/ (AuditRepository, WAL)\n├── features/          scalp_features (50D) · schema registry · schema_contract (70D SSoT)\n│                      liquidity_engine · regime_classifier · temporal (research)\n├── models/            ScalpNet (dual-path TCN + self-attention)\n├── training/          walk_forward_trainer · labeling/ (triple-barrier)\n├── signals/           policy · rule matrix (~30 SMC rules)\n├── strategies/        factory (+ provider_gate for LLM/AI services)\n├── risk/              RiskEngine (Kelly sizing, clamps, kill switch)\n├── execution/         order_manager (+ "}, {"u": "/fa/contributing/add-language/", "t": "Adding a Language [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  مشارکت  /  افزودن زبان  \n Adding a Language \n The multilingual architecture is data-driven: adding Turkish, French, Russian, \n Chinese or Japanese is a directory + registry entry — no code changes. \n Recipe \n \n  Create the language tree  \n \n  ⧉      site/content/&lt;lang&gt;/            # translated site content (mirror of en tree)\n   docs/&lt;lang&gt;/index.md            # optional docs-root landing page   \n \n  Register the language  in  scripts/docs/site_config.py : \n \n  ⧉      LANGUAGES = {\n       &quot;en&quot;: {&quot;name&quot;: &quot;English&quot;, &quot;dir&quot;: &quot;ltr&quot;},\n       &quot;fa&quot;: {&quot;name&quot;: &quot;فارسی&quot;,   &quot;dir&quot;: &quot;rtl&quot;},\n       ...\n       &quot;tr&quot;: {&quot;name&quot;: &quot;Türkçe&quot;,  &quot;dir&quot;: &quot;ltr&quot;},   # ← new\n   }   \n \n  Translate core pages first  (in priority order): \n \n  index  →  getting-"}, {"u": "/fa/contributing/contribution-guide/", "t": "Contribution Guide [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  مشارکت  /  راهنمای مشارکت  \n این مخزن توسط عامل‌های هماهنگ تحت یک قرارداد مهندسی سخت‌گیرانه توسعه می‌یابد؛ مشارکت‌کنندگان انسانی از همان نظم بهره می‌برند. \n راه‌اندازی \n  ⧉   git clone https://github.com/Opselon/NexusTradingForexBot.git\ncd NexusTradingForexBot\npython -m venv .venv &amp;&amp; .\\.venv\\Scripts\\Activate.ps1\npip install -e .[dev]\npytest tests/unit -q   \n نظم تغییر \n \n  اول حافظه مهندسی را بخوانید :  \">https://github.com/Opselon/NexusTradingForexBot/blob/main/agents/skill.md\">  agents/skill.md   (نقشه معماری)،  \">https://github.com/Opselon/NexusTradingForexBot/blob/main/agents/runtime_invariants.md\">  agents/runtime_invariants.md  ،  \">https://github.com/Opselon/NexusTradingForexBot/blob/main/agents/bugs.md\">  agents/bugs.md  . \n  قبل از کدنویسی ادعا کنید  — یک ردیف به  agents/taskboard.md  اضافه کنید. \n  استفاده مجدد &gt; گسترش &gt; بازآرایی &gt; ایجاد ؛ فایل‌های مسیر داغ ق"}, {"u": "/fa/contributing/documentation/", "t": "Documentation Workflow [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  مشارکت  /  گردش‌کار مستندات  \n Documentation Workflow \n Ownership \n Documentation is owned by the  Nexus-Docs  role \n (registry:  docs/agent_handoffs/DOCS_REGISTRY.md ). The boundary is hard: \n docs changes never touch runtime code, and code owners never need to fix docs \n tooling. If documentation exposes a suspected code defect, it is recorded in \n the registry with subsystem attribution — the implementation stays untouched. \n Information architecture \n  ⧉   docs/            engineering documentation (markdown, this IA tree)\nsite/            GitHub Pages source (builds docs/ + translations into a static site)\nscripts/docs/    validation tooling (check_docs.py, check_translations.py, build_site.py)\n.github/workflows/docs.yml    docs CI + Pages deploy   \n Source of truth \n \n  English  is the source language; every other language is a translation \n \n with status metadata ( complete | pa"}, {"u": "/fa/engineering/ci/", "t": "CI Architecture [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  مهندسی  /  معماری CI  \n CI Architecture \n Workflows \n  \n   Workflow  Trigger  Purpose    \n   ci.yml   push (main/develop/ci-tests), PR, weekly drift scan  ruff · format · mypy · pytest (critical; matrix arms for integration/e2e/research/model on demand)  \n   tests-os.yml   matrix OS runs  cross-platform unit sanity  \n   security.yml   PR + weekly schedule  CodeQL + Trivy  \n   osv-scanner.yml   schedule  dependency vulnerabilities  \n   lockfile-diff.yml   dependency file changes  lockfile drift  \n   js-tests.yml   Web/ changes   node --check  + JS tests  \n   release.yml    v*  tags  only   build + verify + publish release artifacts  \n   docker.yml   Docker surface changes  image build gates  \n   docs.yml   docs/site/README changes  documentation validation + Pages deploy (this platform)  \n   \n Trigger policy (CI_TRIGGER_POLICY v1): tags never fire CI (release-only), main \n pushes run th"}, {"u": "/fa/engineering/quality/", "t": "Quality & Testing [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  مهندسی  /  کیفیت و تست  \n Quality &amp; Testing \n The quality gate \n Every push passes  beforePush.sh  /  beforePush.ps1  (5 stages): \n \n  ruff check  (lint) \n  ruff format  check \n  mypy src  \n  CRITICAL suite  pytest run ( tests/critical_suite.txt , ~779 tests, \n \n RAM-aware xdist workers, coverage) \n \n Forensic  deploy gate  writing  artifacts/forensics/deploy_gate_result.json  \n \n  -FullSuite  runs the whole ~1931-test unit corpus. CI mirrors the gate \n ( .github/workflows/ci.yml ) and adds CodeQL, Trivy, OSV, lockfile-diff and JS \n tests on separate workflows. \n Test architecture \n  \n   Suite  Location  Character    \n  Unit   tests/unit/   ~1900 tests; critical subset in  critical_suite.txt   \n  Integration   tests/integration/   API + engine-level, run standalone/sequential in CI  \n  Golden   tests/golden/  +  test_*_golden.py   byte/behavior-identical extraction gates (decomposi"}, {"u": "/fa/engineering/release-process/", "t": "Release Process [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  مهندسی  /  فرایند انتشار  \n Release Process \n Versioning \n Semver, single canonical source:  pyproject.toml  ( version = \"9.0.6\" ) \n stamped into every build artifact. The README never hard-codes a conflicting \n version — it defers to  nexus version  / the release metadata. \n Pipeline ( .github/workflows/release.yml ) \n Tag-triggered  only  ( v* ). Stages: \n \n Validate tag vs version metadata \n Run the critical test suite (a release run that fails the suite does not \n \n publish — see the v9.0.6 re-cut history in the taskboard) \n \n Build Windows x64 artifacts:  NexusScalpEngine-&lt;version&gt;-win-x64-setup.exe  \n \n + portable  .zip  (PyInstaller) \n \n Generate SHA-256 digests, release manifest, SBOM; embed manifest in the \n \n portable bundle \n \n Publish GitHub Release \n  Post-publish verification  ( release/verify.py ): checksums, manifest \n \n paths, embedded layout (BUG-160 lineage) \n "}, {"u": "/fa/engineering/security/", "t": "Security [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  مهندسی  /  امنیت  \n Security \n Secrets \n \n Secrets live in the  settings DB  / secret store — never in  live.yaml , \n \n never committed (INV-010). Provider URLs/keys are redacted in health \n endpoints and logs ( [REDACTED_SECRET] ). \n \n  scripts/ci/scan_secrets.py  fails CI on secret-shaped strings in \n \n source/config/docs. \n \n Diagnostics export ( nexus export-diagnostics ) is sanitized by contract — \n \n never contains secrets. \n Scanning (CI) \n CodeQL (SAST), Trivy (containers/FS), OSV dependency scanning, lockfile-diff, \n secret scan — see  CI architecture . \n Trust boundaries \n  \n   Boundary  Rule    \n  broker ↔ engine   IMT5Port  adapters only; account-identity fail-safe at connect  \n  research/learning ↔ execution  zero order authority (INV-002); shadow never mutates execution  \n  observability ↔ trading  incidents/forensics are diagnostic-only  \n  Telegram  read-only outbound ("}, {"u": "/fa/getting-started/configuration/", "t": "Configuration [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  شروع  /  پیکربندی  \n پیکربندی \n پیکربندی سه لایه با مرجعیت‌های متفاوت دارد. قاطی‌کردن آن‌ها یک خطای کلاسیک است — پیش از ویرایش دستی YAML این صفحه را بخوانید. \n 1.  AppConfig  (بوت‌استرپ / درون‌ریزی / برون‌بری) \n  src/nexus_scalp/configuration/config.py  — قرارداد YAML را بارگذاری می‌کند ( configs/base.yaml  پایه مرجع؛  configs/live.yaml.example  نمونه با شکل live). فقط برای بوت‌استرپ/درون‌ریزی/برون‌بری استفاده می‌شود. \n 2. پیکربندی زمان اجرا (وضعیت زنده مرجع) \n  RuntimeConfiguration  از طریق  RuntimeConfigStore.get_snapshot()   وضعیت زنده مرجع  است — نسخه‌دار و با بارگذاری مجدد داغ. مصرف‌کنندگان باید از  get_snapshot()  بخوانند، نه از مقادیر کش‌شده سازنده. برچسب‌های دامنه تعیین می‌کنند تغییر چه زمانی اعمال می‌شود ( LIVE_IMMEDIATE  در برابر  NEXT_DECISION ). \n 3. پایگاه داده تنظیمات (اسرار + قصد کاربر) \n اعتبارنامه‌ها (مثلاً تلگرام) در پایگاه داده تنظیمات از طریق  settings_service.set_t"}, {"u": "/fa/getting-started/first-run/", "t": "First-Run Safety [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  شروع  /  اجرای اول  \n اجرای اول — ایمنی (دمو → SHADOW → LIVE) \n این موتور روی بروکر واقعی اجرا می‌شود. راهنمای رسمی مخزن یک پلکان سخت‌گیرانه است — هیچ پله‌ای را رد نکنید. \n  \n   پله  اقدام  چرا    \n  ۱️⃣  در MT5 وارد یک  حساب دمو  شوید ( File → Open an Account → Practice/Demo ) و پیش از هر کاری شماره/برچسب حساب را تأیید کنید  حساب LIVE و دمو در پنجره ورود MT5 یکسان به نظر می‌رسند  \n  ۲️⃣  در MT5:  Tools → Options → Expert Advisors → تیک \"Allow Algo Trading\"   بدون این، سفارش‌ها رد می‌شوند  \n  ۳️⃣   configs/live.yaml  را به  configs/demo.yaml  کپی کنید؛ اعتبارنامه دمو را وارد کنید؛  risk.max_concurrent_positions: 1 ،  risk.risk_per_trade_pct  (مثلاً 0.5)،  risk.max_account_drawdown_pct  را تأیید کنید  هرگز با پیکربندی LIVE در دسترس پول واقعی کار نکنید  \n  ۴️⃣  ابتدا  SHADOW  را اجرا کنید ( nexus start --mode shadow ) چند روز؛ داشبورد و گزارش‌های تلگرام را بررسی کنید  مدل، سیگنال‌ها و گی"}, {"u": "/fa/getting-started/installation/", "t": "Installation [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  شروع  /  نصب  \n موتور اسکالپ نکسوس یک  پلتفرم پژوهش‌محور معاملات کمی  است: یک زمان‌اجر شش‌ضلعی (Hexagonal) و رویدادمحور برای متاتریدر ۵ (بازار اصلی: طلا XAUUSD تایم M1) که داده‌های بازار، مهندسی ویژگی علّی، استنتاج مدل، سیاست استراتژی، کنترل ریسک، بازپخش (Replay)، اجرا، مشاهده‌پذیری و اعتبارسنجی بازتولیدپذیر را در یک خط لوله قابل‌ممیزی یکپارچه می‌کند. \n &lt;div class=\"callout\"&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;این وعده سود نیست.&lt;/strong&gt; این یک پلتفرم پژوهش و مهندسی است. وضعیت‌ها بر اساس شواهد درجه‌بندی شده‌اند و نتایج منفی هم منتشر می‌شوند — از جمله رد شدن کاندیدای پژوهشی ۷۰D خودمان بر اساس شواهد Out-of-Sample. اسکالپ با اهرم ریسک مالی شدیدی دارد.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt; \n چه چیزی آن را متفاوت می‌کند \n \n  شواهد قبل از ادعا  — متریک‌های بدون شواهد به صورت  n/a  نمایش داده می‌شوند، هرگز صفر جعلی نیستند. \n  بدون آینده‌نگری (No Lookahead)  — Walk-Forward با Purge و Embargo، ویژگی‌های کاملاً ع"}, {"u": "/fa/getting-started/quickstart/", "t": "Quickstart [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  شروع  /  شروع سریع  \n شروع سریع \n  ⧉   # ۱. نصب (توسعه‌دهندگان، از سورس)\ngit clone https://github.com/Opselon/NexusTradingForexBot.git\ncd NexusTradingForexBot\npython -m venv .venv &amp;&amp; .\\.venv\\Scripts\\Activate.ps1   # لینوکس: source .venv/bin/activate\npip install -e .[dev]\n\n# ۲. سلامت سیستم\nnexus doctor          # عیب‌یابی فقط-خواندنی در ۱۹ دسته + پیشنهاد رفع\nnexus health          # READY / DEGRADED / NOT READY\n\n# ۳. اجرا — PAPER پیش‌فرض است، هرگز بی‌صدا LIVE نمی‌شود\nnexus start           # شبیه‌سازی کاغذی، داشبورد روی http://127.0.0.1:8080\n\n# ۴. ارزیابی روی داده واقعی، با صفر اختیار سفارش\nnexus start --mode shadow\n\n# ۵. توقف\nnexus stop            # برای اجرای --daemon؛ در پیش‌زمینه Ctrl+C   \n معنای حالت‌ها \n  \n   حالت  داده  سفارش  کاربرد    \n   paper  (پیش‌فرض)  شبیه‌سازی‌شده  شبیه‌سازی‌شده  اجرای اول، UI، توسعه  \n   shadow   زنده   هیچ — صفر اختیار سفارش  ( simulated=True )  ا"}, {"u": "/fa/guides/api/", "t": "API Reference [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  راهنما  /  مرجع API  \n API Reference \n The Control Center backend is a FastAPI application exposing * 203  /api/   \n endpoints across 22 groups** (verified by scanning the route modules in \n  src/nexus_scalp/web/ ), plus Server-Sent Events for ticks and WebSocket for \n the dashboard. Everything the UI does, the API does — the UI is a consumer of \n the same surface. \n  یادداشت  Endpoint counts are generated from the repository's actual route decorators —  they drift with the code, and the docs doctor flags stale counts.  \n Discovery \n \n  Health / readiness:   GET /health  →  200  with  READY / DEGRADED ,  503  when NOT READY. \n  Engine state:   GET /api/status  and  GET /api/live/state  (the dashboard heart, includes the effective serving contract). \n  OpenAPI:  the FastAPI app serves its schema at  /openapi.json  and Swagger UI at  /docs  on the same port as the UI (  http://127.0.0.1:"}, {"u": "/fa/guides/cli/", "t": "CLI Guide [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  راهنما  /  راهنمای CLI  \n CLI Guide \n  nexus  is the application command (installation lifecycle lives in \n  install.ps1 ; everything you  operate  lives in  nexus ). From source: \n  python -m nexus_scalp.cli.main  (alias  nse ). \n Commands \n  ⧉   nexus help            # same authoritative surface as --help (+ &#x27;nexus help start&#x27;)\nnexus version         # build identity (--json / --plain)\nnexus doctor          # read-only diagnostics (19 categories) + suggested fixes\nnexus status          # health + environment + version\nnexus health          # quick health summary (READY / DEGRADED / NOT READY)\nnexus config          # inspect/validate active configuration (secrets masked)\nnexus start           # PAPER mode by default — never LIVE silently\nnexus stop / restart  # control the background engine (honest dead-pid reporting)\nnexus logs [--tail N] [--errors]\nnexus test --mode quick|u"}, {"u": "/fa/guides/common-workflows/", "t": "Common Workflows [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  راهنما  /  گردش‌کارهای رایج  \n Common Workflows \n 1. Daily development loop \n  ⧉   git pull &amp;&amp; .venv/Scripts/Activate.ps1        # Windows dev\nnexus test --mode quick                        # fast sanity\n# ... edit ...\npytest tests/unit -q -k &quot;70 or schema&quot;         # targeted suite\n./beforePush.ps1 -SkipPush                     # full gate before pushing   \n 2. Evaluate the engine on real data (risk-free) \n  ⧉   nexus start --mode shadow      # live feed, zero order authority\n# observe Control Center → SHADOW section: disagreement analysis, drift, health\nnexus stop   \n 3. Research a candidate \n  ⧉   nexus model-dataset-build      # canonical dataset (fingerprinted)\nnexus model-experiment-create  # fair A/B/C protocol\nnexus model-train              # deterministic, seeded\nnexus model-validate           # walk-forward + OOS gate + robustness\nnexus model-replay          "}, {"u": "/fa/guides/troubleshooting/", "t": "Troubleshooting [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  راهنما  /  عیب‌یابی  \n Troubleshooting \n  Rule of thumb:  nexus doctor  first — it reports 19 diagnostic categories  with suggested fixes and is the same gate the engine runs pre-launch.  \n Engine refuses to start \n  \n   Symptom  Likely cause  Action    \n  \"MT5 terminal missing/not running\"  terminal closed / not installed  start MT5, log in (demo first), retry  \n  config validation error  YAML contract violation   nexus config --validate &lt;path&gt; ; fix the named key  \n  environment blocked (exit 3)  Windows ARM64  unsupported by dependency stack; use x64  \n  migration gate failure  schema drift   nexus db migrate ; check  nexus db hygiene status   \n   \n UI / dashboard \n  \n   Symptom  Likely cause  Action    \n  dashboard unreachable  port drift (dev UI/API ports can move)  check  nexus status  output / launcher log for the bound port  \n  \"Cannot GET /\" on some port  wrong port — so"}, {"u": "/fa/docs-hub/", "t": "Nexus Scalp Engine — Documentation [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  مرکز مستندات  \n Nexus Scalp Engine — Documentation \n  Research-driven quantitative trading platform  — a hexagonal, event-driven \n scalping engine for MetaTrader 5 (primary market: XAUUSD M1), built around \n causal feature engineering, artifact-first model governance, deterministic \n research tooling, and forensic observability. \n  مهم  This documentation describes a  research and engineering platform . It is  not investment advice, and nothing here is a promise of profitability.  Leveraged scalping carries extreme financial risk. See   Project Status  for what is certified vs experimental.  \n Start here \n  \n   Question  Page    \n  What is Nexus and why does it exist?   Vision   \n  How do I run it?   Quickstart   \n  How is the architecture structured?   Architecture Overview   \n  How does data become a decision?   Data Flow   \n  How is research validated?   Research Methodology   \n  Wh"}, {"u": "/fa/project/capabilities/", "t": "Capability Matrix [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  پروژه  /  ماتریس قابلیت‌ها  \n Capability Matrix \n Legend: ✅ Certified · 🟢 Implemented · 🟡 Experimental · 🔵 Research · 🚧 In \n progress · 📌 Planned · ⚪ Not verified \n  \n   Capability  Status  Evidence (repository)  Notes    \n  Causal 50D feature engine ( scalp_v1 )  ✅ Certified   features/scalp_features.py , schema registry, golden/parity tests  live contract; NaN/Inf deterministic fallback  \n  70D canonical contract ( scalp_v3 )  🟢 Implemented (research)   features/schema_contract.py  SSoT, hash, inference validator (10 rejection codes)  candidate-only; negative OOS evidence so far  \n  Liquidity intelligence (10D block)  🟡 Experimental   features/liquidity_engine.py , INV-019 causality rules  research series; governed by  liquidity_features_enabled   \n  News intelligence 10D + bounded gate  🟡 Experimental   news/ , gate bounds boost ≤0.05 / penalty ≤0.10  opt-in, disabled by default; ca"}, {"u": "/fa/project/milestones/", "t": "Milestones & Project Story [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  پروژه  /  نقاط عطف  \n Milestones — the project story \n This is a factual history reconstructed from the repository's own records \n (taskboard, decision records, forensic reports). No invented narrative. \n Phase I — Engine core (single-agent era) \n The original engine: hexagonal architecture, MT5 adapters, 50D causal features, \n ScalpNet, policy matrix, risk engine, order manager, SQLite WAL ledger, \n FastAPI Control Center. Foundation invariants established: no sync DB on the \n tick path, no order authority for learning components. \n Phase II — Multi-agent forensic era \n Development moved to a  multi-agent model  (up to 56+ parallel AI agents) with \n a strict engineering contract: taskboard, locks, bug ledger, runtime invariants, \n change control. The bug ledger (BUG-001…) and forensic acceptance reports date \n from this era. Key products: database hygiene, migrations, incident respons"}, {"u": "/fa/project/roadmap/", "t": "Roadmap [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  پروژه  /  نقشه راه  \n نقشه راه \n  یادداشت  واژگان: موارد  برنامه‌ریزی‌شده ،  در حال ارزیابی ،  جهت پژوهشی  یا   تکمیل‌شده  هستند — نه «به‌زودی» و نه تضمین‌شده. هر مورد دروازه تکمیل دارد.  \n اکنون \n  \n   جریان  مورد  وضعیت  معیار تکمیل    \n  اعتبارسنجی  بازسازی شواهد کاندیدای 70D با معناشناسی اصلاح‌شده اطمینان (CHG-0042)  در حال ارزیابی  کاندیدای معتبر با مصنوعات walk-forward + OOS بازتولیدپذیر، یا توقف مستندشده  \n  پژوهش  تعمیق شواهد خلاف‌واقع (CHG-0041، ۲۰۹۵ تصمیم)  در جریان  ادغام شواهد طبقه‌بندی‌شده در بازنگری سیاست  \n  زمان‌اجرا  سخت‌سازی قرارداد record-builder (BUG-185)  تکمیل‌شده  تست دروازه اجرا در هر ۷ نقطه جهش bundle  \n   \n بعد \n  \n   جریان  مورد  وضعیت  وابستگی    \n  ML  تصمیم ارتقای چمپیون 70D (اپراتوری)  برنامه‌ریزی‌شده  کاندیدای معتبر + راستی‌آزمایی ۱۴-دروازه‌ای  \n  سیاست  بازنگری سیاست با شواهد خلاف‌واقع  برنامه‌ریزی‌شده  خروجی موتور counterfactual  \n  مستندات  پوشش ترجمه"}, {"u": "/fa/project/scope/", "t": "Scope [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  پروژه  /  محدوده  \n Scope \n In scope \n \n A complete quantitative trading  pipeline : data adapters (MT5/paper/gateway), \n \n causal feature engineering (50D active contract; 60D/70D research family), \n deep model inference (ScalpNet TCN + self-attention), SMC policy matrix, \n invariant risk engine, execution with 60-scenario router, SQLite WAL \n accounting ledger, experience/autopsy intelligence, research &amp; validation \n (walk-forward, OOS gate, robustness), replay and shadow runtimes, model \n governance, observability (structured logs, incidents, forensics, Telegram), \n FastAPI Control Center UI, packaged Windows release + installer + update/rollback. \n \n  Multi-agent engineering memory : architecture map, bug ledger, runtime \n \n invariants, contracts, taskboard, decision records — treated as first-class \n repository artifacts. \n Out of scope (by design) \n \n Multi-broker support bey"}, {"u": "/fa/project/status/", "t": "Project Status [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  پروژه  /  وضعیت پروژه  \n وضعیت پروژه \n  مهم  برچسب‌های وضعیت شواهدمحورند. «پیاده‌سازی‌شده» یعنی قابلیت در کد موجود و با  تست پوشش داده شده. «تایید‌شده» برای قابلیت‌هایی است که سابقه پذیرش جنگل‌بانی  رسمی دارند. هیچ‌جا ادعای سودآوری تضمین‌شده وجود ندارد.  \n تصویر کلی \n  \n   بُعد  وضعیت  شواهد    \n  نسخه   9.0.6  (semver، منبع یکتا:  pyproject.toml )  خط لوله انتشار  \n  انتشار   منتشرشده  (تگ‌های v9.0.0 تا v9.0.6؛ SHA-256، مانیفست، SBOM)  GitHub Releases  \n  زمان‌اجرا  سخت‌شده؛ PAPER پیش‌فرض؛ LIVE فقط با تأیید صریح  قرارداد CLI + دکتر پیش‌پرواز  \n  اجرای زنده  کارا (MT5 Win32 IPC + دروازه ZMQ) با fail-safe تطبیق حساب  رگرسیون BUG-142  \n  حلقه پژوهش  سرتاسری کارا (دیتاست ← walk-forward ← دروازه OOS)  مجموعه‌های research/  \n  قرارداد زنده 50D ( scalp_v1 )   فعال    features/schema.py   \n  قرارداد 70D ( scalp_v3 )  SSoT پژوهشی؛  فقط کاندید    features/schema_contract.py   \n  شواهد 70D تا ام"}, {"u": "/fa/project/vision/", "t": "Vision & Why [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  پروژه  /  چشم‌انداز و چرایی  \n چشم‌انداز — چرا نکسوس؟ \n مشکل \n پروژه‌های معاملات الگوریتمی معمولاً به یکی از این دو شکل شکست می‌خورند: \n \n  حقیقت را پنهان می‌کنند.  متریک‌ها ساختگی یا خوش‌بینانه‌اند، شکست‌ها بی‌صداست \n \n و فاصله‌ی بک‌تست تا اجرای واقعی هرگز اندازه‌گیری نمی‌شود. \n \n  آینده را لو می‌دهند.  ویژگی‌ها یا برچسب‌ها از اطلاعاتی استفاده می‌کنند که \n \n در لحظه تصمیم در دسترس نبوده — پس نتیجه فارغ از ظاهرش از بنیاد نامعتبر است. \n موتور اسکالپ نکسوس دقیقاً علیه همین دو شکست ساخته شد: یک **خط لوله کامل و \n قابل‌ممیزی** — داده بازار ← ویژگی ← مدل ← سیاست ← ریسک ← اجرا ← حسابداری ← \n پژوهش — که در آن هر مرحله مشاهده‌پذیر، هر هویت اثر‌انگاشت‌شده و هر ادعا \n ردپذیر (falsifiable) است. \n فلسفه (مستند در مخزن) \n \n  شواهد قبل از ادعا.  متریک بدون شواهد  n/a  نمایش داده می‌شود — هرگز صفر \n \n جعلی. ادعاهای زمان اجرا درجه‌بندی می‌شوند (CODE / TEST / INTEGRATION / LIVE). \n \n  بدون نگاه به آیند"}, {"u": "/fa/reference/cli-reference/", "t": "CLI Reference [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  مرجع  /  مرجع CLI  \n CLI Reference \n The authoritative surface is always  nexus help  /  nexus &lt;command&gt; --help  \n (this page documents the verified contract; the CLI is golden-tested by 66 \n end-to-end tests). \n Global flags \n  \n   Flag  Effect    \n   --json   machine-readable output (parity-tested keys)  \n   --plain   no color, no formatting  \n   --no-color   disable color only  \n   \n Command groups \n  \n   Command  Purpose  Notes    \n  `nexus start [--mode paper\\  shadow\\  live] [--port N] [--daemon]`  run engine  paper default; live needs interactive  --yes /confirmation; port default 8080  \n   nexus stop  /  nexus restart   daemon control  pidfile-based; dead-pid reported honestly (BUG-172)  \n   nexus doctor   19-category diagnostics + suggested fixes   --json  for tooling  \n   nexus status  /  nexus health   environment + health  READY / DEGRADED / NOT READY  \n   nexus confi"}, {"u": "/fa/reference/faq/", "t": "FAQ [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  مرجع  /  پرسش‌های متداول  \n پرسش‌های متداول \n  نکسوس چیست؟  \n یک پلتفرم پژوهش‌محور معاملات کمی: موتور اسکالپ شش‌ضلعی و رویدادمحور برای متاتریدر ۵ (XAUUSD M1) با ویژگی‌های علّی، مدل‌های عمیق، ریسک ثابت‌شده، پژوهش قطعی و مشاهده‌پذیری فارنزیک. \n  آیا این یک ربات معاملاتی زنده است؟  \n می‌تواند معاملات زنده اجرا کند — اما پیش‌فرض PAPER است، SHADOW صفر اختیار سفارش دارد، LIVE نیازمند تأیید صریح تعاملی است و مخزن کاندیداهای ردشده را منتشر می‌کند. این پلتفرمی پژوهشی با زمان‌اجر است، نه دستگاه پول. \n  بدون MT5 می‌توانم اجرا کنم؟  \n بله — حالت PAPER و کل مجموعه تست بدون بروکر اجرا می‌شوند؛ Docker هم به‌صورت پیش‌فرض در PAPER کار می‌کند. \n  ۷۰D چیست؟  \n قرارداد مرجع ویژگی پژوهشی (۵۰ پایه + ۱۰ اخبار + ۱۰ نقدینگی). زنده نیست — قرارداد زنده ۵۰D است. کاندیدای ۷۰D تاکنون بر اساس شواهد OOS رد شده است. \n  نشتی (Lookahead) چگونه پیشگیری می‌شود؟  \n Walk-Forward پاکسازی‌شده و تحریم‌شده، ویژگی‌های کاملاً علّ"}, {"u": "/fa/reference/glossary/", "t": "Glossary [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  مرجع  /  واژه‌نامه  \n Glossary \n Project-specific terms. Product/module names (Nexus, ScalpNet, OrderManager, \n MT5, 70D, 50D) are canonical and never translated in code; each language's \n  terminology file  defines how they are presented. \n  \n   Term  Meaning in NSE    \n   50D / scalp_v1   the 50-dimensional causal base feature contract — the ACTIVE live feature schema  \n   70D / scalp_v3   the canonical research feature contract: Base 50 (0..49) + News 10 (50..59) + Liquidity 10 (60..69); candidate-only, not live  \n   scalp_v4   a candidate 70D-family contract (integration-era); classified LEGACY/semantically-different vs v3  \n   Schema hash   SHA-256 over canonical JSON of feature (index, name, family) — reordering invalidates models  \n   ScalpNet   dual-path model: 2D MLP for single-tick snapshots, 3D TCN + self-attention for sequences; 4-logit head  \n   Champion / Challenger   pro"}, {"u": "/fa/reference/terminology/", "t": "Terminology & Translations [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  مرجع  /  اصطلاحات و ترجمه‌ها  \n Terminology &amp; Translations \n Untranslatable canon \n These stay in English/Latin script in every language (identifiers, contracts, \n product names): \n `Nexus · ScalpNet · OrderManager · RiskEngine · LiveEngine · IMT5Port · \n AuditRepository · MT5 · ZMQ · SQLite · FastAPI · 50D · 70D · scalp_v1 · \n scalp_v3 · NO_TRADE · BUY · SELL · WAIT · Champion · Challenger · Shadow · \n OOS · walk-forward · O(1) · MFE · MAE` \n Canonical term translations \n The authoritative per-language table lives in \n  site/terminology/&lt;lang&gt;.json  (consumed by the translation audit). Core \n entries: \n  \n   EN  FA (فارسی)  ES  AR (العربية)  DE    \n  Feature Vector  بردار ویژگی  Vector de características  متجه السمات  Merkmalsvektor  \n  Feature Contract  قرارداد ویژگی  Contrato de características  عقد السمات  Merkmalsvertrag  \n  Model Registry  ثبت مدل  Registro de modelos  "}, {"u": "/fa/research/backtesting/", "t": "Backtesting [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  پژوهش  /  بک‌تست  \n Backtesting \n Determinism \n Backtests ( research/backtest.py ) are deterministic: fixed seeds, frozen \n datasets, no wall-clock dependence. Same inputs ⇒ same results. \n Friction model \n Spread, slippage and latency are modeled, not ignored: \n \n fills on historical bid/ask (direction-aware), \n tick-level SL/TP first-touch resolution, \n logical latency applied to the decision path, \n robustness stress re-runs under degraded friction (spread/slippage/latency \n \n shocks) — a strategy that only works under ideal fills does not pass. \n Boundary honesty \n \n Backtests produce evidence, not promises. Results feed the validation \n \n pipeline; they never bypass the OOS gate. \n \n Fees/commissions follow the configured friction profile; metrics without the \n \n underlying evidence render  n/a  — never fabricated zeros. \n \n Streaming replay ( research/streaming_replay.py ) is the"}, {"u": "/fa/research/counterfactuals/", "t": "Counterfactuals [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  پژوهش  /  خلاف‌واقع  \n Counterfactuals (CHG-0041) \n The question \n Backtests score trades that happened. The counterfactual engine asks the \n other question: **what would have happened on the decisions the engine did NOT \n take?** If the engine abstains (NO_TRADE), was the abstention valuable? \n How it works \n  research/counterfactual.py : \n \n Loads canonical tick datasets (fingerprinted, offline) and decision \n \n snapshots from  audit_signals . \n \n Joins each NO_TRADE decision to the tick window at decision time. \n Applies  certified fill semantics  hypothetically at time T. \n Walks ticks forward to compute MFE / MAE / R / cost / time-to-target. \n Classifies each abstention using  documented rules  (never ad-hoc). \n Stratifies evidence by gate, regime, confidence, session, direction. \n \n First evidence run (2026-09-01) \n 2095 NO_TRADE decisions (2026-08-24 → 09-01) walked over 3.2M ti"}, {"u": "/fa/research/datasets/", "t": "Datasets [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  پژوهش  /  دیتاست‌ها  \n Datasets \n Bar datasets \n Built by  research/dataset.py  +  model_generation/  with quality gates \n (coverage, ordering, duplicates, horizon boundaries). Each dataset is a \n versioned artifact with a fingerprint ( ds_*  id) used in manifests and run \n snapshots. \n Tick datasets (CHG-0041 / TICK_DATASET_META v2) \n  research/mt5_tick_dataset.py  acquires ticks from the **certified adapter \n surface** ( copy_ticks_range ,  COPY_TICKS_ALL ), with: \n \n bounded, deduplicated acquisition (post BUG-188 semantics), \n immutable parquet store with  content fingerprints , \n provenance metadata v2 (symbol, window, source, acquisition identity), \n cache-hit idempotence — re-running acquisition never duplicates. \n \n After acquisition the dataset is fully  offline : research needs no broker. \n Rules \n \n A dataset is immutable once fingerprinted — corrections produce a new \n \n da"}, {"u": "/fa/research/methodology/", "t": "Research Methodology [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  پژوهش  /  روش‌شناسی  \n پژوهش برای تولید  شواهد ابطال‌پذیر  وجود دارد. کاندیدایی که ابطال‌پذیر نباشد (بدون OOS، بدون برابری بازپخش، بدون منشأ) هرگز به مسیر زنده راه نمی‌یابد. \n زنجیره \n  ⧉   داده (دیتاست‌های اثرانگشت‌شده) → ویژگی‌ها (قرارداد علّی) → برچسب‌گذاری (سه‌سد)\n→ آموزش (بذردار، قطعی) → بک‌تست (آگاه از اصطکاک)\n→ Walk-Forward (پاکسازی + تحریم) → گیت OOS (شکست یعنی REJECTED)\n→ تست استحکام → خلاف‌واقع → رجیستری → سایه → ترویج اپراتور   \n اجزا \n \n  دیتاست‌ها  — تغییرناپذیر، اثرانگشت‌شده، با منشأ؛ دیتاست‌های تیک از سطح آداپتور معتبر دریافت و پس از آن آفلاین‌اند. \n  بک‌تست‌ها  — قطعی؛ اسپرد/اسلیپیج/لاتنسی مدل می‌شوند. \n  بازپخش  — بی‌دقیق (Bit-Exact) نسبت به دیتاست (تست‌های ضد-نشتی)؛ بازپخش جریانی موتور مشترک را روی ساعت منطقی با پرشدن شبیه‌سازی‌شده اجرا می‌کند و فراخوانی  order_send  در آن با تست ممنوع شده است. \n  خلاف‌واقع (CHG-0041)  — قدم زدن تصمیم‌های NO_TRADE با پر شدن فرضی: ۲۰۹۵"}, {"u": "/fa/research/out-of-sample/", "t": "Out-of-Sample Gate [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  پژوهش  /  گیت OOS  \n Out-of-Sample (OOS) Gate \n Contract \n  research/oos.py  is a  hard gate : out-of-sample failure ⇒ candidate \n REJECTED, regardless of in-sample performance. There is no override path in \n the pipeline. \n Floors (model lifecycle validation) \n  \n   Metric  Floor    \n  macro-F1 (OOS)  ≥ 0.34  \n  balanced accuracy  ≥ 0.34  \n  calibration error (ECE)  ≤ 0.15  \n  minimum evidence  ≥ 100 rows  \n   \n Evidence the gate bites \n The 70D liquidity candidate — the most heavily engineered research series in \n the repository — was rejected by this exact gate (OOS NOT_ELIGIBLE) after \n real-data walk-forward and shadow benchmarks came back negative/inconclusive. \n A gate that rejects nothing is decoration; this one has a public rejection on \n its record. See  Project Status  and \n  docs/TASK-05-70D-SHADOW-FINAL.md . \n Temporal OOS protocol \n Temporal splits only ( timestamp -order"}, {"u": "/fa/research/replay/", "t": "Replay [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  پژوهش  /  بازپخش  \n Replay \n What replay is \n Replay re-runs the engine's decision logic over historical data and proves it \n produces  the same decisions  the live/training pipeline produced on that \n data. It is the execution-fidelity check between research and runtime. \n Two engines \n  \n   Engine  Module  Character    \n  Dataset replay   model_generation/replay.py  +  replay_70d_vector    bit-exact : replay vector must equal the dataset's stored vector (anti-leakage tests)  \n  Streaming replay   research/streaming_replay.py  (CHG-0035)  shared  LiveEngine  over a logical clock (zero sleeps): incremental bar aggregation, causal 50D + news + liquidity at time T, frozen policy + RiskEngine, direction-aware simulated fills on historical bid/ask, tick SL/TP first-touch, ledger MFE/MAE —  NO  order_send  (test-enforced)   \n   \n Anti-leakage \n Features at time T may consume only informatio"}, {"u": "/fa/research/reproducibility/", "t": "Reproducibility [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  پژوهش  /  بازتولیدپذیری  \n Reproducibility \n Identity chain \n Every research artifact carries the chain that produced it: \n  ⧉   dataset fingerprint → feature schema hash → model manifest (scaler, weights)\n→ git commit → effective config (seeds, splits, purge/embargo)   \n Run snapshots ( research_run_snapshots ) store these at run time; provenance \n fields may be  NOT_RECORDED  (honest) but are never invented or backfilled. \n Determinism sources \n \n seeded training (seed-before-model construction — BUG-101 regression), \n frozen datasets (immutable, fingerprinted), \n logical-clock streaming replay (zero sleeps), \n freeze capture at forward-test cutoff +  post-run re-verification  of the \n \n freeze ( research/forward_test.py ). \n What breaks reproducibility (and is therefore guarded) \n  \n   Threat  Guard    \n  dataset mutation  immutable fingerprinted artifacts  \n  feature reordering  sc"}, {"u": "/fa/research/validation/", "t": "Validation [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  پژوهش  /  اعتبارسنجی  \n اعتبارسنجی دلیل وجود این پلتفرم است. شکست در هر گیت برای آن کاندیدا پایانی است — بدون میانگین‌گیری، بدون استثنا. \n زنجیره گیت‌ها \n  \n   لایه  گیت‌ها    \n  دیتاست  گیت‌های کیفیت · اثرانگشت · منشأ  \n  ویژگی‌ها  هش اسکیما · بُعد · بازه · ترتیب  \n  مدل  گیت بارگذاری ۱۰-گانه · کالیبراسیون · حداقل شواهد  \n  پژوهش  Walk-Forward پاکسازی‌شده/تحریم‌شده · کف‌های OOS · استحکام  \n  حکمرانی  راستی‌آزمایی ۱۴-گانه · تراکنش ترویج  \n  زمان‌اجر  گیت استقرار فارنزیک قبل از هر انتشار  \n  انتشار  SHA-256 · مانیفست · SBOM · راستی‌آزمایی پس از انتشار  \n   \n کف‌های OOS (چرخه حیات مدل) \n macro-F1 ≥ ۰٫۳۴ · دقت متوازن ≥ ۰٫۳۴ · ECE ≤ ۰٫۱۵ · شواهد ≥ ۱۰۰ ردیف. \n گیت واقعاً می‌گزد — اثبات عمومی \n کاندیدای نقدینگی ۷۰D — پژوهش‌شده‌ترین سری این مخزن — توسط همین زنجیره رد شد (OOS NOT_ELIGIBLE) پس از آنکه Walk-Forward و بنچمارک سایه روی داده واقعی منفی بازگشت. قرارداد زنده روی ۵۰D ماند. گیتی که چیز"}, {"u": "/fa/research/walk-forward/", "t": "Walk-Forward [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "  پژوهش  /  Walk-Forward  \n Walk-Forward \n Method \n  training/walk_forward_trainer.py  +  research/walkforward.py  implement \n  purged, embargoed walk-forward  (Lopez de Prado): training folds are \n separated from test folds by a purge gap (label horizon) and an embargo gap \n (serial-correlation buffer), evaluated across temporally ordered folds. \n Defaults that matter (BUG-183) \n The production research path once ran with purge/embargo silently disabled — \n the constants existed but weren't wired. This is recorded as BUG-183 and fixed \n with regression tests:  DEFAULT_PURGE_SECONDS = 300 , `DEFAULT_EMBARGO_SECONDS \n = 60  are now wired into  ResearchPipeline.validate_candidate`, \n  OOSGate.evaluate ,  WalkForwardEngine.validate  and  BacktestEngine.run , and \n the  effective  purge/embargo values are recorded in every run's config. \n Why it is non-negotiable \n A walk-forward without pur"}, {"u": "/fa/getting-started/", "t": "شروع [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "Install, run and configure the engine. PAPER mode is the default; SHADOW gives you live data with zero order authority."}, {"u": "/fa/project/", "t": "پروژه [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "What Nexus is, what is certified vs experimental, where it is going — all evidence-graded."}, {"u": "/fa/architecture/", "t": "معماری [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "How the engine is built: hexagonal layers, the tick-to-decision path, model governance, and the intelligence loop."}, {"u": "/fa/research/", "t": "پژوهش [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "How historical data becomes falsifiable evidence — datasets, backtests, walk-forward, OOS, replay, counterfactuals."}, {"u": "/fa/engineering/", "t": "مهندسی [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "Quality gates, CI architecture, the release process, and the security posture."}, {"u": "/fa/guides/", "t": "راهنما [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "Operating the engine day to day: CLI, REST API, troubleshooting, common workflows."}, {"u": "/fa/contributing/", "t": "مشارکت [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "The engineering contract, documentation ownership, and how to add a language."}, {"u": "/fa/reference/", "t": "مرجع [fa]", "l": "fa", "x": "CLI reference, glossary, terminology, and honest answers in the FAQ."}, {"u": "/ar/", "t": "Home [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "Nexus Scalp Engine documentation homepage what's new capabilities architecture research"}, {"u": "/ar/releases/", "t": "الإصدارات [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "releases v9.0.8 changelog what's new history 959d7d9"}, {"u": "/ar/architecture/code-navigation/", "t": "Code Navigation Map — Nexus Scalp Engine [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  البنية  /  code navigation  \n Code Navigation Map — Nexus Scalp Engine \n  Where to find things, for a developer (or agent) landing fresh in this repo.  This map is an INDEX. Detailed truth lives in:  -  agents/skill.md  — authoritative architecture map + repo contract (READ FIRST)  -  docs/architecture/dependency-map.md  — subsystem edges + contracts  -  docs/architecture/comment-style.md  — comment/doc conventions  -  docs/RELEASE.md  — CLI exit codes, update protocol, release verification  -  agents/bugs.md  — bug ledger (append-only; grep  ^## BUG-  tail for next free id)  \n Startup &amp; lifecycle \n  \n   Concern  Where    \n  Primary launcher (bootstrap sys.path, adapter bind, engine + web)   NexusTradingForexBot.py   \n  CLI entry ( nexus  /  nse , Typer)   src/nexus_scalp/cli/main.py   \n  Engine construction + async tick loop   src/nexus_scalp/application/live_engine.py  ( run_loop"}, {"u": "/ar/architecture/comment-style/", "t": "Comment Style Guide — Nexus Scalp Engine [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  البنية  /  comment style  \n Comment Style Guide — Nexus Scalp Engine \n  Applies to all Python source in  src/ ,  tests/ , and  scripts/ .  Repo rule of thumb:  the repository should not contain more comments — it should contain better comments.   \n The one test \n  Could a competent developer derive this from the code itself?  \n If YES → do not comment. If NO → the comment may be valuable; then ask: \n \"Will this still be true and useful six months from now?\" If NO → do not write it. \n What comments are FOR \n A comment must be one of: \n  \n   Category  Documents  Example    \n  INVARIANT  a rule the code must keep but does not enforce visibly  \"Resume-safe hash: the hasher must cover the already-downloaded bytes too.\"  \n  SAFETY  fail-closed / fail-safe semantics  \"Fail closed: no inference must never yield a trade decision.\"  \n  CONCURRENCY  lock ownership, ordering, atomicity  \"Hold the "}, {"u": "/ar/architecture/control-center-ui/", "t": "Control Center UI Architecture (CHG-0043, TASK-CONTROL-CENTER) [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  البنية  /  control center ui  \n Control Center UI Architecture (CHG-0043, TASK-CONTROL-CENTER) \n  Operator-facing architecture of the NEXUS Control Center. UI-owned doc;  backend architecture lives in  docs/architecture/  elsewhere. Status  semantics here are the CONTRACT for every future CC view.  \n Purpose \n One coherent surface where an operator answers, without reading logs: \n WHAT is happening → WHY → WHAT changed → WHAT is blocked → WHAT is healthy → \n WHAT is serving → WHY did/didn't a trade happen → WHAT is safe to do next. \n Observation model: OBSERVE → UNDERSTAND → INVESTIGATE → ACT → VERIFY. \n Navigation &amp; Screens \n  \n   Tab (nav id)  Screen  Data sources (all read-only)    \n  Control Center ( tab-control-center )  Overview: mode banner, 6-tile status strip (Runtime/Data/Model/Inference/Database/MT5), runtime truth, market snapshot, latest decision, active warnings   /ap"}, {"u": "/ar/architecture/crash-safety/", "t": "Crash-Safety Architecture (NSE) [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  البنية  /  crash safety  \n Crash-Safety Architecture (NSE) \n  Status: HARDENED_WITH_GAPS baseline documented 2026-09-01 (rev 2 — checker  regex fix + 381-site silent-handler backlog tracked as P1 violations).  Owner: Nexus-Main (crash-containment master pass).  Scope: the failure contract of every major execution boundary, from process  startup through model tensor execution, trading execution, Web/API, updater,  release pipeline, and shutdown.  Companion documents:  failure-recovery-matrix.md  (per-subsystem failure  matrix),  artifacts/forensics/crash-safety-audit.json  (machine audit).  \n \n 1. Governing principle \n The requirement is NOT \"the application must never crash\". The requirement is: \n  ⧉   NO SILENT CRASH      NO SILENT EXCEPTION      NO FALSE SUCCESS\nNO FAKE HEALTH       NO FABRICATED MODEL OUTPUT\nNO UNSAFE TRADING AFTER CRITICAL FAILURE\nNO CORRUPTED STATE AFTER FAILURE  "}, {"u": "/ar/architecture/data-flow/", "t": "Data Flow — Tick to Decision [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  البنية  /  تدفق البيانات  \n Data Flow — from tick to decision \n This is the canonical path (from  agents/skill.md  §4). Every arrow is a \n contract boundary. \n  ⧉   TickData (MT5 / paper / gateway)\n  → ScalpFeatureEngine.to_tensor_input()\n      50D base (scalp_v1 · FEATURE_NAMES · [-3,+3] · finite)\n  → assemble_70d / build_70d_vector()\n      70D canonical: Base 0..49 | News 10D 50..59 | Liquidity 10D 60..69\n  → InferenceContractValidator\n      scaler dim == feature dim · schema hash · finite · bounds\n  → ScalpNet → 4 logits (NO_TRADE / BUY / SELL / WAIT) → confidence gate 0.35\n  → regime_classifier (Regime Guardian)\n  → signals/policy + rule_matrix (~30 rules, TTL 5s cache)\n  → RiskEngine.calculate_dynamic_volume() + evaluate_proposal()\n      free-margin 20% clamp · tier caps · HARD_MAX_LOTS\n  → OrderManager (60-scenario router · 11 position states ·\n      MAX_TOTAL_EXPOSURE=1 · 30s re"}, {"u": "/ar/architecture/database/", "t": "Database Architecture [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  البنية  /  قاعدة البيانات  \n Database Architecture \n Canonical stores \n  \n   DB  Contents  Notes    \n   artifacts/audit.db   trading ledger, experience outcomes, accounting, research registry, strategy lifecycle, incidents, hygiene  one canonical ledger; SQLite  WAL   \n   artifacts/news.db   news ingestion, analysis, consensus, impacts  lazy schema on first save  \n   candle_intel.db   candle intelligence  versioned schema  \n  settings DB  secrets + user intent (Telegram creds via  settings_service )  never in YAML (INV-010)  \n   \n Write path \n  AuditRepository  queues writes to a  background worker thread  — the tick \n hot path never performs synchronous DB work (INV-001). Historical \n experience/outcome/ledger rows are  immutable  (INV-007); corrections go \n through evidence → reconstruction → derived records with provenance, never row \n rewrites. \n Migrations \n  src/nexus_scalp/datab"}, {"u": "/ar/architecture/dependency-map/", "t": "Architecture Dependency Map — Nexus Scalp Engine (NSE) [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  البنية  /  dependency map  \n Architecture Dependency Map — Nexus Scalp Engine (NSE) \n  Maintained per the MASTER MULTI-AGENT CONTRACT §9 (see  agents/multi-agent-git-contract.md ).  Describes actual subsystem relationships (verified against executable code; see agents/skill.md for the full inventory).  Every edge documents: contract, direction, expected data, safety guarantees.  \n Canonical high-level flow \n  ⧉   MT5\n  │  (tick/order/position/account events)\n  ▼\nMT5 Adapter / Providers            [ports: IMT5Port; adapters: mt5/, paper/, remote]\n  │  (normalized events)\n  ▼\nLiveEngine (async event loop)      [src/nexus_scalp/application/live_engine.py]\n  ├─ Feature Engine                [features/scalp_features.py → FEATURE_VECTOR_50D]\n  ├─ Model Runtime                 [models/scalp_net.py → MODEL_MANIFEST; Champion/Challenger]\n  ├─ News Context                  [news/ → NEWS_CONTEXT]"}, {"u": "/ar/architecture/execution-pipeline/", "t": "Execution Pipeline [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  البنية  /  خط أنابيب التنفيذ  \n Execution Pipeline \n  execution/order_manager.py  is the single dispatch authority (INV-004). It is \n large by design (convention-locked hot path) and is being decomposed \n surgically, seam by seam, with golden tests. \n Path of an order \n  ⧉   TradeProposal (frozen domain contract, execution_id trace)\n  → policy/confluence checks (SMC matrix, Regime Guardian, confidence gate)\n  → RiskEngine.evaluate_proposal() → dynamic volume (fractional Kelly)\n  → OrderManager router (60 scenarios: fills, rejections, partials, errors)\n  → IMT5Port adapter (Win32 IPC / ZMQ / paper)\n  → position lifecycle (11 states with hysteresis)\n  → protective exits (SL/TP first-touch, breakeven lock, profit giveback,\n      adaptive exit protection)\n  → broker reconciliation (broker truth wins — INV-011)\n  → accounting + autopsy (immutable ledger)   \n Hard clamps (never bypassed) \n  "}, {"u": "/ar/architecture/failure-recovery-matrix/", "t": "Failure-Recovery Matrix (NSE crash-containment pass) [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  البنية  /  failure recovery matrix  \n Failure-Recovery Matrix (NSE crash-containment pass) \n  Status: baseline 2026-09-01. Companion to  crash-safety.md  and   artifacts/forensics/crash-safety-audit.json .  Every row = subsystem × failure → expected console log, state, recovery,  exit, and the test that proves it. GREEN means failure-injected → detected →  logged → safe behavior → regression exists (never \"a try/except exists\").  \n Legend — State: truthful runtime state after the failure. Log: minimum \n console/file record. Rec: recovery policy. Exit: CLI/process exit contract. \n Test: primary regression evidence. \n  \n   #  Subsystem  Failure  Log (console)  State  Rec  Exit  Test    \n  1  startup  missing/invalid config at launch  red panel  cfg_detail=Parse error…  + doctor FAIL  NOT READY  halt  1 / EXIT_RUNTIME  launcher doctor contract; BUG-149/156 lineage  \n  2  startup   _prefli"}, {"u": "/ar/architecture/model-pipeline/", "t": "Model Pipeline [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  البنية  /  خط أنابيب النموذج  \n Model Pipeline \n Lifecycle \n  ⧉   DATASET (versioned artifact + quality gates + fingerprint)\n  → EXPERIMENT (equal budgets/seeds/splits; dataset-fairness gate)\n  → CANDIDATE MODEL (+ manifest: schema hash · scaler · dataset ID · git commit)\n  → VALIDATION (walk-forward · OOS gate · robustness · calibration)\n  → REGISTRY (content-addressed; challenger only)\n  → LOAD GATE (10 gates, enforced at every attach)\n  → SHADOW PARITY (zero order authority)\n  → OPERATOR PROMOTION (READY_FOR_REVIEW → APPROVED → CHAMPION; atomic transaction)\n  → ROLLBACK PREVIEW / EMERGENCY FREEZE   \n Artifact-first Model Factory ( model_generation/ ) \n Datasets, experiments and models are **versioned filesystem artifacts with \n manifests** — inference needs no database. The manifest carries \n  feature_schema_hash ,  training_dataset_id , scaler identity and git commit. \n ScalpNet re"}, {"u": "/ar/architecture/observability-log-contract/", "t": "Observability Log Contract — frozen 2026-09-01 (Agent 2) [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  البنية  /  observability log contract  \n Observability Log Contract — frozen 2026-09-01 (Agent 2) \n Authoritative in-repo reference for the log-noise contracts proven in the \n operational-observability sprint and pinned by \n  tests/unit/test_operational_log_hygiene.py  + \n  tests/unit/test_observability_contract_freeze.py  + \n  tests/unit/test_logging_redaction.py . \n Any future change to these behaviors MUST update those tests in the same \n commit (test-first rule: a new repetitive runtime event needs an \n aggregation/transition/rate-limit test before merge). \n Companion tooling:  src/nexus_scalp/observability/event_aggregator.py  \n (EventBatchAggregator — bounded, thread-safe, first-occurrence-immediate). \n \n Core invariants (all events) \n \n SEVERITY ladder: DEBUG = diagnostic detail; INFO = normal state / bounded \n \n informational transitions; WARNING = first failure or actionable \n"}, {"u": "/ar/architecture/observability-map/", "t": "Observability Map — Nexus Scalp Engine (NSE) [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  البنية  /  observability map  \n Observability Map — Nexus Scalp Engine (NSE) \n  TASK-OBS-AUDIT (2026-08-31, HEAD baseline 1f60832; delivered at dcc80d7).  Agent: Hermes-ObsForensic. AUDIT-ONLY: zero runtime code changed.  Machine-readable companion:  artifacts/forensics/observability-audit.json .  Method: black-box reconstruction from runtime evidence (logs / DBs / artifacts /  live API / CLI) FIRST, then targeted read-only code sweeps for every claim.  Evidence markers: [L]=live-probed today, [DB]=DB census, [LOG]=log sample, [C]=code file:line.  \n 1. What the system actually produces today \n  \n   Channel  Reality (verified)    \n  Logs  severity-split  logs/{critical,error,warning,info}/YYYY/MM/*.log , ISO-8601  +03:30 , 10 MB part rotation, retention 30/30/90/365 d [C observability/logging.py:388-394]. Only 08-29 + 08-31 exist; 08-30 absent. ~190 MB on 08-31 (131 MB error).  \n  Log r"}, {"u": "/ar/architecture/observability/", "t": "Observability [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  البنية  /  قابلية المراقبة  \n Observability \n NSE treats observability as a subsystem with contracts, not a logging afterthought. \n If the engine cannot show  why  it did something, its behavior is indistinguishable \n from a bug — so showing why is engineered, not hoped for. \n Structured logging ( observability/logging.py ) \n \n Severity-split, date-organized storage:  logs/&lt;sev&gt;/YYYY/MM/YYYY-MM-DD.log . \n ISO-8601 timestamps (broker-local offset aware), event/component/category/ \n \n error-code fields, correlation context. \n \n Daily + size rotation with zero-loss part files; per-severity retention. \n Key + high-entropy redaction; ANSI-free stacks. \n \n Incident response ( incidents/ ) \n Canonical incident model ( INC-YYYY-hex8 , 8 statuses, 5 severities), \n fingerprint correlation, causal-chain timeline reconstruction, value lineage \n with first-divergence location, WHY workflows, "}, {"u": "/ar/architecture/order_manager_architecture/", "t": "ORDER_MANAGER.PY — Architectural Map (Agent-5, Phase A) [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  البنية  /  order manager architecture  \n ORDER_MANAGER.PY — Architectural Map (Agent-5, Phase A) \n Evidence base: forensic inventory at HEAD  0015608  (post Agent-4 winner-protection \n sprint  0839da3 ). No edits made during this phase. This document precedes any \n extraction (task brief §24). \n 1. Current shape \n 6372 LOC, 1 god class + 6 support types \n  \n   Item  Span  Notes    \n  Module constants (18)  L60-155  exposure caps, BE/giveback/trailing geometry  \n  ExitMechanism (Enum)  L158  exit taxonomy  \n  PositionState (Enum)  L172  11 in-trade lifecycles  \n  PositionEvaluationStep  L190  trajectory step record  \n  LSFTicketState  L209  LSF per-ticket state  \n  PositionProtectionState  L226  per-ticket protection facts (dataclass)  \n  SmartPositionMetrics  L281  57 derived metrics (dataclass)  \n  OrderLifecycleManager  L348-6372  81 methods, 99 distinct  self.*  state attrs  \n   \n 2"}, {"u": "/ar/architecture/overview/", "t": "Architecture Overview [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  البنية  /  نظرة عامة  \n NSE بنيته  سداسية (Ports-and-Adapters) ومدفوعة بالأحداث : منصات الوسطاء والنماذج ومحوّلات الشبكة خلف عقود المنافذ ( IMT5Port ،  IGatewayPort )؛ النطاق لا يعرف أبدًا أي وسيط متصل. \n  ⧉   بيانات السوق (MT5 / ZMQ / paper)\n  → خصائص سببية — قاعدة 50D (scalp_v1) · تجميع 70D خاضع للحوكمة\n  → مدقق الاستدلال — بصمة المخطط · بُعد المقياس · الحدود (رفض صاخب)\n  → ScalpNet (TCN + انتباه ذاتي) — 4 logits → بوابة الثقة\n  → حارس النظام السعري → مصفوفة سياسات SMC (~30 قاعدة)\n  → محرك المخاطر (حجم كِيلي · هامش ≤20% · سقوف الفئات · HARD_MAX_LOTS=10)\n  → OrderManager (موجّه 60-سيناريو · 11 حالة مركز · تفكيك ذري)\n  → محوّل IMT5Port → MT5 / paper / shadow (صفر صلاحية أوامر)\n  → المحاسبة (SQLite WAL غير قابل للتغيير) → الخبرة والتشريح\n  → قابلية المراقبة (سجلات · حوادث · جنائي) + مركز التحكم (REST/SSE/WS)   \n الطبقات \n  \n   الطبقة  المسؤولية  الحد الصارم    \n  النطاق  عقود Pydantic م"}, {"u": "/ar/architecture/qa-assurance-contract/", "t": "QA ASSURANCE CONTRACT — Deep Assurance Layer (CHG-0045) [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  البنية  /  qa assurance contract  \n QA ASSURANCE CONTRACT — Deep Assurance Layer (CHG-0045) \n  Owner: Nexus-Main (TASK-QA-DEEP-ASSURANCE). This document is the contract  for the OSS-grade adversarial QA layer: lanes, markers, budgets, the JSON  result schema, and the governance rules for flaky/open-defect tests.  \n 1. Position in the gate hierarchy \n  \n   Lane  Command  When  Budget    \n  Pre-push critical gate (existing, NOT replaced)   beforePush.sh  /  check_local.py   every push  ~2.5 min  \n   Deep assurance — fast    python scripts/qa/deep_assurance.py --fast   PR / push lane in CI  &lt; 60 s  \n   Deep assurance — full    python scripts/qa/deep_assurance.py   main / scheduled / dispatch  &lt; 5 min  \n  Mutation proof   python scripts/qa/run_mutations.py   scheduled / dispatch (weekly)  &lt; 15 min  \n   \n The deep-assurance layer NEVER replaces the runtime gate; it adds \n independe"}, {"u": "/ar/architecture/QA_BLIND_SPOT_MATRIX/", "t": "QA BLIND-SPOT MATRIX — Nexus Scalp Engine [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  البنية  /  QA BLIND SPOT MATRIX  \n QA BLIND-SPOT MATRIX — Nexus Scalp Engine \n  CHG-0045 / TASK-QA-DEEP-ASSURANCE (Nexus-Main, 2026-09-02).  Required first milestone of the OSS-grade adversarial QA brief: prove which  gaps matter BEFORE building test mass. Derived from  agents/bugs.md   (BUG-001..BUG-208) and  agents/change_control.md  (CHG-0001..CHG-0050).  \n 1. Method \n \n  Defect-history mining  — every BUG/CHG row classified by subsystem, \n \n severity (P0 money/execution · P1 decision-path/trust · P2 operator \n trust/diagnostics · P3 robustness), and named regression test. \n \n  Detection-quality audit  — does the named regression test the ROOT \n \n CAUSE or only the incident's symptom path? \n \n  Re-entry analysis  — can the same class return through another door? \n  Verdict  — KEEP / IMPROVE / MERGE / DELETE / MISSING per test family. \n \n 2. Matrix — defect history → detection → gap "}, {"u": "/ar/architecture/repository-hygiene/", "t": "Repository Hygiene Audit — Nexus Scalp Engine [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  البنية  /  repository hygiene  \n Repository Hygiene Audit — Nexus Scalp Engine \n   Date:  2026-08-31 ·  HEAD:   1f60832  (main) ·  Working tree:  UNCHANGED (0 modifications)   Mode:  READ-ONLY forensic librarian pass. Nothing was fixed, moved, deleted, or refactored.   Machine-readable twin:   artifacts/forensics/repository-hygiene-audit.json    2026-08-31 repair pass:  CLEANUP-001/002/003/004/005/006 repaired — networkx declared as runtime dep, psycopg declared via new  postgres  extra, requirements ranges reconciled to pyproject, skill.md runner path fixed, tick_storage.py removed, 32 e2e_cc files archived to  scratch/e2e_cc_archive/ , .pyproj.bak removed.   Scope guard:  excludes all active-agent work (BUG-166..174, anti-crash, decomposition, release).  \n 1. What was analyzed \n \n 1,621 tracked files (724 py / 625 md / 80 json / 22 js / 16 mjs / 15 ps1 / 10 yml) \n 351 Python source f"}, {"u": "/ar/architecture/research-stack/", "t": "Research Stack [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  البنية  /  منظومة البحث  \n Research Stack \n The research side answers one question with evidence: **is this candidate good \n enough to trust — and can we prove it on data it never saw?** \n Pipeline \n  ⧉   DATA (canonical tick/bar datasets, provenance-fingerprinted)\n  → FEATURES (same causal contract as live: 50D base, governed 70D assembly)\n  → LABELING (triple-barrier, purged + embargoed)\n  → TRAINING (deterministic seeds, walk-forward)\n  → BACKTEST (friction-aware: spread / slippage / latency)\n  → WALK-FORWARD VALIDATION\n  → OOS GATE (hard: failure ⇒ REJECTED)\n  → ROBUSTNESS STRESS\n  → COUNTERFACTUAL / STRATIFICATION EVIDENCE\n  → CANDIDATE REGISTRY (content-addressed)\n  → SHADOW COMPARISON (zero order authority)\n  → OPERATOR-GATED PROMOTION   \n Key guarantees \n \n  Leakage prevention (INV-008):  purged + embargoed walk-forward \n \n (Lopez de Prado); broker history REPLACE+ALIGN; liquid"}, {"u": "/ar/architecture/runtime-certification-gate/", "t": "Runtime Certification Gate — canonical pre-push contract [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  البنية  /  runtime certification gate  \n Runtime Certification Gate — canonical pre-push contract \n   CHANGE-ID:  CHG-0051 ·  TASK-ID:  TASK-RUNTIME-GATE ·  Status:  ACTIVE   One command. One answer.   python scripts/ci/runtime_gate.py   \n 1. Purpose \n The repository has many test families (runtime, features, 50D/70D, models, \n database, execution, providers, research, CLI, observability, installer, \n integration). The problem was never test count — it was the absence of ONE \n strong, trustworthy, repeatable command answering: \n  \"Is the composed runtime safe, coherent, loadable, and operational enough  for an agent to push its change?\"  \n The Runtime Certification Gate is that command. It is a **curated, layered \n certification of the REAL composed runtime** — not \"run all pytest\". It \n exercises the actual boot path (config → adapter →  LiveEngine  service \n graph → decision pipeline"}, {"u": "/ar/architecture/runtime/", "t": "Runtime — the LiveEngine Loop [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  البنية  /  وقت التشغيل  \n Runtime — the LiveEngine loop \n  application/live_engine.py  is the orchestrator: a single async event loop \n that drives the tick pipeline and coordinates background workers. \n Startup sequence \n \n Launcher binds an adapter ( DirectMT5Adapter  /  RemoteMT5GatewayAdapter  / \n \n paper) behind  IMT5Port . \n \n Pre-flight  doctor gate : MT5 terminal present? config valid? platform \n \n supported? — otherwise the engine refuses to start. \n \n Migration gate: canonical DB migration engine runs (additive, checksummed). \n Model load: Champion bundle validated by the  10-gate load gate  (manifest \n \n hash, scaler dim, schema family, width contract…). \n \n Mode select:  PAPER (default)  / SHADOW / LIVE (interactive confirmation). \n Web server: FastAPI Control Center + SSE + WebSocket. \n Workers start (audit writer, research, hygiene, incidents, Telegram). \n \n Tick pipeline"}, {"u": "/ar/architecture/system-map/", "t": "System Map [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  البنية  /  خريطة النظام  \n System Map \n Package inventory ( src/nexus_scalp/ ) \n  ⧉   nexus_scalp/\n├── domain/            frozen Pydantic contracts (TickData, TradeProposal, …)\n├── ports/             IMT5Port · IGatewayPort        ← the hexagon seam\n├── adapters/          mt5/ (Win32 IPC) · gateway (ZMQ) · paper/ · database/ (AuditRepository, WAL)\n├── features/          scalp_features (50D) · schema registry · schema_contract (70D SSoT)\n│                      liquidity_engine · regime_classifier · temporal (research)\n├── models/            ScalpNet (dual-path TCN + self-attention)\n├── training/          walk_forward_trainer · labeling/ (triple-barrier)\n├── signals/           policy · rule matrix (~30 SMC rules)\n├── strategies/        factory (+ provider_gate for LLM/AI services)\n├── risk/              RiskEngine (Kelly sizing, clamps, kill switch)\n├── execution/         order_manager ("}, {"u": "/ar/contributing/add-language/", "t": "Adding a Language [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  المساهمة  /  إضافة لغة  \n Adding a Language \n The multilingual architecture is data-driven: adding Turkish, French, Russian, \n Chinese or Japanese is a directory + registry entry — no code changes. \n Recipe \n \n  Create the language tree  \n \n  ⧉      site/content/&lt;lang&gt;/            # translated site content (mirror of en tree)\n   docs/&lt;lang&gt;/index.md            # optional docs-root landing page   \n \n  Register the language  in  scripts/docs/site_config.py : \n \n  ⧉      LANGUAGES = {\n       &quot;en&quot;: {&quot;name&quot;: &quot;English&quot;, &quot;dir&quot;: &quot;ltr&quot;},\n       &quot;fa&quot;: {&quot;name&quot;: &quot;فارسی&quot;,   &quot;dir&quot;: &quot;rtl&quot;},\n       ...\n       &quot;tr&quot;: {&quot;name&quot;: &quot;Türkçe&quot;,  &quot;dir&quot;: &quot;ltr&quot;},   # ← new\n   }   \n \n  Translate core pages first  (in priority order): \n \n  index  →  getting-"}, {"u": "/ar/contributing/contribution-guide/", "t": "Contribution Guide [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  المساهمة  /  دليل المساهمة  \n يطور هذا المستودع وكلاء منسقون بموجب عقد هندسي صارم؛ ويستفيد المساهمون البشر من الانضباط نفسه. \n التهيئة \n  ⧉   git clone https://github.com/Opselon/NexusTradingForexBot.git\ncd NexusTradingForexBot\npython -m venv .venv &amp;&amp; .\\.venv\\Scripts\\Activate.ps1\npip install -e .[dev]\npytest tests/unit -q   \n انضباط التغيير \n \n  اقرأ الذاكرة الهندسية أولاً :  \">https://github.com/Opselon/NexusTradingForexBot/blob/main/agents/skill.md\">  agents/skill.md   (خريطة البنية)،  \">https://github.com/Opselon/NexusTradingForexBot/blob/main/agents/runtime_invariants.md\">  agents/runtime_invariants.md  ،  \">https://github.com/Opselon/NexusTradingForexBot/blob/main/agents/bugs.md\">  agents/bugs.md  . \n  اطلب قبل أن تبرمج  — أضف صفًا إلى  agents/taskboard.md . \n  إعادة الاستخدام &gt; التوسيع &gt; إعادة الهيكلة &gt; الإنشاء ؛ ملفات المسار الساخن مقفلة بالاتفاق. \n  الكوميتات :"}, {"u": "/ar/contributing/documentation/", "t": "Documentation Workflow [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  المساهمة  /  سير عمل التوثيق  \n Documentation Workflow \n Ownership \n Documentation is owned by the  Nexus-Docs  role \n (registry:  docs/agent_handoffs/DOCS_REGISTRY.md ). The boundary is hard: \n docs changes never touch runtime code, and code owners never need to fix docs \n tooling. If documentation exposes a suspected code defect, it is recorded in \n the registry with subsystem attribution — the implementation stays untouched. \n Information architecture \n  ⧉   docs/            engineering documentation (markdown, this IA tree)\nsite/            GitHub Pages source (builds docs/ + translations into a static site)\nscripts/docs/    validation tooling (check_docs.py, check_translations.py, build_site.py)\n.github/workflows/docs.yml    docs CI + Pages deploy   \n Source of truth \n \n  English  is the source language; every other language is a translation \n \n with status metadata ( complete | p"}, {"u": "/ar/engineering/ci/", "t": "CI Architecture [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  الهندسة  /  بنية CI  \n CI Architecture \n Workflows \n  \n   Workflow  Trigger  Purpose    \n   ci.yml   push (main/develop/ci-tests), PR, weekly drift scan  ruff · format · mypy · pytest (critical; matrix arms for integration/e2e/research/model on demand)  \n   tests-os.yml   matrix OS runs  cross-platform unit sanity  \n   security.yml   PR + weekly schedule  CodeQL + Trivy  \n   osv-scanner.yml   schedule  dependency vulnerabilities  \n   lockfile-diff.yml   dependency file changes  lockfile drift  \n   js-tests.yml   Web/ changes   node --check  + JS tests  \n   release.yml    v*  tags  only   build + verify + publish release artifacts  \n   docker.yml   Docker surface changes  image build gates  \n   docs.yml   docs/site/README changes  documentation validation + Pages deploy (this platform)  \n   \n Trigger policy (CI_TRIGGER_POLICY v1): tags never fire CI (release-only), main \n pushes run the"}, {"u": "/ar/engineering/quality/", "t": "Quality & Testing [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  الهندسة  /  الجودة والاختبار  \n Quality &amp; Testing \n The quality gate \n Every push passes  beforePush.sh  /  beforePush.ps1  (5 stages): \n \n  ruff check  (lint) \n  ruff format  check \n  mypy src  \n  CRITICAL suite  pytest run ( tests/critical_suite.txt , ~779 tests, \n \n RAM-aware xdist workers, coverage) \n \n Forensic  deploy gate  writing  artifacts/forensics/deploy_gate_result.json  \n \n  -FullSuite  runs the whole ~1931-test unit corpus. CI mirrors the gate \n ( .github/workflows/ci.yml ) and adds CodeQL, Trivy, OSV, lockfile-diff and JS \n tests on separate workflows. \n Test architecture \n  \n   Suite  Location  Character    \n  Unit   tests/unit/   ~1900 tests; critical subset in  critical_suite.txt   \n  Integration   tests/integration/   API + engine-level, run standalone/sequential in CI  \n  Golden   tests/golden/  +  test_*_golden.py   byte/behavior-identical extraction gates (dec"}, {"u": "/ar/engineering/release-process/", "t": "Release Process [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  الهندسة  /  عملية الإصدار  \n Release Process \n Versioning \n Semver, single canonical source:  pyproject.toml  ( version = \"9.0.6\" ) \n stamped into every build artifact. The README never hard-codes a conflicting \n version — it defers to  nexus version  / the release metadata. \n Pipeline ( .github/workflows/release.yml ) \n Tag-triggered  only  ( v* ). Stages: \n \n Validate tag vs version metadata \n Run the critical test suite (a release run that fails the suite does not \n \n publish — see the v9.0.6 re-cut history in the taskboard) \n \n Build Windows x64 artifacts:  NexusScalpEngine-&lt;version&gt;-win-x64-setup.exe  \n \n + portable  .zip  (PyInstaller) \n \n Generate SHA-256 digests, release manifest, SBOM; embed manifest in the \n \n portable bundle \n \n Publish GitHub Release \n  Post-publish verification  ( release/verify.py ): checksums, manifest \n \n paths, embedded layout (BUG-160 lineage) \n"}, {"u": "/ar/engineering/security/", "t": "Security [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  الهندسة  /  الأمان  \n Security \n Secrets \n \n Secrets live in the  settings DB  / secret store — never in  live.yaml , \n \n never committed (INV-010). Provider URLs/keys are redacted in health \n endpoints and logs ( [REDACTED_SECRET] ). \n \n  scripts/ci/scan_secrets.py  fails CI on secret-shaped strings in \n \n source/config/docs. \n \n Diagnostics export ( nexus export-diagnostics ) is sanitized by contract — \n \n never contains secrets. \n Scanning (CI) \n CodeQL (SAST), Trivy (containers/FS), OSV dependency scanning, lockfile-diff, \n secret scan — see  CI architecture . \n Trust boundaries \n  \n   Boundary  Rule    \n  broker ↔ engine   IMT5Port  adapters only; account-identity fail-safe at connect  \n  research/learning ↔ execution  zero order authority (INV-002); shadow never mutates execution  \n  observability ↔ trading  incidents/forensics are diagnostic-only  \n  Telegram  read-only outbound"}, {"u": "/ar/getting-started/configuration/", "t": "Configuration [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  البداية  /  الإعداد  \n الإعداد \n للإعداد ثلاث طبقات بمرجعيات مختلفة. خلطها خطأ كلاسيكي — اقرأ هذه الصفحة قبل تحرير YAML يدويًا. \n 1.  AppConfig  (التهيئة / الاستيراد / التصدير) \n  src/nexus_scalp/configuration/config.py  — يحمّل عقد YAML ( configs/base.yaml  هو الأساس المرجعي؛ و configs/live.yaml.example  مثال بصيغة live). يُستخدم للتهيئة والاستيراد والتصدير فقط. \n 2. إعداد وقت التشغيل (الحالة الحية المرجعية) \n  RuntimeConfiguration  عبر  RuntimeConfigStore.get_snapshot()  هي  الحالة الحية المرجعية  — مُسنة الإصدار وقابلة لإعادة التحميل الساخن. على المستهلكين القراءة عبر  get_snapshot()  لا القيم المخبأة من المُنشئ. وتحدد وسوم النطاق متى يسري التغيير ( LIVE_IMMEDIATE  مقابل  NEXT_DECISION ). \n 3. قاعدة بيانات الإعدادات (الأسرار + نية المستخدم) \n بيانات الاعتماد (مثل تيليجرام) تُخزَّن في قاعدة بيانات الإعدادات عبر  settings_service.set_telegram()  —  أبدًا  في  live.yaml  ولا تُرفع للمس"}, {"u": "/ar/getting-started/first-run/", "t": "First-Run Safety [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  البداية  /  التشغيل الأول  \n التشغيل الأول — السلامة (تجريبي → SHADOW → LIVE) \n ينفّذ هذا المحرك أوامر على وسيط حقيقي. التوجيه الرسمي للمستودع سلّم صارم — لا تتجاوز أي خطوة. \n  \n   الخطوة  الإجراء  السبب    \n  ١️⃣  سجّل الدخول إلى  حساب تجريبي  في MT5 ( File → Open an Account → Practice/Demo ) وأكّد رقم/اسم الحساب قبل أي شيء  الحساب الحي والتجريبي يبدوان متطابقين في نافذة دخول MT5  \n  ٢️⃣  في MT5:  Tools → Options → Expert Advisors → فعّل \"Allow Algo Trading\"   بدونه تُرفض الأوامر  \n  ٣️⃣  انسخ  configs/live.yaml  إلى  configs/demo.yaml ؛ أدخل بيانات الحساب التجريبي؛ أكّد  risk.max_concurrent_positions: 1  و  risk.risk_per_trade_pct  (مثل 0.5) و  risk.max_account_drawdown_pct   لا تلمس إعدادًا حيًا بينما المال الحقيقي في المتناول  \n  ٤️⃣  شغّل  SHADOW  أولًا ( nexus start --mode shadow ) لعدة أيام؛ راقب لوحة التحكم وتقارير تيليجرام  يثبت النموذج والإشارات والبوابات قبل أي تنفيذ  \n  ٥️⃣"}, {"u": "/ar/getting-started/installation/", "t": "Installation [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  البداية  /  التثبيت  \n محرك Nexus Scalp هو  منصة تداول كمي قائمة على البحث : نظام تشغيل سداسي (Hexagonal) مدفوع بالأحداث لميتاتريدر 5 (السوق الأساسي: الذهب XAUUSD على فريم M1) يربط بيانات السوق، وهندسة الخصائص السببية، واستدلال النماذج، وسياسة الاستراتيجية، وضبط المخاطر، وإعادة التشغيل (Replay)، والتنفيذ، وقابلية المراقبة، والتحقق القابل لإعادة الإنتاج في خط أنابيب واحد قابل للتدقيق. \n &lt;div class=\"callout\"&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ليس وعدًا بالربح.&lt;/strong&gt; هذه منصة بحث وهندسة. الحالات تُدرَّج وفق الأدلة، والنتائج السلبية تُنشر — بما في ذلك رفض مرشحنا البحثي 70D استنادًا إلى أدلة خارج العينة. التداول بالرافعة على أطراف قصيرة يحمل مخاطر مالية بالغة.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt; \n ما الذي يجعله مختلفًا \n \n  الأدلة قبل الادعاءات  — المقاييس بلا أدلة تظهر  n/a ، وليس أصفارًا مزيفة أبدًا. \n  بلا نظرة مستقبلية  — Walk-Forward مع Purge و Embargo، وخصائص سببية صارمة (INV-008). \n  التكافؤ ال"}, {"u": "/ar/getting-started/quickstart/", "t": "Quickstart [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  البداية  /  البداية السريعة  \n البداية السريعة \n  ⧉   # 1. التثبيت (المطورون، من المصدر)\ngit clone https://github.com/Opselon/NexusTradingForexBot.git\ncd NexusTradingForexBot\npython -m venv .venv &amp;&amp; .\\.venv\\Scripts\\Activate.ps1   # لينكس: source .venv/bin/activate\npip install -e .[dev]\n\n# 2. فحص النظام\nnexus doctor          # تشخيص للقراءة فقط في 19 فئة + إصلاحات مقترحة\nnexus health          # READY / DEGRADED / NOT READY\n\n# 3. التشغيل — PAPER افتراضياً، لا LIVE بصمت أبداً\nnexus start           # محاكاة، مركز التحكم على http://127.0.0.1:8080\n\n# 4. التقييم على بيانات حقيقية مع صفر سلطة أوامر\nnexus start --mode shadow\n\n# 5. الإيقاف\nnexus stop            # لوضع --daemon؛ أو Ctrl+C في المقدمة   \n الأوضاع \n  \n   الوضع  البيانات  الأوامر  الاستخدام    \n   paper  (افتراضي)  محاكاة  محاكاة  أول تشغيل، الواجهة، التطوير  \n   shadow   حقيقية   لا شيء — صفر سلطة  ( simulated=True )  تقييم "}, {"u": "/ar/guides/api/", "t": "API Reference [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  أدلة  /  مرجع API  \n API Reference \n The Control Center backend is a FastAPI application exposing * 203  /api/   \n endpoints across 22 groups** (verified by scanning the route modules in \n  src/nexus_scalp/web/ ), plus Server-Sent Events for ticks and WebSocket for \n the dashboard. Everything the UI does, the API does — the UI is a consumer of \n the same surface. \n  ملاحظة  Endpoint counts are generated from the repository's actual route decorators —  they drift with the code, and the docs doctor flags stale counts.  \n Discovery \n \n  Health / readiness:   GET /health  →  200  with  READY / DEGRADED ,  503  when NOT READY. \n  Engine state:   GET /api/status  and  GET /api/live/state  (the dashboard heart, includes the effective serving contract). \n  OpenAPI:  the FastAPI app serves its schema at  /openapi.json  and Swagger UI at  /docs  on the same port as the UI (  http://127.0.0.1:808"}, {"u": "/ar/guides/cli/", "t": "CLI Guide [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  أدلة  /  دليل CLI  \n CLI Guide \n  nexus  is the application command (installation lifecycle lives in \n  install.ps1 ; everything you  operate  lives in  nexus ). From source: \n  python -m nexus_scalp.cli.main  (alias  nse ). \n Commands \n  ⧉   nexus help            # same authoritative surface as --help (+ &#x27;nexus help start&#x27;)\nnexus version         # build identity (--json / --plain)\nnexus doctor          # read-only diagnostics (19 categories) + suggested fixes\nnexus status          # health + environment + version\nnexus health          # quick health summary (READY / DEGRADED / NOT READY)\nnexus config          # inspect/validate active configuration (secrets masked)\nnexus start           # PAPER mode by default — never LIVE silently\nnexus stop / restart  # control the background engine (honest dead-pid reporting)\nnexus logs [--tail N] [--errors]\nnexus test --mode quick|unit|i"}, {"u": "/ar/guides/common-workflows/", "t": "Common Workflows [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  أدلة  /  سير العمل الشائعة  \n Common Workflows \n 1. Daily development loop \n  ⧉   git pull &amp;&amp; .venv/Scripts/Activate.ps1        # Windows dev\nnexus test --mode quick                        # fast sanity\n# ... edit ...\npytest tests/unit -q -k &quot;70 or schema&quot;         # targeted suite\n./beforePush.ps1 -SkipPush                     # full gate before pushing   \n 2. Evaluate the engine on real data (risk-free) \n  ⧉   nexus start --mode shadow      # live feed, zero order authority\n# observe Control Center → SHADOW section: disagreement analysis, drift, health\nnexus stop   \n 3. Research a candidate \n  ⧉   nexus model-dataset-build      # canonical dataset (fingerprinted)\nnexus model-experiment-create  # fair A/B/C protocol\nnexus model-train              # deterministic, seeded\nnexus model-validate           # walk-forward + OOS gate + robustness\nnexus model-replay           "}, {"u": "/ar/guides/troubleshooting/", "t": "Troubleshooting [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  أدلة  /  استكشاف الأخطاء  \n Troubleshooting \n  Rule of thumb:  nexus doctor  first — it reports 19 diagnostic categories  with suggested fixes and is the same gate the engine runs pre-launch.  \n Engine refuses to start \n  \n   Symptom  Likely cause  Action    \n  \"MT5 terminal missing/not running\"  terminal closed / not installed  start MT5, log in (demo first), retry  \n  config validation error  YAML contract violation   nexus config --validate &lt;path&gt; ; fix the named key  \n  environment blocked (exit 3)  Windows ARM64  unsupported by dependency stack; use x64  \n  migration gate failure  schema drift   nexus db migrate ; check  nexus db hygiene status   \n   \n UI / dashboard \n  \n   Symptom  Likely cause  Action    \n  dashboard unreachable  port drift (dev UI/API ports can move)  check  nexus status  output / launcher log for the bound port  \n  \"Cannot GET /\" on some port  wrong port"}, {"u": "/ar/docs-hub/", "t": "Nexus Scalp Engine — Documentation [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  مركز التوثيق  \n Nexus Scalp Engine — Documentation \n  Research-driven quantitative trading platform  — a hexagonal, event-driven \n scalping engine for MetaTrader 5 (primary market: XAUUSD M1), built around \n causal feature engineering, artifact-first model governance, deterministic \n research tooling, and forensic observability. \n  مهم  This documentation describes a  research and engineering platform . It is  not investment advice, and nothing here is a promise of profitability.  Leveraged scalping carries extreme financial risk. See   Project Status  for what is certified vs experimental.  \n Start here \n  \n   Question  Page    \n  What is Nexus and why does it exist?   Vision   \n  How do I run it?   Quickstart   \n  How is the architecture structured?   Architecture Overview   \n  How does data become a decision?   Data Flow   \n  How is research validated?   Research Methodology   \n  Wh"}, {"u": "/ar/project/capabilities/", "t": "Capability Matrix [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  المشروع  /  مصفوفة القدرات  \n Capability Matrix \n Legend: ✅ Certified · 🟢 Implemented · 🟡 Experimental · 🔵 Research · 🚧 In \n progress · 📌 Planned · ⚪ Not verified \n  \n   Capability  Status  Evidence (repository)  Notes    \n  Causal 50D feature engine ( scalp_v1 )  ✅ Certified   features/scalp_features.py , schema registry, golden/parity tests  live contract; NaN/Inf deterministic fallback  \n  70D canonical contract ( scalp_v3 )  🟢 Implemented (research)   features/schema_contract.py  SSoT, hash, inference validator (10 rejection codes)  candidate-only; negative OOS evidence so far  \n  Liquidity intelligence (10D block)  🟡 Experimental   features/liquidity_engine.py , INV-019 causality rules  research series; governed by  liquidity_features_enabled   \n  News intelligence 10D + bounded gate  🟡 Experimental   news/ , gate bounds boost ≤0.05 / penalty ≤0.10  opt-in, disabled by default; ca"}, {"u": "/ar/project/milestones/", "t": "Milestones & Project Story [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  المشروع  /  المحطات  \n Milestones — the project story \n This is a factual history reconstructed from the repository's own records \n (taskboard, decision records, forensic reports). No invented narrative. \n Phase I — Engine core (single-agent era) \n The original engine: hexagonal architecture, MT5 adapters, 50D causal features, \n ScalpNet, policy matrix, risk engine, order manager, SQLite WAL ledger, \n FastAPI Control Center. Foundation invariants established: no sync DB on the \n tick path, no order authority for learning components. \n Phase II — Multi-agent forensic era \n Development moved to a  multi-agent model  (up to 56+ parallel AI agents) with \n a strict engineering contract: taskboard, locks, bug ledger, runtime invariants, \n change control. The bug ledger (BUG-001…) and forensic acceptance reports date \n from this era. Key products: database hygiene, migrations, incident respon"}, {"u": "/ar/project/roadmap/", "t": "Roadmap [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  المشروع  /  خارطة الطريق  \n انضباط الصياغة: البنود «مخطط»، «تحت التقييم»، «اتجاه بحثي» أو «مكتمل» — أبدًا «قريبًا»، وأبدًا مضمونًا. \n الآن (نشط) \n  \n   التدفق  البند  الحالة    \n  التحقق  إعادة بناء أدلة مرشح 70D (دلالات الثقة المصححة، CHG-0042)  تحت التقييم  \n  البحث  تعميق أدلة المضاد للواقع (CHG-0041)  جارٍ  \n  البنية  تفكيك الملفات الكبيرة باختبارات ذهبية (CHG-0032-A1)  جارٍ  \n  وقت التشغيل  تحصين عقد باني السجلات (BUG-185)  مكتمل  \n   \n التالي \n  \n   التدفق  البند  التبعيات    \n  ML  قرار ترقية 70D — بقرار المشغّل، أو تقاعد صادق  مرشح متحقق + تحقق 14-بوابة  \n  التحقق  مراجعة سياسة قائمة على المضاد للواقع  مخرجات المضاد للواقع  \n  الوثائق  تغطية ترجمة 100% للصفحات الأساسية  سير عمل الترجمة  \n  قابلية المراقبة  سد فجوات OBS-001..016  أدلة التدقيق  \n   \n لاحقًا (اتجاهات بحثية) \n مرشح ترقية السيولة الزمنية ( scalp_v4_temporal_candidate ) · دمج MSLIE في السياسة · اختيار النموذج المشروط"}, {"u": "/ar/project/scope/", "t": "Scope [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  المشروع  /  النطاق  \n Scope \n In scope \n \n A complete quantitative trading  pipeline : data adapters (MT5/paper/gateway), \n \n causal feature engineering (50D active contract; 60D/70D research family), \n deep model inference (ScalpNet TCN + self-attention), SMC policy matrix, \n invariant risk engine, execution with 60-scenario router, SQLite WAL \n accounting ledger, experience/autopsy intelligence, research &amp; validation \n (walk-forward, OOS gate, robustness), replay and shadow runtimes, model \n governance, observability (structured logs, incidents, forensics, Telegram), \n FastAPI Control Center UI, packaged Windows release + installer + update/rollback. \n \n  Multi-agent engineering memory : architecture map, bug ledger, runtime \n \n invariants, contracts, taskboard, decision records — treated as first-class \n repository artifacts. \n Out of scope (by design) \n \n Multi-broker support b"}, {"u": "/ar/project/status/", "t": "Project Status [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  المشروع  /  حالة المشروع  \n حالة المشروع \n  مهم  تُدرَّج الحالات بالأدلة. «مُنفّذ» = موجود في الكود ومغطى بالاختبارات.  «مُصادق» = إضافةً بقبول جنائي رسمي. لا وعود ربحية هنا.  \n لمحة \n  \n   البعد  الحالة  الأدلة    \n  الإصدار   9.0.6  (semver، مصدر وحيد  pyproject.toml )  خط أنابيب الإصدار  \n  الإصدارات   منشورة  (وسوم v9.0.0 إلى v9.0.6؛ SHA-256، بيان، SBOM)  GitHub Releases  \n  وقت التشغيل  مُتين؛ PAPER افتراضياً؛ LIVE بتأكيد صريح  عقد CLI + الفحص المسبق  \n  التنفيذ الحي  يعمل (MT5 Win32 IPC + بوابة ZMQ) مع fail-safe مطابقة الحساب  انحدار BUG-142  \n  حلقة البحث  من طرف إلى طرف (مجموعات بيانات ← walk-forward ← بوابة OOS)  اختبارات research/  \n  العقد الحي 50D ( scalp_v1 )   نشط    features/schema.py   \n  عقد 70D ( scalp_v3 )  مرجع البحث (SSoT)؛  مرشّح فقط    features/schema_contract.py   \n  أدلة 70D حتى اليوم  walk-forward وظل على بيانات حقيقية  سلبية / غير حاسمة  (OOS NOT_ELIGIBLE)  ت"}, {"u": "/ar/project/vision/", "t": "Vision & Why [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  المشروع  /  الرؤية والغاية  \n الرؤية — لماذا نكسوس؟ \n المشكلة \n تُخفق مشاريع التداول الخوارزمي عادةً بإحدى طريقتين: \n \n  تُخفي الحقيقة.  مقاييس مفبركة، إخفاقات صامتة، والفجوة بين الاختبار \n \n التاريخي والتشغيل الفعلي لا تُقاس أبداً. \n \n  تسرّب المستقبل.  الخصائص أو الملصقات تستخدم معلومات لم تكن متاحة لحظة \n \n القرار — نتائج غير صالحة بنيوياً مهما بدت جيدة. \n بُني محرك نكسوس ضد كلا الفشلين:  خط أنابيب كامل قابل التدقيق  — بيانات \n السوق ← الخصائص ← النموذج ← السياسة ← المخاطر ← التنفيذ ← المحاسبة ← \n البحث — حيث كل مرحلة قابلة للرصد، وكل هوية مُسجَّمة ببصمة، وكل ادعاء قابل \n للدحض. \n الفلسفة (مدعومة بالمستودع) \n \n  الأدلة قبل الادعاءات.  المقاييس بلا أدلة تُعرض  n/a  — أبداً أصفاراً \n \n مفبركة. \n \n  لا إطلالة للمستقبل.  walk-forward مع purge و embargo، خصائص سببية صارمة \n \n (INV-008). \n \n  التكافؤ السببي.  live = replay = التدريب؛ عقد الخصائص نفسه مع بصمة \n \n المخطط. \n \n  حقيقة وقت الت"}, {"u": "/ar/reference/cli-reference/", "t": "CLI Reference [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  مرجع  /  مرجع CLI  \n CLI Reference \n The authoritative surface is always  nexus help  /  nexus &lt;command&gt; --help  \n (this page documents the verified contract; the CLI is golden-tested by 66 \n end-to-end tests). \n Global flags \n  \n   Flag  Effect    \n   --json   machine-readable output (parity-tested keys)  \n   --plain   no color, no formatting  \n   --no-color   disable color only  \n   \n Command groups \n  \n   Command  Purpose  Notes    \n  `nexus start [--mode paper\\  shadow\\  live] [--port N] [--daemon]`  run engine  paper default; live needs interactive  --yes /confirmation; port default 8080  \n   nexus stop  /  nexus restart   daemon control  pidfile-based; dead-pid reported honestly (BUG-172)  \n   nexus doctor   19-category diagnostics + suggested fixes   --json  for tooling  \n   nexus status  /  nexus health   environment + health  READY / DEGRADED / NOT READY  \n   nexus confi"}, {"u": "/ar/reference/faq/", "t": "FAQ [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  مرجع  /  الأسئلة الشائعة  \n الأسئلة الشائعة \n  ما هو Nexus؟  \n منصة تداول كمي قائمة على البحث: محرك تداول سداسي مدفوع بالأحداث لميتاتريدر 5 (XAUUSD M1) بخصائص سببية ونماذج عميقة ومخاطر ثابتة وبحث حتمي وقابلية مراقبة جنائية. \n  هل هذا روبوت تداول حي؟  \n يمكنه تنفيذ صفقات حية — لكن PAPER هو الافتراضي، وSHADOW بلا صلاحية أوامر، وLIVE يتطلب تأكيدًا تفاعليًا صريحًا، والمستودع ينشر المرشحين المرفوضين. إنها منصة بحث بنظام تشغيل، وليست آلة نقود. \n  هل أستطيع تشغيله بدون MT5؟  \n نعم — وضع PAPER ومجموعة الاختبارات كاملة تعملان بدون وسيط؛ وDocker يعمل جاهزًا بوضع PAPER. \n  ما هو 70D؟  \n عقد الخصائص البحثي المعياري (50 قاعدة + 10 أخبار + 10 سيولة). ليس حيًا — العقد الحي هو 50D. مرشح 70D مرفوض حتى الآن وفق أدلة OOS. \n  كيف يُمنع التسريب؟  \n Walk-Forward منقّى ومحجور، خصائص سببية صارمة، معالجة REPLACE+ALIGN للتاريخ، اختبارات إعادة تشغيل مطابقة بت-بت، وتسجيل قيم التطهير/الحجر الفعلية لكل تشغيل. \n  كي"}, {"u": "/ar/reference/glossary/", "t": "Glossary [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  مرجع  /  المسرد  \n Glossary \n Project-specific terms. Product/module names (Nexus, ScalpNet, OrderManager, \n MT5, 70D, 50D) are canonical and never translated in code; each language's \n  terminology file  defines how they are presented. \n  \n   Term  Meaning in NSE    \n   50D / scalp_v1   the 50-dimensional causal base feature contract — the ACTIVE live feature schema  \n   70D / scalp_v3   the canonical research feature contract: Base 50 (0..49) + News 10 (50..59) + Liquidity 10 (60..69); candidate-only, not live  \n   scalp_v4   a candidate 70D-family contract (integration-era); classified LEGACY/semantically-different vs v3  \n   Schema hash   SHA-256 over canonical JSON of feature (index, name, family) — reordering invalidates models  \n   ScalpNet   dual-path model: 2D MLP for single-tick snapshots, 3D TCN + self-attention for sequences; 4-logit head  \n   Champion / Challenger   produc"}, {"u": "/ar/reference/terminology/", "t": "Terminology & Translations [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  مرجع  /  المصطلحات والترجمات  \n Terminology &amp; Translations \n Untranslatable canon \n These stay in English/Latin script in every language (identifiers, contracts, \n product names): \n `Nexus · ScalpNet · OrderManager · RiskEngine · LiveEngine · IMT5Port · \n AuditRepository · MT5 · ZMQ · SQLite · FastAPI · 50D · 70D · scalp_v1 · \n scalp_v3 · NO_TRADE · BUY · SELL · WAIT · Champion · Challenger · Shadow · \n OOS · walk-forward · O(1) · MFE · MAE` \n Canonical term translations \n The authoritative per-language table lives in \n  site/terminology/&lt;lang&gt;.json  (consumed by the translation audit). Core \n entries: \n  \n   EN  FA (فارسی)  ES  AR (العربية)  DE    \n  Feature Vector  بردار ویژگی  Vector de características  متجه السمات  Merkmalsvektor  \n  Feature Contract  قرارداد ویژگی  Contrato de características  عقد السمات  Merkmalsvertrag  \n  Model Registry  ثبت مدل  Registro de modelos  "}, {"u": "/ar/research/backtesting/", "t": "Backtesting [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  البحث  /  الاختبار الرجعي  \n Backtesting \n Determinism \n Backtests ( research/backtest.py ) are deterministic: fixed seeds, frozen \n datasets, no wall-clock dependence. Same inputs ⇒ same results. \n Friction model \n Spread, slippage and latency are modeled, not ignored: \n \n fills on historical bid/ask (direction-aware), \n tick-level SL/TP first-touch resolution, \n logical latency applied to the decision path, \n robustness stress re-runs under degraded friction (spread/slippage/latency \n \n shocks) — a strategy that only works under ideal fills does not pass. \n Boundary honesty \n \n Backtests produce evidence, not promises. Results feed the validation \n \n pipeline; they never bypass the OOS gate. \n \n Fees/commissions follow the configured friction profile; metrics without the \n \n underlying evidence render  n/a  — never fabricated zeros. \n \n Streaming replay ( research/streaming_replay.py"}, {"u": "/ar/research/counterfactuals/", "t": "Counterfactuals [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  البحث  /  المضاد للواقع  \n Counterfactuals (CHG-0041) \n The question \n Backtests score trades that happened. The counterfactual engine asks the \n other question: **what would have happened on the decisions the engine did NOT \n take?** If the engine abstains (NO_TRADE), was the abstention valuable? \n How it works \n  research/counterfactual.py : \n \n Loads canonical tick datasets (fingerprinted, offline) and decision \n \n snapshots from  audit_signals . \n \n Joins each NO_TRADE decision to the tick window at decision time. \n Applies  certified fill semantics  hypothetically at time T. \n Walks ticks forward to compute MFE / MAE / R / cost / time-to-target. \n Classifies each abstention using  documented rules  (never ad-hoc). \n Stratifies evidence by gate, regime, confidence, session, direction. \n \n First evidence run (2026-09-01) \n 2095 NO_TRADE decisions (2026-08-24 → 09-01) walked over 3.2"}, {"u": "/ar/research/datasets/", "t": "Datasets [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  البحث  /  مجموعات البيانات  \n Datasets \n Bar datasets \n Built by  research/dataset.py  +  model_generation/  with quality gates \n (coverage, ordering, duplicates, horizon boundaries). Each dataset is a \n versioned artifact with a fingerprint ( ds_*  id) used in manifests and run \n snapshots. \n Tick datasets (CHG-0041 / TICK_DATASET_META v2) \n  research/mt5_tick_dataset.py  acquires ticks from the **certified adapter \n surface** ( copy_ticks_range ,  COPY_TICKS_ALL ), with: \n \n bounded, deduplicated acquisition (post BUG-188 semantics), \n immutable parquet store with  content fingerprints , \n provenance metadata v2 (symbol, window, source, acquisition identity), \n cache-hit idempotence — re-running acquisition never duplicates. \n \n After acquisition the dataset is fully  offline : research needs no broker. \n Rules \n \n A dataset is immutable once fingerprinted — corrections produce a new"}, {"u": "/ar/research/methodology/", "t": "Research Methodology [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  البحث  /  المنهجية  \n البحث موجود لإنتاج  أدلة قابلة للتكذيب . المرشح الذي لا يمكن تكذيبه (بلا OOS، بلا تكافؤ إعادة تشغيل، بلا مصدر) لا يلمس مسار الحي أبدًا. \n السلسلة \n  ⧉   بيانات (مجموعات ببصمة) → خصائص (عقد سببي) → وسم (حاجز ثلاثي)\n→ تدريب (ببذرة، حتمي) → اختبار رجعي (واعٍ بالاحتكاك)\n→ Walk-Forward (تطهير + حجر) → بوابة OOS (فشل ⇒ REJECTED)\n→ اختبار المتانة → مضاد للواقع → السجل → الظل → ترقية المشغّل   \n المكونات \n \n  مجموعات البيانات  — غير قابلة للتغيير، ببصمة، بمصدر متتبع؛ مجموعات التيك تُقتنى عبر سطح المحوّل المعتمد وتبقى دون اتصال بعد الاقتناء. \n  الاختبارات الرجعية  — حتمية؛ فروق الأسعار/الانزلاق/زمن التأخير تُنمذج. \n  إعادة التشغيل  — مطابقة بت-بت مع مجموعة البيانات (اختبارات مانعة للتسريب)؛ إعادة التشغيل المتدفقة تشغّل المحرك المشترك على ساعة منطقية بتعبئات محاكاة ومحظور بموجب اختبار استدعاء  order_send . \n  المضاد للواقع (CHG-0041)  — مشي قرارات NO_TRADE بتعبئات افتراضية:"}, {"u": "/ar/research/out-of-sample/", "t": "Out-of-Sample Gate [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  البحث  /  بوابة OOS  \n Out-of-Sample (OOS) Gate \n Contract \n  research/oos.py  is a  hard gate : out-of-sample failure ⇒ candidate \n REJECTED, regardless of in-sample performance. There is no override path in \n the pipeline. \n Floors (model lifecycle validation) \n  \n   Metric  Floor    \n  macro-F1 (OOS)  ≥ 0.34  \n  balanced accuracy  ≥ 0.34  \n  calibration error (ECE)  ≤ 0.15  \n  minimum evidence  ≥ 100 rows  \n   \n Evidence the gate bites \n The 70D liquidity candidate — the most heavily engineered research series in \n the repository — was rejected by this exact gate (OOS NOT_ELIGIBLE) after \n real-data walk-forward and shadow benchmarks came back negative/inconclusive. \n A gate that rejects nothing is decoration; this one has a public rejection on \n its record. See  Project Status  and \n  docs/TASK-05-70D-SHADOW-FINAL.md . \n Temporal OOS protocol \n Temporal splits only ( timestamp -ord"}, {"u": "/ar/research/replay/", "t": "Replay [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  البحث  /  إعادة التشغيل  \n Replay \n What replay is \n Replay re-runs the engine's decision logic over historical data and proves it \n produces  the same decisions  the live/training pipeline produced on that \n data. It is the execution-fidelity check between research and runtime. \n Two engines \n  \n   Engine  Module  Character    \n  Dataset replay   model_generation/replay.py  +  replay_70d_vector    bit-exact : replay vector must equal the dataset's stored vector (anti-leakage tests)  \n  Streaming replay   research/streaming_replay.py  (CHG-0035)  shared  LiveEngine  over a logical clock (zero sleeps): incremental bar aggregation, causal 50D + news + liquidity at time T, frozen policy + RiskEngine, direction-aware simulated fills on historical bid/ask, tick SL/TP first-touch, ledger MFE/MAE —  NO  order_send  (test-enforced)   \n   \n Anti-leakage \n Features at time T may consume only inf"}, {"u": "/ar/research/reproducibility/", "t": "Reproducibility [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  البحث  /  قابلية إعادة الإنتاج  \n Reproducibility \n Identity chain \n Every research artifact carries the chain that produced it: \n  ⧉   dataset fingerprint → feature schema hash → model manifest (scaler, weights)\n→ git commit → effective config (seeds, splits, purge/embargo)   \n Run snapshots ( research_run_snapshots ) store these at run time; provenance \n fields may be  NOT_RECORDED  (honest) but are never invented or backfilled. \n Determinism sources \n \n seeded training (seed-before-model construction — BUG-101 regression), \n frozen datasets (immutable, fingerprinted), \n logical-clock streaming replay (zero sleeps), \n freeze capture at forward-test cutoff +  post-run re-verification  of the \n \n freeze ( research/forward_test.py ). \n What breaks reproducibility (and is therefore guarded) \n  \n   Threat  Guard    \n  dataset mutation  immutable fingerprinted artifacts  \n  feature reorder"}, {"u": "/ar/research/validation/", "t": "Validation [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  البحث  /  التحقق  \n التحقق هو سبب وجود المنصة. الفشل في أي بوابة نهائي لذلك المرشح — بلا متوسطات، بلا استثناءات. \n سلسلة البوابات \n  \n   الطبقة  البوابات    \n  البيانات  بوابات الجودة · البصمة · المصدر  \n  الخصائص  بصمة المخطط · البُعد · الحدود · الترتيب  \n  النموذج  بوابة تحميل بـ10 بوابات · المعايرة · الحد الأدنى للأدلة  \n  البحث  Walk-Forward منقّى/محجور · حدود OOS · المتانة  \n  الحوكمة  تحقق 14-بوابة · معاملة الترقية  \n  وقت التشغيل  بوابة النشر الجنائية قبل كل إصدار  \n  الإصدار  SHA-256 · بيانات · SBOM · تحقق لاحق للنشر  \n   \n حدود OOS الدنيا (دورة حياة النموذج) \n macro-F1 ≥ 0.34 · الدقة المتوازنة ≥ 0.34 · ECE ≤ 0.15 · أدلة ≥ 100 صف. \n البوابة تعضّ — برهان علني \n مرشح السيولة 70D — أكثر سلاسل البحث هندسةً في المستودع — رُفض بواسطة هذه السلسلة نفسها (OOS NOT_ELIGIBLE) بعد أن جاءت نتائج Walk-Forward ومعايير الظل سلبية على بيانات حقيقية. بقي العقد الحي على 50D. البوابة التي لا ترفض ش"}, {"u": "/ar/research/walk-forward/", "t": "Walk-Forward [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "  البحث  /  Walk-Forward  \n Walk-Forward \n Method \n  training/walk_forward_trainer.py  +  research/walkforward.py  implement \n  purged, embargoed walk-forward  (Lopez de Prado): training folds are \n separated from test folds by a purge gap (label horizon) and an embargo gap \n (serial-correlation buffer), evaluated across temporally ordered folds. \n Defaults that matter (BUG-183) \n The production research path once ran with purge/embargo silently disabled — \n the constants existed but weren't wired. This is recorded as BUG-183 and fixed \n with regression tests:  DEFAULT_PURGE_SECONDS = 300 , `DEFAULT_EMBARGO_SECONDS \n = 60  are now wired into  ResearchPipeline.validate_candidate`, \n  OOSGate.evaluate ,  WalkForwardEngine.validate  and  BacktestEngine.run , and \n the  effective  purge/embargo values are recorded in every run's config. \n Why it is non-negotiable \n A walk-forward without pur"}, {"u": "/ar/getting-started/", "t": "البداية [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "Install, run and configure the engine. PAPER mode is the default; SHADOW gives you live data with zero order authority."}, {"u": "/ar/project/", "t": "المشروع [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "What Nexus is, what is certified vs experimental, where it is going — all evidence-graded."}, {"u": "/ar/architecture/", "t": "البنية [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "How the engine is built: hexagonal layers, the tick-to-decision path, model governance, and the intelligence loop."}, {"u": "/ar/research/", "t": "البحث [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "How historical data becomes falsifiable evidence — datasets, backtests, walk-forward, OOS, replay, counterfactuals."}, {"u": "/ar/engineering/", "t": "الهندسة [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "Quality gates, CI architecture, the release process, and the security posture."}, {"u": "/ar/guides/", "t": "أدلة [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "Operating the engine day to day: CLI, REST API, troubleshooting, common workflows."}, {"u": "/ar/contributing/", "t": "المساهمة [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "The engineering contract, documentation ownership, and how to add a language."}, {"u": "/ar/reference/", "t": "مرجع [ar]", "l": "ar", "x": "CLI reference, glossary, terminology, and honest answers in the FAQ."}, {"u": "/es/", "t": "Home [es]", "l": "es", "x": "Nexus Scalp Engine documentation homepage what's new capabilities architecture research"}, {"u": "/es/releases/", "t": "Versiones [es]", "l": "es", "x": "releases v9.0.8 changelog what's new history 959d7d9"}, {"u": "/es/architecture/code-navigation/", "t": "Code Navigation Map — Nexus Scalp Engine [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Arquitectura  /  code navigation  \n Code Navigation Map — Nexus Scalp Engine \n  Where to find things, for a developer (or agent) landing fresh in this repo.  This map is an INDEX. Detailed truth lives in:  -  agents/skill.md  — authoritative architecture map + repo contract (READ FIRST)  -  docs/architecture/dependency-map.md  — subsystem edges + contracts  -  docs/architecture/comment-style.md  — comment/doc conventions  -  docs/RELEASE.md  — CLI exit codes, update protocol, release verification  -  agents/bugs.md  — bug ledger (append-only; grep  ^## BUG-  tail for next free id)  \n Startup &amp; lifecycle \n  \n   Concern  Where    \n  Primary launcher (bootstrap sys.path, adapter bind, engine + web)   NexusTradingForexBot.py   \n  CLI entry ( nexus  /  nse , Typer)   src/nexus_scalp/cli/main.py   \n  Engine construction + async tick loop   src/nexus_scalp/application/live_engine.py  ( ru"}, {"u": "/es/architecture/comment-style/", "t": "Comment Style Guide — Nexus Scalp Engine [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Arquitectura  /  comment style  \n Comment Style Guide — Nexus Scalp Engine \n  Applies to all Python source in  src/ ,  tests/ , and  scripts/ .  Repo rule of thumb:  the repository should not contain more comments — it should contain better comments.   \n The one test \n  Could a competent developer derive this from the code itself?  \n If YES → do not comment. If NO → the comment may be valuable; then ask: \n \"Will this still be true and useful six months from now?\" If NO → do not write it. \n What comments are FOR \n A comment must be one of: \n  \n   Category  Documents  Example    \n  INVARIANT  a rule the code must keep but does not enforce visibly  \"Resume-safe hash: the hasher must cover the already-downloaded bytes too.\"  \n  SAFETY  fail-closed / fail-safe semantics  \"Fail closed: no inference must never yield a trade decision.\"  \n  CONCURRENCY  lock ownership, ordering, atomicity  \"Hol"}, {"u": "/es/architecture/control-center-ui/", "t": "Control Center UI Architecture (CHG-0043, TASK-CONTROL-CENTER) [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Arquitectura  /  control center ui  \n Control Center UI Architecture (CHG-0043, TASK-CONTROL-CENTER) \n  Operator-facing architecture of the NEXUS Control Center. UI-owned doc;  backend architecture lives in  docs/architecture/  elsewhere. Status  semantics here are the CONTRACT for every future CC view.  \n Purpose \n One coherent surface where an operator answers, without reading logs: \n WHAT is happening → WHY → WHAT changed → WHAT is blocked → WHAT is healthy → \n WHAT is serving → WHY did/didn't a trade happen → WHAT is safe to do next. \n Observation model: OBSERVE → UNDERSTAND → INVESTIGATE → ACT → VERIFY. \n Navigation &amp; Screens \n  \n   Tab (nav id)  Screen  Data sources (all read-only)    \n  Control Center ( tab-control-center )  Overview: mode banner, 6-tile status strip (Runtime/Data/Model/Inference/Database/MT5), runtime truth, market snapshot, latest decision, active warnings"}, {"u": "/es/architecture/crash-safety/", "t": "Crash-Safety Architecture (NSE) [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Arquitectura  /  crash safety  \n Crash-Safety Architecture (NSE) \n  Status: HARDENED_WITH_GAPS baseline documented 2026-09-01 (rev 2 — checker  regex fix + 381-site silent-handler backlog tracked as P1 violations).  Owner: Nexus-Main (crash-containment master pass).  Scope: the failure contract of every major execution boundary, from process  startup through model tensor execution, trading execution, Web/API, updater,  release pipeline, and shutdown.  Companion documents:  failure-recovery-matrix.md  (per-subsystem failure  matrix),  artifacts/forensics/crash-safety-audit.json  (machine audit).  \n \n 1. Governing principle \n The requirement is NOT \"the application must never crash\". The requirement is: \n  ⧉   NO SILENT CRASH      NO SILENT EXCEPTION      NO FALSE SUCCESS\nNO FAKE HEALTH       NO FABRICATED MODEL OUTPUT\nNO UNSAFE TRADING AFTER CRITICAL FAILURE\nNO CORRUPTED STATE AFTER FAI"}, {"u": "/es/architecture/data-flow/", "t": "Data Flow — Tick to Decision [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Arquitectura  /  Flujo de datos  \n Data Flow — from tick to decision \n This is the canonical path (from  agents/skill.md  §4). Every arrow is a \n contract boundary. \n  ⧉   TickData (MT5 / paper / gateway)\n  → ScalpFeatureEngine.to_tensor_input()\n      50D base (scalp_v1 · FEATURE_NAMES · [-3,+3] · finite)\n  → assemble_70d / build_70d_vector()\n      70D canonical: Base 0..49 | News 10D 50..59 | Liquidity 10D 60..69\n  → InferenceContractValidator\n      scaler dim == feature dim · schema hash · finite · bounds\n  → ScalpNet → 4 logits (NO_TRADE / BUY / SELL / WAIT) → confidence gate 0.35\n  → regime_classifier (Regime Guardian)\n  → signals/policy + rule_matrix (~30 rules, TTL 5s cache)\n  → RiskEngine.calculate_dynamic_volume() + evaluate_proposal()\n      free-margin 20% clamp · tier caps · HARD_MAX_LOTS\n  → OrderManager (60-scenario router · 11 position states ·\n      MAX_TOTAL_EXPOSURE=1 ·"}, {"u": "/es/architecture/database/", "t": "Database Architecture [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Arquitectura  /  Base de datos  \n Database Architecture \n Canonical stores \n  \n   DB  Contents  Notes    \n   artifacts/audit.db   trading ledger, experience outcomes, accounting, research registry, strategy lifecycle, incidents, hygiene  one canonical ledger; SQLite  WAL   \n   artifacts/news.db   news ingestion, analysis, consensus, impacts  lazy schema on first save  \n   candle_intel.db   candle intelligence  versioned schema  \n  settings DB  secrets + user intent (Telegram creds via  settings_service )  never in YAML (INV-010)  \n   \n Write path \n  AuditRepository  queues writes to a  background worker thread  — the tick \n hot path never performs synchronous DB work (INV-001). Historical \n experience/outcome/ledger rows are  immutable  (INV-007); corrections go \n through evidence → reconstruction → derived records with provenance, never row \n rewrites. \n Migrations \n  src/nexus_scalp/"}, {"u": "/es/architecture/dependency-map/", "t": "Architecture Dependency Map — Nexus Scalp Engine (NSE) [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Arquitectura  /  dependency map  \n Architecture Dependency Map — Nexus Scalp Engine (NSE) \n  Maintained per the MASTER MULTI-AGENT CONTRACT §9 (see  agents/multi-agent-git-contract.md ).  Describes actual subsystem relationships (verified against executable code; see agents/skill.md for the full inventory).  Every edge documents: contract, direction, expected data, safety guarantees.  \n Canonical high-level flow \n  ⧉   MT5\n  │  (tick/order/position/account events)\n  ▼\nMT5 Adapter / Providers            [ports: IMT5Port; adapters: mt5/, paper/, remote]\n  │  (normalized events)\n  ▼\nLiveEngine (async event loop)      [src/nexus_scalp/application/live_engine.py]\n  ├─ Feature Engine                [features/scalp_features.py → FEATURE_VECTOR_50D]\n  ├─ Model Runtime                 [models/scalp_net.py → MODEL_MANIFEST; Champion/Challenger]\n  ├─ News Context                  [news/ → NEWS_CO"}, {"u": "/es/architecture/execution-pipeline/", "t": "Execution Pipeline [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Arquitectura  /  Pipeline de ejecución  \n Execution Pipeline \n  execution/order_manager.py  is the single dispatch authority (INV-004). It is \n large by design (convention-locked hot path) and is being decomposed \n surgically, seam by seam, with golden tests. \n Path of an order \n  ⧉   TradeProposal (frozen domain contract, execution_id trace)\n  → policy/confluence checks (SMC matrix, Regime Guardian, confidence gate)\n  → RiskEngine.evaluate_proposal() → dynamic volume (fractional Kelly)\n  → OrderManager router (60 scenarios: fills, rejections, partials, errors)\n  → IMT5Port adapter (Win32 IPC / ZMQ / paper)\n  → position lifecycle (11 states with hysteresis)\n  → protective exits (SL/TP first-touch, breakeven lock, profit giveback,\n      adaptive exit protection)\n  → broker reconciliation (broker truth wins — INV-011)\n  → accounting + autopsy (immutable ledger)   \n Hard clamps (never byp"}, {"u": "/es/architecture/failure-recovery-matrix/", "t": "Failure-Recovery Matrix (NSE crash-containment pass) [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Arquitectura  /  failure recovery matrix  \n Failure-Recovery Matrix (NSE crash-containment pass) \n  Status: baseline 2026-09-01. Companion to  crash-safety.md  and   artifacts/forensics/crash-safety-audit.json .  Every row = subsystem × failure → expected console log, state, recovery,  exit, and the test that proves it. GREEN means failure-injected → detected →  logged → safe behavior → regression exists (never \"a try/except exists\").  \n Legend — State: truthful runtime state after the failure. Log: minimum \n console/file record. Rec: recovery policy. Exit: CLI/process exit contract. \n Test: primary regression evidence. \n  \n   #  Subsystem  Failure  Log (console)  State  Rec  Exit  Test    \n  1  startup  missing/invalid config at launch  red panel  cfg_detail=Parse error…  + doctor FAIL  NOT READY  halt  1 / EXIT_RUNTIME  launcher doctor contract; BUG-149/156 lineage  \n  2  startup   _"}, {"u": "/es/architecture/model-pipeline/", "t": "Model Pipeline [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Arquitectura  /  Pipeline de modelos  \n Model Pipeline \n Lifecycle \n  ⧉   DATASET (versioned artifact + quality gates + fingerprint)\n  → EXPERIMENT (equal budgets/seeds/splits; dataset-fairness gate)\n  → CANDIDATE MODEL (+ manifest: schema hash · scaler · dataset ID · git commit)\n  → VALIDATION (walk-forward · OOS gate · robustness · calibration)\n  → REGISTRY (content-addressed; challenger only)\n  → LOAD GATE (10 gates, enforced at every attach)\n  → SHADOW PARITY (zero order authority)\n  → OPERATOR PROMOTION (READY_FOR_REVIEW → APPROVED → CHAMPION; atomic transaction)\n  → ROLLBACK PREVIEW / EMERGENCY FREEZE   \n Artifact-first Model Factory ( model_generation/ ) \n Datasets, experiments and models are **versioned filesystem artifacts with \n manifests** — inference needs no database. The manifest carries \n  feature_schema_hash ,  training_dataset_id , scaler identity and git commit. \n Sca"}, {"u": "/es/architecture/observability-log-contract/", "t": "Observability Log Contract — frozen 2026-09-01 (Agent 2) [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Arquitectura  /  observability log contract  \n Observability Log Contract — frozen 2026-09-01 (Agent 2) \n Authoritative in-repo reference for the log-noise contracts proven in the \n operational-observability sprint and pinned by \n  tests/unit/test_operational_log_hygiene.py  + \n  tests/unit/test_observability_contract_freeze.py  + \n  tests/unit/test_logging_redaction.py . \n Any future change to these behaviors MUST update those tests in the same \n commit (test-first rule: a new repetitive runtime event needs an \n aggregation/transition/rate-limit test before merge). \n Companion tooling:  src/nexus_scalp/observability/event_aggregator.py  \n (EventBatchAggregator — bounded, thread-safe, first-occurrence-immediate). \n \n Core invariants (all events) \n \n SEVERITY ladder: DEBUG = diagnostic detail; INFO = normal state / bounded \n \n informational transitions; WARNING = first failure or action"}, {"u": "/es/architecture/observability-map/", "t": "Observability Map — Nexus Scalp Engine (NSE) [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Arquitectura  /  observability map  \n Observability Map — Nexus Scalp Engine (NSE) \n  TASK-OBS-AUDIT (2026-08-31, HEAD baseline 1f60832; delivered at dcc80d7).  Agent: Hermes-ObsForensic. AUDIT-ONLY: zero runtime code changed.  Machine-readable companion:  artifacts/forensics/observability-audit.json .  Method: black-box reconstruction from runtime evidence (logs / DBs / artifacts /  live API / CLI) FIRST, then targeted read-only code sweeps for every claim.  Evidence markers: [L]=live-probed today, [DB]=DB census, [LOG]=log sample, [C]=code file:line.  \n 1. What the system actually produces today \n  \n   Channel  Reality (verified)    \n  Logs  severity-split  logs/{critical,error,warning,info}/YYYY/MM/*.log , ISO-8601  +03:30 , 10 MB part rotation, retention 30/30/90/365 d [C observability/logging.py:388-394]. Only 08-29 + 08-31 exist; 08-30 absent. ~190 MB on 08-31 (131 MB error).  \n "}, {"u": "/es/architecture/observability/", "t": "Observability [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Arquitectura  /  Observabilidad  \n Observability \n NSE treats observability as a subsystem with contracts, not a logging afterthought. \n If the engine cannot show  why  it did something, its behavior is indistinguishable \n from a bug — so showing why is engineered, not hoped for. \n Structured logging ( observability/logging.py ) \n \n Severity-split, date-organized storage:  logs/&lt;sev&gt;/YYYY/MM/YYYY-MM-DD.log . \n ISO-8601 timestamps (broker-local offset aware), event/component/category/ \n \n error-code fields, correlation context. \n \n Daily + size rotation with zero-loss part files; per-severity retention. \n Key + high-entropy redaction; ANSI-free stacks. \n \n Incident response ( incidents/ ) \n Canonical incident model ( INC-YYYY-hex8 , 8 statuses, 5 severities), \n fingerprint correlation, causal-chain timeline reconstruction, value lineage \n with first-divergence location, WHY workfl"}, {"u": "/es/architecture/order_manager_architecture/", "t": "ORDER_MANAGER.PY — Architectural Map (Agent-5, Phase A) [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Arquitectura  /  order manager architecture  \n ORDER_MANAGER.PY — Architectural Map (Agent-5, Phase A) \n Evidence base: forensic inventory at HEAD  0015608  (post Agent-4 winner-protection \n sprint  0839da3 ). No edits made during this phase. This document precedes any \n extraction (task brief §24). \n 1. Current shape \n 6372 LOC, 1 god class + 6 support types \n  \n   Item  Span  Notes    \n  Module constants (18)  L60-155  exposure caps, BE/giveback/trailing geometry  \n  ExitMechanism (Enum)  L158  exit taxonomy  \n  PositionState (Enum)  L172  11 in-trade lifecycles  \n  PositionEvaluationStep  L190  trajectory step record  \n  LSFTicketState  L209  LSF per-ticket state  \n  PositionProtectionState  L226  per-ticket protection facts (dataclass)  \n  SmartPositionMetrics  L281  57 derived metrics (dataclass)  \n  OrderLifecycleManager  L348-6372  81 methods, 99 distinct  self.*  state attrs  \n"}, {"u": "/es/architecture/overview/", "t": "Architecture Overview [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Arquitectura  /  Visión general  \n NSE es  hexagonal (ports-and-adapters) y dirigido por eventos : las plataformas de bróker, modelos y adaptadores de red están detrás de contratos de puerto ( IMT5Port ,  IGatewayPort ); el dominio nunca sabe qué bróker está conectado. \n  ⧉   Datos de mercado (MT5 / ZMQ / paper)\n  → Características causales — base 50D (scalp_v1) · ensamblado 70D gobernado\n  → Validador de inferencia — hash de esquema · dim del scaler · límites (rechazo sonoro)\n  → ScalpNet (TCN + auto-atención) — 4 logits → puerta de confianza\n  → Guardián de régimen → Matriz de política SMC (~30 reglas)\n  → Motor de riesgo (tamaño Kelly · margen ≤20% · topes de nivel · HARD_MAX_LOTS=10)\n  → OrderManager (router de 60 escenarios · 11 estados de posición · teardown atómico)\n  → Adaptador IMT5Port → MT5 / paper / shadow (autoridad de órdenes cero)\n  → Contabilidad (SQLite WAL inmutable) "}, {"u": "/es/architecture/qa-assurance-contract/", "t": "QA ASSURANCE CONTRACT — Deep Assurance Layer (CHG-0045) [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Arquitectura  /  qa assurance contract  \n QA ASSURANCE CONTRACT — Deep Assurance Layer (CHG-0045) \n  Owner: Nexus-Main (TASK-QA-DEEP-ASSURANCE). This document is the contract  for the OSS-grade adversarial QA layer: lanes, markers, budgets, the JSON  result schema, and the governance rules for flaky/open-defect tests.  \n 1. Position in the gate hierarchy \n  \n   Lane  Command  When  Budget    \n  Pre-push critical gate (existing, NOT replaced)   beforePush.sh  /  check_local.py   every push  ~2.5 min  \n   Deep assurance — fast    python scripts/qa/deep_assurance.py --fast   PR / push lane in CI  &lt; 60 s  \n   Deep assurance — full    python scripts/qa/deep_assurance.py   main / scheduled / dispatch  &lt; 5 min  \n  Mutation proof   python scripts/qa/run_mutations.py   scheduled / dispatch (weekly)  &lt; 15 min  \n   \n The deep-assurance layer NEVER replaces the runtime gate; it adds \n ind"}, {"u": "/es/architecture/QA_BLIND_SPOT_MATRIX/", "t": "QA BLIND-SPOT MATRIX — Nexus Scalp Engine [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Arquitectura  /  QA BLIND SPOT MATRIX  \n QA BLIND-SPOT MATRIX — Nexus Scalp Engine \n  CHG-0045 / TASK-QA-DEEP-ASSURANCE (Nexus-Main, 2026-09-02).  Required first milestone of the OSS-grade adversarial QA brief: prove which  gaps matter BEFORE building test mass. Derived from  agents/bugs.md   (BUG-001..BUG-208) and  agents/change_control.md  (CHG-0001..CHG-0050).  \n 1. Method \n \n  Defect-history mining  — every BUG/CHG row classified by subsystem, \n \n severity (P0 money/execution · P1 decision-path/trust · P2 operator \n trust/diagnostics · P3 robustness), and named regression test. \n \n  Detection-quality audit  — does the named regression test the ROOT \n \n CAUSE or only the incident's symptom path? \n \n  Re-entry analysis  — can the same class return through another door? \n  Verdict  — KEEP / IMPROVE / MERGE / DELETE / MISSING per test family. \n \n 2. Matrix — defect history → detection "}, {"u": "/es/architecture/repository-hygiene/", "t": "Repository Hygiene Audit — Nexus Scalp Engine [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Arquitectura  /  repository hygiene  \n Repository Hygiene Audit — Nexus Scalp Engine \n   Date:  2026-08-31 ·  HEAD:   1f60832  (main) ·  Working tree:  UNCHANGED (0 modifications)   Mode:  READ-ONLY forensic librarian pass. Nothing was fixed, moved, deleted, or refactored.   Machine-readable twin:   artifacts/forensics/repository-hygiene-audit.json    2026-08-31 repair pass:  CLEANUP-001/002/003/004/005/006 repaired — networkx declared as runtime dep, psycopg declared via new  postgres  extra, requirements ranges reconciled to pyproject, skill.md runner path fixed, tick_storage.py removed, 32 e2e_cc files archived to  scratch/e2e_cc_archive/ , .pyproj.bak removed.   Scope guard:  excludes all active-agent work (BUG-166..174, anti-crash, decomposition, release).  \n 1. What was analyzed \n \n 1,621 tracked files (724 py / 625 md / 80 json / 22 js / 16 mjs / 15 ps1 / 10 yml) \n 351 Python so"}, {"u": "/es/architecture/research-stack/", "t": "Research Stack [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Arquitectura  /  Pila de investigación  \n Research Stack \n The research side answers one question with evidence: **is this candidate good \n enough to trust — and can we prove it on data it never saw?** \n Pipeline \n  ⧉   DATA (canonical tick/bar datasets, provenance-fingerprinted)\n  → FEATURES (same causal contract as live: 50D base, governed 70D assembly)\n  → LABELING (triple-barrier, purged + embargoed)\n  → TRAINING (deterministic seeds, walk-forward)\n  → BACKTEST (friction-aware: spread / slippage / latency)\n  → WALK-FORWARD VALIDATION\n  → OOS GATE (hard: failure ⇒ REJECTED)\n  → ROBUSTNESS STRESS\n  → COUNTERFACTUAL / STRATIFICATION EVIDENCE\n  → CANDIDATE REGISTRY (content-addressed)\n  → SHADOW COMPARISON (zero order authority)\n  → OPERATOR-GATED PROMOTION   \n Key guarantees \n \n  Leakage prevention (INV-008):  purged + embargoed walk-forward \n \n (Lopez de Prado); broker history REPLAC"}, {"u": "/es/architecture/runtime-certification-gate/", "t": "Runtime Certification Gate — canonical pre-push contract [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Arquitectura  /  runtime certification gate  \n Runtime Certification Gate — canonical pre-push contract \n   CHANGE-ID:  CHG-0051 ·  TASK-ID:  TASK-RUNTIME-GATE ·  Status:  ACTIVE   One command. One answer.   python scripts/ci/runtime_gate.py   \n 1. Purpose \n The repository has many test families (runtime, features, 50D/70D, models, \n database, execution, providers, research, CLI, observability, installer, \n integration). The problem was never test count — it was the absence of ONE \n strong, trustworthy, repeatable command answering: \n  \"Is the composed runtime safe, coherent, loadable, and operational enough  for an agent to push its change?\"  \n The Runtime Certification Gate is that command. It is a **curated, layered \n certification of the REAL composed runtime** — not \"run all pytest\". It \n exercises the actual boot path (config → adapter →  LiveEngine  service \n graph → decision pi"}, {"u": "/es/architecture/runtime/", "t": "Runtime — the LiveEngine Loop [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Arquitectura  /  Runtime  \n Runtime — the LiveEngine loop \n  application/live_engine.py  is the orchestrator: a single async event loop \n that drives the tick pipeline and coordinates background workers. \n Startup sequence \n \n Launcher binds an adapter ( DirectMT5Adapter  /  RemoteMT5GatewayAdapter  / \n \n paper) behind  IMT5Port . \n \n Pre-flight  doctor gate : MT5 terminal present? config valid? platform \n \n supported? — otherwise the engine refuses to start. \n \n Migration gate: canonical DB migration engine runs (additive, checksummed). \n Model load: Champion bundle validated by the  10-gate load gate  (manifest \n \n hash, scaler dim, schema family, width contract…). \n \n Mode select:  PAPER (default)  / SHADOW / LIVE (interactive confirmation). \n Web server: FastAPI Control Center + SSE + WebSocket. \n Workers start (audit writer, research, hygiene, incidents, Telegram). \n \n Tick pipeli"}, {"u": "/es/architecture/system-map/", "t": "System Map [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Arquitectura  /  Mapa del sistema  \n System Map \n Package inventory ( src/nexus_scalp/ ) \n  ⧉   nexus_scalp/\n├── domain/            frozen Pydantic contracts (TickData, TradeProposal, …)\n├── ports/             IMT5Port · IGatewayPort        ← the hexagon seam\n├── adapters/          mt5/ (Win32 IPC) · gateway (ZMQ) · paper/ · database/ (AuditRepository, WAL)\n├── features/          scalp_features (50D) · schema registry · schema_contract (70D SSoT)\n│                      liquidity_engine · regime_classifier · temporal (research)\n├── models/            ScalpNet (dual-path TCN + self-attention)\n├── training/          walk_forward_trainer · labeling/ (triple-barrier)\n├── signals/           policy · rule matrix (~30 SMC rules)\n├── strategies/        factory (+ provider_gate for LLM/AI services)\n├── risk/              RiskEngine (Kelly sizing, clamps, kill switch)\n├── execution/         order"}, {"u": "/es/contributing/add-language/", "t": "Adding a Language [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Contribuir  /  Añadir un idioma  \n Adding a Language \n The multilingual architecture is data-driven: adding Turkish, French, Russian, \n Chinese or Japanese is a directory + registry entry — no code changes. \n Recipe \n \n  Create the language tree  \n \n  ⧉      site/content/&lt;lang&gt;/            # translated site content (mirror of en tree)\n   docs/&lt;lang&gt;/index.md            # optional docs-root landing page   \n \n  Register the language  in  scripts/docs/site_config.py : \n \n  ⧉      LANGUAGES = {\n       &quot;en&quot;: {&quot;name&quot;: &quot;English&quot;, &quot;dir&quot;: &quot;ltr&quot;},\n       &quot;fa&quot;: {&quot;name&quot;: &quot;فارسی&quot;,   &quot;dir&quot;: &quot;rtl&quot;},\n       ...\n       &quot;tr&quot;: {&quot;name&quot;: &quot;Türkçe&quot;,  &quot;dir&quot;: &quot;ltr&quot;},   # ← new\n   }   \n \n  Translate core pages first  (in priority order): \n \n  index  → "}, {"u": "/es/contributing/contribution-guide/", "t": "Contribution Guide [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Contribuir  /  Guía de contribución  \n El repositorio se desarrolla con agentes coordinados bajo un contrato de ingeniería estricto; los contribuyentes humanos se benefician de la misma disciplina. \n Bootstrap \n  ⧉   git clone https://github.com/Opselon/NexusTradingForexBot.git\ncd NexusTradingForexBot\npython -m venv .venv &amp;&amp; .\\.venv\\Scripts\\Activate.ps1\npip install -e .[dev]\npytest tests/unit -q   \n Disciplina de cambio \n \n  Lee primero la memoria de ingeniería :  \">https://github.com/Opselon/NexusTradingForexBot/blob/main/agents/skill.md\">  agents/skill.md   (mapa de arquitectura),  \">https://github.com/Opselon/NexusTradingForexBot/blob/main/agents/runtime_invariants.md\">  agents/runtime_invariants.md  ,  \">https://github.com/Opselon/NexusTradingForexBot/blob/main/agents/bugs.md\">  agents/bugs.md  . \n  Reclama antes de codificar  — añade una fila a  agents/taskboard.md . \n  Re"}, {"u": "/es/contributing/documentation/", "t": "Documentation Workflow [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Contribuir  /  Flujo de documentación  \n Documentation Workflow \n Ownership \n Documentation is owned by the  Nexus-Docs  role \n (registry:  docs/agent_handoffs/DOCS_REGISTRY.md ). The boundary is hard: \n docs changes never touch runtime code, and code owners never need to fix docs \n tooling. If documentation exposes a suspected code defect, it is recorded in \n the registry with subsystem attribution — the implementation stays untouched. \n Information architecture \n  ⧉   docs/            engineering documentation (markdown, this IA tree)\nsite/            GitHub Pages source (builds docs/ + translations into a static site)\nscripts/docs/    validation tooling (check_docs.py, check_translations.py, build_site.py)\n.github/workflows/docs.yml    docs CI + Pages deploy   \n Source of truth \n \n  English  is the source language; every other language is a translation \n \n with status metadata ( com"}, {"u": "/es/engineering/ci/", "t": "CI Architecture [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Ingeniería  /  Arquitectura de CI  \n CI Architecture \n Workflows \n  \n   Workflow  Trigger  Purpose    \n   ci.yml   push (main/develop/ci-tests), PR, weekly drift scan  ruff · format · mypy · pytest (critical; matrix arms for integration/e2e/research/model on demand)  \n   tests-os.yml   matrix OS runs  cross-platform unit sanity  \n   security.yml   PR + weekly schedule  CodeQL + Trivy  \n   osv-scanner.yml   schedule  dependency vulnerabilities  \n   lockfile-diff.yml   dependency file changes  lockfile drift  \n   js-tests.yml   Web/ changes   node --check  + JS tests  \n   release.yml    v*  tags  only   build + verify + publish release artifacts  \n   docker.yml   Docker surface changes  image build gates  \n   docs.yml   docs/site/README changes  documentation validation + Pages deploy (this platform)  \n   \n Trigger policy (CI_TRIGGER_POLICY v1): tags never fire CI (release-only), main \n "}, {"u": "/es/engineering/quality/", "t": "Quality & Testing [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Ingeniería  /  Calidad y pruebas  \n Quality &amp; Testing \n The quality gate \n Every push passes  beforePush.sh  /  beforePush.ps1  (5 stages): \n \n  ruff check  (lint) \n  ruff format  check \n  mypy src  \n  CRITICAL suite  pytest run ( tests/critical_suite.txt , ~779 tests, \n \n RAM-aware xdist workers, coverage) \n \n Forensic  deploy gate  writing  artifacts/forensics/deploy_gate_result.json  \n \n  -FullSuite  runs the whole ~1931-test unit corpus. CI mirrors the gate \n ( .github/workflows/ci.yml ) and adds CodeQL, Trivy, OSV, lockfile-diff and JS \n tests on separate workflows. \n Test architecture \n  \n   Suite  Location  Character    \n  Unit   tests/unit/   ~1900 tests; critical subset in  critical_suite.txt   \n  Integration   tests/integration/   API + engine-level, run standalone/sequential in CI  \n  Golden   tests/golden/  +  test_*_golden.py   byte/behavior-identical extraction gates "}, {"u": "/es/engineering/release-process/", "t": "Release Process [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Ingeniería  /  Proceso de release  \n Release Process \n Versioning \n Semver, single canonical source:  pyproject.toml  ( version = \"9.0.6\" ) \n stamped into every build artifact. The README never hard-codes a conflicting \n version — it defers to  nexus version  / the release metadata. \n Pipeline ( .github/workflows/release.yml ) \n Tag-triggered  only  ( v* ). Stages: \n \n Validate tag vs version metadata \n Run the critical test suite (a release run that fails the suite does not \n \n publish — see the v9.0.6 re-cut history in the taskboard) \n \n Build Windows x64 artifacts:  NexusScalpEngine-&lt;version&gt;-win-x64-setup.exe  \n \n + portable  .zip  (PyInstaller) \n \n Generate SHA-256 digests, release manifest, SBOM; embed manifest in the \n \n portable bundle \n \n Publish GitHub Release \n  Post-publish verification  ( release/verify.py ): checksums, manifest \n \n paths, embedded layout (BUG-160 li"}, {"u": "/es/engineering/security/", "t": "Security [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Ingeniería  /  Seguridad  \n Security \n Secrets \n \n Secrets live in the  settings DB  / secret store — never in  live.yaml , \n \n never committed (INV-010). Provider URLs/keys are redacted in health \n endpoints and logs ( [REDACTED_SECRET] ). \n \n  scripts/ci/scan_secrets.py  fails CI on secret-shaped strings in \n \n source/config/docs. \n \n Diagnostics export ( nexus export-diagnostics ) is sanitized by contract — \n \n never contains secrets. \n Scanning (CI) \n CodeQL (SAST), Trivy (containers/FS), OSV dependency scanning, lockfile-diff, \n secret scan — see  CI architecture . \n Trust boundaries \n  \n   Boundary  Rule    \n  broker ↔ engine   IMT5Port  adapters only; account-identity fail-safe at connect  \n  research/learning ↔ execution  zero order authority (INV-002); shadow never mutates execution  \n  observability ↔ trading  incidents/forensics are diagnostic-only  \n  Telegram  read-only ou"}, {"u": "/es/getting-started/configuration/", "t": "Configuration [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Inicio  /  Configuración  \n Configuration \n Configuration has three layers with different authorities. Mixing them up is a \n classic failure mode — read this page before editing YAML by hand. \n 1.  AppConfig  (bootstrap / import / export) \n  src/nexus_scalp/configuration/config.py  — loads the YAML contract \n ( configs/base.yaml  is the canonical base;  configs/live.yaml.example  is the \n live-shaped example). Used for bootstrap/import/export only. \n 2. Runtime configuration (authoritative live state) \n  RuntimeConfiguration  via  RuntimeConfigStore.get_snapshot()  is the \n  authoritative live state  — versioned, hot-reloadable. Consumers must read \n through  get_snapshot() , never cached constructor values. Scope tags decide \n when a change applies ( LIVE_IMMEDIATE  vs  NEXT_DECISION ). \n 3. Settings DB (secrets + user intent) \n Credentials (e.g. Telegram) live in the settings databas"}, {"u": "/es/getting-started/first-run/", "t": "First-Run Safety [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Inicio  /  Primera ejecución  \n First-Run Safety (Demo → Shadow → Live) \n This engine executes on a real broker. The repository's own first-run guidance \n is a strict ladder — do not skip steps. \n  \n   Step  Action  Why    \n  1️⃣  Log into a  DEMO account  in MT5 ( File → Open an Account → Practice/Demo ), confirm the account number/label before touching the bot  LIVE and demo accounts can look identical in MT5's login window  \n  2️⃣  MT5:  Tools → Options → Expert Advisors → tick \"Allow Algo Trading\"   Without this, orders are rejected  \n  3️⃣  Copy  configs/live.yaml  →  configs/demo.yaml ; set demo credentials; confirm  risk.max_concurrent_positions: 1 ,  risk.risk_per_trade_pct  (e.g. 0.5),  risk.max_account_drawdown_pct   Never touch a live config while real money can be reached  \n  4️⃣  Run  SHADOW  first ( nexus start --mode shadow ) for days; review the dashboard + Telegram rep"}, {"u": "/es/getting-started/installation/", "t": "Installation [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Inicio  /  Instalación  \n Nexus Scalp Engine es una  plataforma de trading cuantitativo basada en investigación : un runtime hexagonal y dirigido por eventos para MetaTrader 5 (mercado principal: XAUUSD M1) que conecta datos de mercado, ingeniería causal de características, inferencia de modelos, política de estrategia, control de riesgo, replay, ejecución, observabilidad y validación reproducible en un único pipeline auditable. \n &lt;div class=\"callout\"&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;No es una promesa de beneficios.&lt;/strong&gt; Es una plataforma de investigación e ingeniería. Los estados se gradúan por evidencia y los resultados negativos se publican — incluido el rechazo de nuestro propio candidato de investigación 70D por evidencia fuera de muestra. El scalping apalancado conlleva un riesgo financiero extremo.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt; \n Qué lo hace diferente \n \n  Evidencia antes que afir"}, {"u": "/es/getting-started/quickstart/", "t": "Quickstart [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Inicio  /  Inicio rápido  \n Inicio rápido \n  ⧉   # 1. Instalar (desarrolladores, desde el código)\ngit clone https://github.com/Opselon/NexusTradingForexBot.git\ncd NexusTradingForexBot\npython -m venv .venv &amp;&amp; .\\.venv\\Scripts\\Activate.ps1   # Linux: source .venv/bin/activate\npip install -e .[dev]\n\n# 2. Verificar el sistema\nnexus doctor          # diagnóstico (solo lectura), 19 categorías + correcciones sugeridas\nnexus health          # READY / DEGRADED / NOT READY\n\n# 3. Ejecutar — PAPER por defecto, nunca LIVE en silencio\nnexus start           # simulación, Control Center en http://127.0.0.1:8080\n\n# 4. Evaluar con datos reales, cero autoridad de órdenes\nnexus start --mode shadow\n\n# 5. Detener\nnexus stop            # para --daemon; Ctrl+C en primer plano   \n Modos \n  \n   Modo  Datos  Órdenes  Uso    \n   paper  (por defecto)  simulados  simuladas  primera ejecución, UI, desarrollo "}, {"u": "/es/guides/api/", "t": "API Reference [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Guías  /  Referencia API  \n API Reference \n The Control Center backend is a FastAPI application exposing * 203  /api/   \n endpoints across 22 groups** (verified by scanning the route modules in \n  src/nexus_scalp/web/ ), plus Server-Sent Events for ticks and WebSocket for \n the dashboard. Everything the UI does, the API does — the UI is a consumer of \n the same surface. \n  NOTA  Endpoint counts are generated from the repository's actual route decorators —  they drift with the code, and the docs doctor flags stale counts.  \n Discovery \n \n  Health / readiness:   GET /health  →  200  with  READY / DEGRADED ,  503  when NOT READY. \n  Engine state:   GET /api/status  and  GET /api/live/state  (the dashboard heart, includes the effective serving contract). \n  OpenAPI:  the FastAPI app serves its schema at  /openapi.json  and Swagger UI at  /docs  on the same port as the UI (  http://127.0.0."}, {"u": "/es/guides/cli/", "t": "CLI Guide [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Guías  /  Guía CLI  \n CLI Guide \n  nexus  is the application command (installation lifecycle lives in \n  install.ps1 ; everything you  operate  lives in  nexus ). From source: \n  python -m nexus_scalp.cli.main  (alias  nse ). \n Commands \n  ⧉   nexus help            # same authoritative surface as --help (+ &#x27;nexus help start&#x27;)\nnexus version         # build identity (--json / --plain)\nnexus doctor          # read-only diagnostics (19 categories) + suggested fixes\nnexus status          # health + environment + version\nnexus health          # quick health summary (READY / DEGRADED / NOT READY)\nnexus config          # inspect/validate active configuration (secrets masked)\nnexus start           # PAPER mode by default — never LIVE silently\nnexus stop / restart  # control the background engine (honest dead-pid reporting)\nnexus logs [--tail N] [--errors]\nnexus test --mode quick|unit|"}, {"u": "/es/guides/common-workflows/", "t": "Common Workflows [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Guías  /  Flujos comunes  \n Common Workflows \n 1. Daily development loop \n  ⧉   git pull &amp;&amp; .venv/Scripts/Activate.ps1        # Windows dev\nnexus test --mode quick                        # fast sanity\n# ... edit ...\npytest tests/unit -q -k &quot;70 or schema&quot;         # targeted suite\n./beforePush.ps1 -SkipPush                     # full gate before pushing   \n 2. Evaluate the engine on real data (risk-free) \n  ⧉   nexus start --mode shadow      # live feed, zero order authority\n# observe Control Center → SHADOW section: disagreement analysis, drift, health\nnexus stop   \n 3. Research a candidate \n  ⧉   nexus model-dataset-build      # canonical dataset (fingerprinted)\nnexus model-experiment-create  # fair A/B/C protocol\nnexus model-train              # deterministic, seeded\nnexus model-validate           # walk-forward + OOS gate + robustness\nnexus model-replay             "}, {"u": "/es/guides/troubleshooting/", "t": "Troubleshooting [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Guías  /  Solución de problemas  \n Troubleshooting \n  Rule of thumb:  nexus doctor  first — it reports 19 diagnostic categories  with suggested fixes and is the same gate the engine runs pre-launch.  \n Engine refuses to start \n  \n   Symptom  Likely cause  Action    \n  \"MT5 terminal missing/not running\"  terminal closed / not installed  start MT5, log in (demo first), retry  \n  config validation error  YAML contract violation   nexus config --validate &lt;path&gt; ; fix the named key  \n  environment blocked (exit 3)  Windows ARM64  unsupported by dependency stack; use x64  \n  migration gate failure  schema drift   nexus db migrate ; check  nexus db hygiene status   \n   \n UI / dashboard \n  \n   Symptom  Likely cause  Action    \n  dashboard unreachable  port drift (dev UI/API ports can move)  check  nexus status  output / launcher log for the bound port  \n  \"Cannot GET /\" on some port  wro"}, {"u": "/es/docs-hub/", "t": "Nexus Scalp Engine — Documentation [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Centro de documentación  \n Nexus Scalp Engine — Documentation \n  Research-driven quantitative trading platform  — a hexagonal, event-driven \n scalping engine for MetaTrader 5 (primary market: XAUUSD M1), built around \n causal feature engineering, artifact-first model governance, deterministic \n research tooling, and forensic observability. \n  IMPORTANTE  This documentation describes a  research and engineering platform . It is  not investment advice, and nothing here is a promise of profitability.  Leveraged scalping carries extreme financial risk. See   Project Status  for what is certified vs experimental.  \n Start here \n  \n   Question  Page    \n  What is Nexus and why does it exist?   Vision   \n  How do I run it?   Quickstart   \n  How is the architecture structured?   Architecture Overview   \n  How does data become a decision?   Data Flow   \n  How is research validated?   Research M"}, {"u": "/es/project/capabilities/", "t": "Capability Matrix [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Proyecto  /  Matriz de capacidades  \n Capability Matrix \n Legend: ✅ Certified · 🟢 Implemented · 🟡 Experimental · 🔵 Research · 🚧 In \n progress · 📌 Planned · ⚪ Not verified \n  \n   Capability  Status  Evidence (repository)  Notes    \n  Causal 50D feature engine ( scalp_v1 )  ✅ Certified   features/scalp_features.py , schema registry, golden/parity tests  live contract; NaN/Inf deterministic fallback  \n  70D canonical contract ( scalp_v3 )  🟢 Implemented (research)   features/schema_contract.py  SSoT, hash, inference validator (10 rejection codes)  candidate-only; negative OOS evidence so far  \n  Liquidity intelligence (10D block)  🟡 Experimental   features/liquidity_engine.py , INV-019 causality rules  research series; governed by  liquidity_features_enabled   \n  News intelligence 10D + bounded gate  🟡 Experimental   news/ , gate bounds boost ≤0.05 / penalty ≤0.10  opt-in, disabled by def"}, {"u": "/es/project/milestones/", "t": "Milestones & Project Story [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Proyecto  /  Hitos  \n Milestones — the project story \n This is a factual history reconstructed from the repository's own records \n (taskboard, decision records, forensic reports). No invented narrative. \n Phase I — Engine core (single-agent era) \n The original engine: hexagonal architecture, MT5 adapters, 50D causal features, \n ScalpNet, policy matrix, risk engine, order manager, SQLite WAL ledger, \n FastAPI Control Center. Foundation invariants established: no sync DB on the \n tick path, no order authority for learning components. \n Phase II — Multi-agent forensic era \n Development moved to a  multi-agent model  (up to 56+ parallel AI agents) with \n a strict engineering contract: taskboard, locks, bug ledger, runtime invariants, \n change control. The bug ledger (BUG-001…) and forensic acceptance reports date \n from this era. Key products: database hygiene, migrations, incident respons"}, {"u": "/es/project/roadmap/", "t": "Roadmap [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Proyecto  /  Hoja de ruta  \n Disciplina de redacción: los ítems son  Planificado ,  En evaluación ,  Dirección de investigación  o  Completado  — nunca \"próximamente\", nunca garantizado. \n AHORA (activo) \n  \n   Flujo  Ítem  Estado    \n  VALIDACIÓN  Reconstruir la evidencia del candidato 70D (semántica de confianza corregida, CHG-0042)  En evaluación  \n  INVESTIGACIÓN  Profundizar la evidencia contrafactual (CHG-0041)  En progreso  \n  ARQUITECTURA  Descomposición de archivos grandes con tests dorados (CHG-0032-A1)  En progreso  \n  RUNTIME  Endurecimiento del contrato de constructores de registros (BUG-185)  Completado  \n   \n DESPUÉS \n  \n   Flujo  Ítem  Dependencias    \n  ML  Decisión de promoción 70D — operada, o retiro honesto  candidato validado + verificación de 14 puertas  \n  VALIDACIÓN  Revisión de política guiada por contrafactuales  salidas contrafactuales  \n  DOCS  100% de cober"}, {"u": "/es/project/scope/", "t": "Scope [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Proyecto  /  Alcance  \n Scope \n In scope \n \n A complete quantitative trading  pipeline : data adapters (MT5/paper/gateway), \n \n causal feature engineering (50D active contract; 60D/70D research family), \n deep model inference (ScalpNet TCN + self-attention), SMC policy matrix, \n invariant risk engine, execution with 60-scenario router, SQLite WAL \n accounting ledger, experience/autopsy intelligence, research &amp; validation \n (walk-forward, OOS gate, robustness), replay and shadow runtimes, model \n governance, observability (structured logs, incidents, forensics, Telegram), \n FastAPI Control Center UI, packaged Windows release + installer + update/rollback. \n \n  Multi-agent engineering memory : architecture map, bug ledger, runtime \n \n invariants, contracts, taskboard, decision records — treated as first-class \n repository artifacts. \n Out of scope (by design) \n \n Multi-broker support"}, {"u": "/es/project/status/", "t": "Project Status [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Proyecto  /  Estado del proyecto  \n Estado del proyecto \n  IMPORTANTE  Las etiquetas se gradúan por evidencia. «Implementado» = existe en código y  está cubierto por pruebas. «Certificado» = además con aceptación forense  formal. Aquí no se promete rentabilidad.  \n Instantánea \n  \n   Dimensión  Estado  Evidencia    \n  Versión   9.0.6  (semver, fuente única  pyproject.toml )  pipeline de releases  \n  Release   Publicado  (v9.0.0 → v9.0.6; SHA-256, manifiestos, SBOM)  GitHub Releases  \n  Runtime  Endurecido; PAPER por defecto; LIVE con confirmación explícita  contrato CLI + doctor  \n  Ejecución en vivo  Funcional (MT5 Win32 IPC + gateway ZMQ) con fail-safe de identidad de cuenta  regresión BUG-142  \n  Ciclo de investigación  De extremo a extremo (datasets → walk-forward → puerta OOS)  suites research/  \n  Contrato en vivo 50D ( scalp_v1 )   ACTIVO    features/schema.py   \n  Contrato 70D "}, {"u": "/es/project/vision/", "t": "Vision & Why [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Proyecto  /  Visión y propósito  \n Visión — por qué Nexus \n El problema \n Los proyectos de trading algorítmico suelen fracasar de dos maneras: \n \n  Ocultan la verdad.  Métricas fabricadas, fallos silenciosos y la brecha \n \n entre backtest y runtime nunca se mide. \n \n  Filtran el futuro.  Características o etiquetas usan información no \n \n disponible en el momento de la decisión — resultados estructuralmente \n inválidos. \n Nexus Scalp Engine se construyó contra ambos modos de fallo: un **pipeline \n completo y auditable** — datos de mercado → características → modelo → \n política → riesgo → ejecución → contabilidad → investigación — donde cada etapa \n es observable, cada identidad está empañetada (fingerprint) y cada afirmación \n es falsable. \n Filosofía (respaldada por el repositorio) \n \n  Evidencia antes que afirmaciones.  Métricas sin evidencia se muestran \n \n  n/a  — nunca ceros fals"}, {"u": "/es/reference/cli-reference/", "t": "CLI Reference [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Referencia  /  Referencia CLI  \n CLI Reference \n The authoritative surface is always  nexus help  /  nexus &lt;command&gt; --help  \n (this page documents the verified contract; the CLI is golden-tested by 66 \n end-to-end tests). \n Global flags \n  \n   Flag  Effect    \n   --json   machine-readable output (parity-tested keys)  \n   --plain   no color, no formatting  \n   --no-color   disable color only  \n   \n Command groups \n  \n   Command  Purpose  Notes    \n  `nexus start [--mode paper\\  shadow\\  live] [--port N] [--daemon]`  run engine  paper default; live needs interactive  --yes /confirmation; port default 8080  \n   nexus stop  /  nexus restart   daemon control  pidfile-based; dead-pid reported honestly (BUG-172)  \n   nexus doctor   19-category diagnostics + suggested fixes   --json  for tooling  \n   nexus status  /  nexus health   environment + health  READY / DEGRADED / NOT READY  \n  "}, {"u": "/es/reference/faq/", "t": "FAQ [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Referencia  /  FAQ  \n FAQ \n  ¿Qué es Nexus?  \n Una plataforma de trading cuantitativo basada en investigación: motor de scalping hexagonal y dirigido por eventos para MetaTrader 5 (XAUUSD M1) con características causales, modelos profundos, riesgo invariante, investigación determinista y observabilidad forense. \n  ¿Es un bot de trading en vivo?  \n Puede ejecutar operaciones en vivo — pero PAPER es el modo por defecto, SHADOW no tiene autoridad de órdenes, LIVE exige confirmación interactiva explícita y el repositorio publica candidatos rechazados. Es una plataforma de investigación con un runtime, no una máquina de dinero. \n  ¿Puedo ejecutarlo sin MT5?  \n Sí — el modo PAPER y la suite completa de tests corren sin bróker; Docker funciona de serie en modo PAPER. \n  ¿Qué es 70D?  \n El contrato de características canónico de investigación (50 base + 10 noticias + 10 liquidez). No está en v"}, {"u": "/es/reference/glossary/", "t": "Glossary [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Referencia  /  Glosario  \n Glossary \n Project-specific terms. Product/module names (Nexus, ScalpNet, OrderManager, \n MT5, 70D, 50D) are canonical and never translated in code; each language's \n  terminology file  defines how they are presented. \n  \n   Term  Meaning in NSE    \n   50D / scalp_v1   the 50-dimensional causal base feature contract — the ACTIVE live feature schema  \n   70D / scalp_v3   the canonical research feature contract: Base 50 (0..49) + News 10 (50..59) + Liquidity 10 (60..69); candidate-only, not live  \n   scalp_v4   a candidate 70D-family contract (integration-era); classified LEGACY/semantically-different vs v3  \n   Schema hash   SHA-256 over canonical JSON of feature (index, name, family) — reordering invalidates models  \n   ScalpNet   dual-path model: 2D MLP for single-tick snapshots, 3D TCN + self-attention for sequences; 4-logit head  \n   Champion / Challenger "}, {"u": "/es/reference/terminology/", "t": "Terminology & Translations [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Referencia  /  Terminología y traducciones  \n Terminology &amp; Translations \n Untranslatable canon \n These stay in English/Latin script in every language (identifiers, contracts, \n product names): \n `Nexus · ScalpNet · OrderManager · RiskEngine · LiveEngine · IMT5Port · \n AuditRepository · MT5 · ZMQ · SQLite · FastAPI · 50D · 70D · scalp_v1 · \n scalp_v3 · NO_TRADE · BUY · SELL · WAIT · Champion · Challenger · Shadow · \n OOS · walk-forward · O(1) · MFE · MAE` \n Canonical term translations \n The authoritative per-language table lives in \n  site/terminology/&lt;lang&gt;.json  (consumed by the translation audit). Core \n entries: \n  \n   EN  FA (فارسی)  ES  AR (العربية)  DE    \n  Feature Vector  بردار ویژگی  Vector de características  متجه السمات  Merkmalsvektor  \n  Feature Contract  قرارداد ویژگی  Contrato de características  عقد السمات  Merkmalsvertrag  \n  Model Registry  ثبت مدل  Registr"}, {"u": "/es/research/backtesting/", "t": "Backtesting [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Investigación  /  Backtesting  \n Backtesting \n Determinism \n Backtests ( research/backtest.py ) are deterministic: fixed seeds, frozen \n datasets, no wall-clock dependence. Same inputs ⇒ same results. \n Friction model \n Spread, slippage and latency are modeled, not ignored: \n \n fills on historical bid/ask (direction-aware), \n tick-level SL/TP first-touch resolution, \n logical latency applied to the decision path, \n robustness stress re-runs under degraded friction (spread/slippage/latency \n \n shocks) — a strategy that only works under ideal fills does not pass. \n Boundary honesty \n \n Backtests produce evidence, not promises. Results feed the validation \n \n pipeline; they never bypass the OOS gate. \n \n Fees/commissions follow the configured friction profile; metrics without the \n \n underlying evidence render  n/a  — never fabricated zeros. \n \n Streaming replay ( research/streaming_repla"}, {"u": "/es/research/counterfactuals/", "t": "Counterfactuals [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Investigación  /  Contrafactuales  \n Counterfactuals (CHG-0041) \n The question \n Backtests score trades that happened. The counterfactual engine asks the \n other question: **what would have happened on the decisions the engine did NOT \n take?** If the engine abstains (NO_TRADE), was the abstention valuable? \n How it works \n  research/counterfactual.py : \n \n Loads canonical tick datasets (fingerprinted, offline) and decision \n \n snapshots from  audit_signals . \n \n Joins each NO_TRADE decision to the tick window at decision time. \n Applies  certified fill semantics  hypothetically at time T. \n Walks ticks forward to compute MFE / MAE / R / cost / time-to-target. \n Classifies each abstention using  documented rules  (never ad-hoc). \n Stratifies evidence by gate, regime, confidence, session, direction. \n \n First evidence run (2026-09-01) \n 2095 NO_TRADE decisions (2026-08-24 → 09-01) walke"}, {"u": "/es/research/datasets/", "t": "Datasets [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Investigación  /  Datasets  \n Datasets \n Bar datasets \n Built by  research/dataset.py  +  model_generation/  with quality gates \n (coverage, ordering, duplicates, horizon boundaries). Each dataset is a \n versioned artifact with a fingerprint ( ds_*  id) used in manifests and run \n snapshots. \n Tick datasets (CHG-0041 / TICK_DATASET_META v2) \n  research/mt5_tick_dataset.py  acquires ticks from the **certified adapter \n surface** ( copy_ticks_range ,  COPY_TICKS_ALL ), with: \n \n bounded, deduplicated acquisition (post BUG-188 semantics), \n immutable parquet store with  content fingerprints , \n provenance metadata v2 (symbol, window, source, acquisition identity), \n cache-hit idempotence — re-running acquisition never duplicates. \n \n After acquisition the dataset is fully  offline : research needs no broker. \n Rules \n \n A dataset is immutable once fingerprinted — corrections produce a new"}, {"u": "/es/research/methodology/", "t": "Research Methodology [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Investigación  /  Metodología  \n La investigación existe para producir  evidencia falsable . Un candidato que no puede ser falsado (sin OOS, sin paridad de replay, sin procedencia) nunca toca la ruta en vivo. \n La cadena \n  ⧉   DATOS (datasets con huella) → CARACTERÍSTICAS (contrato causal) → ETIQUETADO (triple-barrera)\n→ ENTRENAMIENTO (con semilla, determinista) → BACKTEST (con fricción)\n→ WALK-FORWARD (purgado + embargo) → PUERTA OOS (fallo ⇒ RECHAZADO)\n→ ESTRÉS DE ROBUSTEZ → CONTRAFACTUAL → REGISTRO → SHADOW → PROMOCIÓN OPERADA   \n Componentes \n \n  Datasets  — inmutables, con huella, procedencia rastreada; los datasets de ticks se adquieren por la superficie de adaptador certificada y quedan offline tras la adquisición. \n  Backtests  — deterministas; spread/slippage/latencia modelados. \n  Replay  — bit-exacto vs dataset (tests anti-fuga); el replay en streaming ejecuta el motor comp"}, {"u": "/es/research/out-of-sample/", "t": "Out-of-Sample Gate [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Investigación  /  Puerta OOS  \n Out-of-Sample (OOS) Gate \n Contract \n  research/oos.py  is a  hard gate : out-of-sample failure ⇒ candidate \n REJECTED, regardless of in-sample performance. There is no override path in \n the pipeline. \n Floors (model lifecycle validation) \n  \n   Metric  Floor    \n  macro-F1 (OOS)  ≥ 0.34  \n  balanced accuracy  ≥ 0.34  \n  calibration error (ECE)  ≤ 0.15  \n  minimum evidence  ≥ 100 rows  \n   \n Evidence the gate bites \n The 70D liquidity candidate — the most heavily engineered research series in \n the repository — was rejected by this exact gate (OOS NOT_ELIGIBLE) after \n real-data walk-forward and shadow benchmarks came back negative/inconclusive. \n A gate that rejects nothing is decoration; this one has a public rejection on \n its record. See  Project Status  and \n  docs/TASK-05-70D-SHADOW-FINAL.md . \n Temporal OOS protocol \n Temporal splits only ( times"}, {"u": "/es/research/replay/", "t": "Replay [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Investigación  /  Replay  \n Replay \n What replay is \n Replay re-runs the engine's decision logic over historical data and proves it \n produces  the same decisions  the live/training pipeline produced on that \n data. It is the execution-fidelity check between research and runtime. \n Two engines \n  \n   Engine  Module  Character    \n  Dataset replay   model_generation/replay.py  +  replay_70d_vector    bit-exact : replay vector must equal the dataset's stored vector (anti-leakage tests)  \n  Streaming replay   research/streaming_replay.py  (CHG-0035)  shared  LiveEngine  over a logical clock (zero sleeps): incremental bar aggregation, causal 50D + news + liquidity at time T, frozen policy + RiskEngine, direction-aware simulated fills on historical bid/ask, tick SL/TP first-touch, ledger MFE/MAE —  NO  order_send  (test-enforced)   \n   \n Anti-leakage \n Features at time T may consume only in"}, {"u": "/es/research/reproducibility/", "t": "Reproducibility [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Investigación  /  Reproducibilidad  \n Reproducibility \n Identity chain \n Every research artifact carries the chain that produced it: \n  ⧉   dataset fingerprint → feature schema hash → model manifest (scaler, weights)\n→ git commit → effective config (seeds, splits, purge/embargo)   \n Run snapshots ( research_run_snapshots ) store these at run time; provenance \n fields may be  NOT_RECORDED  (honest) but are never invented or backfilled. \n Determinism sources \n \n seeded training (seed-before-model construction — BUG-101 regression), \n frozen datasets (immutable, fingerprinted), \n logical-clock streaming replay (zero sleeps), \n freeze capture at forward-test cutoff +  post-run re-verification  of the \n \n freeze ( research/forward_test.py ). \n What breaks reproducibility (and is therefore guarded) \n  \n   Threat  Guard    \n  dataset mutation  immutable fingerprinted artifacts  \n  feature reo"}, {"u": "/es/research/validation/", "t": "Validation [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Investigación  /  Validación  \n La validación es la razón de ser de la plataforma. Un fallo en cualquier puerta es terminal para ese candidato — sin promedios, sin excepciones. \n La cadena de puertas \n  \n   Capa  Puertas    \n  Dataset  puertas de calidad · huella · procedencia  \n  Características  hash de esquema · dimensión · límites · orden  \n  Modelo  puerta de carga de 10 pasos · calibración · evidencia mínima  \n  Investigación  walk-forward purgado/con embargo · pisos OOS · robustez  \n  Gobernanza  verificación de 14 puertas · transacción de promoción  \n  Runtime  puerta de despliegue forense antes de cada release  \n  Release  SHA-256 · manifiestos · SBOM · verificación posterior  \n   \n Pisos OOS (ciclo de vida del modelo) \n macro-F1 ≥ 0.34 · exactitud balanceada ≥ 0.34 · ECE ≤ 0.15 · evidencia ≥ 100 filas. \n La puerta muerde — prueba pública \n El candidato de liquidez 70D — la se"}, {"u": "/es/research/walk-forward/", "t": "Walk-Forward [es]", "l": "es", "x": "  Investigación  /  Walk-Forward  \n Walk-Forward \n Method \n  training/walk_forward_trainer.py  +  research/walkforward.py  implement \n  purged, embargoed walk-forward  (Lopez de Prado): training folds are \n separated from test folds by a purge gap (label horizon) and an embargo gap \n (serial-correlation buffer), evaluated across temporally ordered folds. \n Defaults that matter (BUG-183) \n The production research path once ran with purge/embargo silently disabled — \n the constants existed but weren't wired. This is recorded as BUG-183 and fixed \n with regression tests:  DEFAULT_PURGE_SECONDS = 300 , `DEFAULT_EMBARGO_SECONDS \n = 60  are now wired into  ResearchPipeline.validate_candidate`, \n  OOSGate.evaluate ,  WalkForwardEngine.validate  and  BacktestEngine.run , and \n the  effective  purge/embargo values are recorded in every run's config. \n Why it is non-negotiable \n A walk-forward wit"}, {"u": "/es/getting-started/", "t": "Inicio [es]", "l": "es", "x": "Install, run and configure the engine. PAPER mode is the default; SHADOW gives you live data with zero order authority."}, {"u": "/es/project/", "t": "Proyecto [es]", "l": "es", "x": "What Nexus is, what is certified vs experimental, where it is going — all evidence-graded."}, {"u": "/es/architecture/", "t": "Arquitectura [es]", "l": "es", "x": "How the engine is built: hexagonal layers, the tick-to-decision path, model governance, and the intelligence loop."}, {"u": "/es/research/", "t": "Investigación [es]", "l": "es", "x": "How historical data becomes falsifiable evidence — datasets, backtests, walk-forward, OOS, replay, counterfactuals."}, {"u": "/es/engineering/", "t": "Ingeniería [es]", "l": "es", "x": "Quality gates, CI architecture, the release process, and the security posture."}, {"u": "/es/guides/", "t": "Guías [es]", "l": "es", "x": "Operating the engine day to day: CLI, REST API, troubleshooting, common workflows."}, {"u": "/es/contributing/", "t": "Contribuir [es]", "l": "es", "x": "The engineering contract, documentation ownership, and how to add a language."}, {"u": "/es/reference/", "t": "Referencia [es]", "l": "es", "x": "CLI reference, glossary, terminology, and honest answers in the FAQ."}, {"u": "/de/", "t": "Home [de]", "l": "de", "x": "Nexus Scalp Engine documentation homepage what's new capabilities architecture research"}, {"u": "/de/releases/", "t": "Releases [de]", "l": "de", "x": "releases v9.0.8 changelog what's new history 959d7d9"}, {"u": "/de/architecture/code-navigation/", "t": "Code Navigation Map — Nexus Scalp Engine [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Architektur  /  code navigation  \n Code Navigation Map — Nexus Scalp Engine \n  Where to find things, for a developer (or agent) landing fresh in this repo.  This map is an INDEX. Detailed truth lives in:  -  agents/skill.md  — authoritative architecture map + repo contract (READ FIRST)  -  docs/architecture/dependency-map.md  — subsystem edges + contracts  -  docs/architecture/comment-style.md  — comment/doc conventions  -  docs/RELEASE.md  — CLI exit codes, update protocol, release verification  -  agents/bugs.md  — bug ledger (append-only; grep  ^## BUG-  tail for next free id)  \n Startup &amp; lifecycle \n  \n   Concern  Where    \n  Primary launcher (bootstrap sys.path, adapter bind, engine + web)   NexusTradingForexBot.py   \n  CLI entry ( nexus  /  nse , Typer)   src/nexus_scalp/cli/main.py   \n  Engine construction + async tick loop   src/nexus_scalp/application/live_engine.py  ( run"}, {"u": "/de/architecture/comment-style/", "t": "Comment Style Guide — Nexus Scalp Engine [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Architektur  /  comment style  \n Comment Style Guide — Nexus Scalp Engine \n  Applies to all Python source in  src/ ,  tests/ , and  scripts/ .  Repo rule of thumb:  the repository should not contain more comments — it should contain better comments.   \n The one test \n  Could a competent developer derive this from the code itself?  \n If YES → do not comment. If NO → the comment may be valuable; then ask: \n \"Will this still be true and useful six months from now?\" If NO → do not write it. \n What comments are FOR \n A comment must be one of: \n  \n   Category  Documents  Example    \n  INVARIANT  a rule the code must keep but does not enforce visibly  \"Resume-safe hash: the hasher must cover the already-downloaded bytes too.\"  \n  SAFETY  fail-closed / fail-safe semantics  \"Fail closed: no inference must never yield a trade decision.\"  \n  CONCURRENCY  lock ownership, ordering, atomicity  \"Hold"}, {"u": "/de/architecture/control-center-ui/", "t": "Control Center UI Architecture (CHG-0043, TASK-CONTROL-CENTER) [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Architektur  /  control center ui  \n Control Center UI Architecture (CHG-0043, TASK-CONTROL-CENTER) \n  Operator-facing architecture of the NEXUS Control Center. UI-owned doc;  backend architecture lives in  docs/architecture/  elsewhere. Status  semantics here are the CONTRACT for every future CC view.  \n Purpose \n One coherent surface where an operator answers, without reading logs: \n WHAT is happening → WHY → WHAT changed → WHAT is blocked → WHAT is healthy → \n WHAT is serving → WHY did/didn't a trade happen → WHAT is safe to do next. \n Observation model: OBSERVE → UNDERSTAND → INVESTIGATE → ACT → VERIFY. \n Navigation &amp; Screens \n  \n   Tab (nav id)  Screen  Data sources (all read-only)    \n  Control Center ( tab-control-center )  Overview: mode banner, 6-tile status strip (Runtime/Data/Model/Inference/Database/MT5), runtime truth, market snapshot, latest decision, active warnings "}, {"u": "/de/architecture/crash-safety/", "t": "Crash-Safety Architecture (NSE) [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Architektur  /  crash safety  \n Crash-Safety Architecture (NSE) \n  Status: HARDENED_WITH_GAPS baseline documented 2026-09-01 (rev 2 — checker  regex fix + 381-site silent-handler backlog tracked as P1 violations).  Owner: Nexus-Main (crash-containment master pass).  Scope: the failure contract of every major execution boundary, from process  startup through model tensor execution, trading execution, Web/API, updater,  release pipeline, and shutdown.  Companion documents:  failure-recovery-matrix.md  (per-subsystem failure  matrix),  artifacts/forensics/crash-safety-audit.json  (machine audit).  \n \n 1. Governing principle \n The requirement is NOT \"the application must never crash\". The requirement is: \n  ⧉   NO SILENT CRASH      NO SILENT EXCEPTION      NO FALSE SUCCESS\nNO FAKE HEALTH       NO FABRICATED MODEL OUTPUT\nNO UNSAFE TRADING AFTER CRITICAL FAILURE\nNO CORRUPTED STATE AFTER FAIL"}, {"u": "/de/architecture/data-flow/", "t": "Data Flow — Tick to Decision [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Architektur  /  Datenfluss  \n Data Flow — from tick to decision \n This is the canonical path (from  agents/skill.md  §4). Every arrow is a \n contract boundary. \n  ⧉   TickData (MT5 / paper / gateway)\n  → ScalpFeatureEngine.to_tensor_input()\n      50D base (scalp_v1 · FEATURE_NAMES · [-3,+3] · finite)\n  → assemble_70d / build_70d_vector()\n      70D canonical: Base 0..49 | News 10D 50..59 | Liquidity 10D 60..69\n  → InferenceContractValidator\n      scaler dim == feature dim · schema hash · finite · bounds\n  → ScalpNet → 4 logits (NO_TRADE / BUY / SELL / WAIT) → confidence gate 0.35\n  → regime_classifier (Regime Guardian)\n  → signals/policy + rule_matrix (~30 rules, TTL 5s cache)\n  → RiskEngine.calculate_dynamic_volume() + evaluate_proposal()\n      free-margin 20% clamp · tier caps · HARD_MAX_LOTS\n  → OrderManager (60-scenario router · 11 position states ·\n      MAX_TOTAL_EXPOSURE=1 · 30s "}, {"u": "/de/architecture/database/", "t": "Database Architecture [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Architektur  /  Datenbank  \n Database Architecture \n Canonical stores \n  \n   DB  Contents  Notes    \n   artifacts/audit.db   trading ledger, experience outcomes, accounting, research registry, strategy lifecycle, incidents, hygiene  one canonical ledger; SQLite  WAL   \n   artifacts/news.db   news ingestion, analysis, consensus, impacts  lazy schema on first save  \n   candle_intel.db   candle intelligence  versioned schema  \n  settings DB  secrets + user intent (Telegram creds via  settings_service )  never in YAML (INV-010)  \n   \n Write path \n  AuditRepository  queues writes to a  background worker thread  — the tick \n hot path never performs synchronous DB work (INV-001). Historical \n experience/outcome/ledger rows are  immutable  (INV-007); corrections go \n through evidence → reconstruction → derived records with provenance, never row \n rewrites. \n Migrations \n  src/nexus_scalp/datab"}, {"u": "/de/architecture/dependency-map/", "t": "Architecture Dependency Map — Nexus Scalp Engine (NSE) [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Architektur  /  dependency map  \n Architecture Dependency Map — Nexus Scalp Engine (NSE) \n  Maintained per the MASTER MULTI-AGENT CONTRACT §9 (see  agents/multi-agent-git-contract.md ).  Describes actual subsystem relationships (verified against executable code; see agents/skill.md for the full inventory).  Every edge documents: contract, direction, expected data, safety guarantees.  \n Canonical high-level flow \n  ⧉   MT5\n  │  (tick/order/position/account events)\n  ▼\nMT5 Adapter / Providers            [ports: IMT5Port; adapters: mt5/, paper/, remote]\n  │  (normalized events)\n  ▼\nLiveEngine (async event loop)      [src/nexus_scalp/application/live_engine.py]\n  ├─ Feature Engine                [features/scalp_features.py → FEATURE_VECTOR_50D]\n  ├─ Model Runtime                 [models/scalp_net.py → MODEL_MANIFEST; Champion/Challenger]\n  ├─ News Context                  [news/ → NEWS_CON"}, {"u": "/de/architecture/execution-pipeline/", "t": "Execution Pipeline [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Architektur  /  Ausführungspipeline  \n Execution Pipeline \n  execution/order_manager.py  is the single dispatch authority (INV-004). It is \n large by design (convention-locked hot path) and is being decomposed \n surgically, seam by seam, with golden tests. \n Path of an order \n  ⧉   TradeProposal (frozen domain contract, execution_id trace)\n  → policy/confluence checks (SMC matrix, Regime Guardian, confidence gate)\n  → RiskEngine.evaluate_proposal() → dynamic volume (fractional Kelly)\n  → OrderManager router (60 scenarios: fills, rejections, partials, errors)\n  → IMT5Port adapter (Win32 IPC / ZMQ / paper)\n  → position lifecycle (11 states with hysteresis)\n  → protective exits (SL/TP first-touch, breakeven lock, profit giveback,\n      adaptive exit protection)\n  → broker reconciliation (broker truth wins — INV-011)\n  → accounting + autopsy (immutable ledger)   \n Hard clamps (never bypass"}, {"u": "/de/architecture/failure-recovery-matrix/", "t": "Failure-Recovery Matrix (NSE crash-containment pass) [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Architektur  /  failure recovery matrix  \n Failure-Recovery Matrix (NSE crash-containment pass) \n  Status: baseline 2026-09-01. Companion to  crash-safety.md  and   artifacts/forensics/crash-safety-audit.json .  Every row = subsystem × failure → expected console log, state, recovery,  exit, and the test that proves it. GREEN means failure-injected → detected →  logged → safe behavior → regression exists (never \"a try/except exists\").  \n Legend — State: truthful runtime state after the failure. Log: minimum \n console/file record. Rec: recovery policy. Exit: CLI/process exit contract. \n Test: primary regression evidence. \n  \n   #  Subsystem  Failure  Log (console)  State  Rec  Exit  Test    \n  1  startup  missing/invalid config at launch  red panel  cfg_detail=Parse error…  + doctor FAIL  NOT READY  halt  1 / EXIT_RUNTIME  launcher doctor contract; BUG-149/156 lineage  \n  2  startup   _p"}, {"u": "/de/architecture/model-pipeline/", "t": "Model Pipeline [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Architektur  /  Modellpipeline  \n Model Pipeline \n Lifecycle \n  ⧉   DATASET (versioned artifact + quality gates + fingerprint)\n  → EXPERIMENT (equal budgets/seeds/splits; dataset-fairness gate)\n  → CANDIDATE MODEL (+ manifest: schema hash · scaler · dataset ID · git commit)\n  → VALIDATION (walk-forward · OOS gate · robustness · calibration)\n  → REGISTRY (content-addressed; challenger only)\n  → LOAD GATE (10 gates, enforced at every attach)\n  → SHADOW PARITY (zero order authority)\n  → OPERATOR PROMOTION (READY_FOR_REVIEW → APPROVED → CHAMPION; atomic transaction)\n  → ROLLBACK PREVIEW / EMERGENCY FREEZE   \n Artifact-first Model Factory ( model_generation/ ) \n Datasets, experiments and models are **versioned filesystem artifacts with \n manifests** — inference needs no database. The manifest carries \n  feature_schema_hash ,  training_dataset_id , scaler identity and git commit. \n ScalpNet "}, {"u": "/de/architecture/observability-log-contract/", "t": "Observability Log Contract — frozen 2026-09-01 (Agent 2) [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Architektur  /  observability log contract  \n Observability Log Contract — frozen 2026-09-01 (Agent 2) \n Authoritative in-repo reference for the log-noise contracts proven in the \n operational-observability sprint and pinned by \n  tests/unit/test_operational_log_hygiene.py  + \n  tests/unit/test_observability_contract_freeze.py  + \n  tests/unit/test_logging_redaction.py . \n Any future change to these behaviors MUST update those tests in the same \n commit (test-first rule: a new repetitive runtime event needs an \n aggregation/transition/rate-limit test before merge). \n Companion tooling:  src/nexus_scalp/observability/event_aggregator.py  \n (EventBatchAggregator — bounded, thread-safe, first-occurrence-immediate). \n \n Core invariants (all events) \n \n SEVERITY ladder: DEBUG = diagnostic detail; INFO = normal state / bounded \n \n informational transitions; WARNING = first failure or actiona"}, {"u": "/de/architecture/observability-map/", "t": "Observability Map — Nexus Scalp Engine (NSE) [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Architektur  /  observability map  \n Observability Map — Nexus Scalp Engine (NSE) \n  TASK-OBS-AUDIT (2026-08-31, HEAD baseline 1f60832; delivered at dcc80d7).  Agent: Hermes-ObsForensic. AUDIT-ONLY: zero runtime code changed.  Machine-readable companion:  artifacts/forensics/observability-audit.json .  Method: black-box reconstruction from runtime evidence (logs / DBs / artifacts /  live API / CLI) FIRST, then targeted read-only code sweeps for every claim.  Evidence markers: [L]=live-probed today, [DB]=DB census, [LOG]=log sample, [C]=code file:line.  \n 1. What the system actually produces today \n  \n   Channel  Reality (verified)    \n  Logs  severity-split  logs/{critical,error,warning,info}/YYYY/MM/*.log , ISO-8601  +03:30 , 10 MB part rotation, retention 30/30/90/365 d [C observability/logging.py:388-394]. Only 08-29 + 08-31 exist; 08-30 absent. ~190 MB on 08-31 (131 MB error).  \n  "}, {"u": "/de/architecture/observability/", "t": "Observability [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Architektur  /  Observability  \n Observability \n NSE treats observability as a subsystem with contracts, not a logging afterthought. \n If the engine cannot show  why  it did something, its behavior is indistinguishable \n from a bug — so showing why is engineered, not hoped for. \n Structured logging ( observability/logging.py ) \n \n Severity-split, date-organized storage:  logs/&lt;sev&gt;/YYYY/MM/YYYY-MM-DD.log . \n ISO-8601 timestamps (broker-local offset aware), event/component/category/ \n \n error-code fields, correlation context. \n \n Daily + size rotation with zero-loss part files; per-severity retention. \n Key + high-entropy redaction; ANSI-free stacks. \n \n Incident response ( incidents/ ) \n Canonical incident model ( INC-YYYY-hex8 , 8 statuses, 5 severities), \n fingerprint correlation, causal-chain timeline reconstruction, value lineage \n with first-divergence location, WHY workflow"}, {"u": "/de/architecture/order_manager_architecture/", "t": "ORDER_MANAGER.PY — Architectural Map (Agent-5, Phase A) [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Architektur  /  order manager architecture  \n ORDER_MANAGER.PY — Architectural Map (Agent-5, Phase A) \n Evidence base: forensic inventory at HEAD  0015608  (post Agent-4 winner-protection \n sprint  0839da3 ). No edits made during this phase. This document precedes any \n extraction (task brief §24). \n 1. Current shape \n 6372 LOC, 1 god class + 6 support types \n  \n   Item  Span  Notes    \n  Module constants (18)  L60-155  exposure caps, BE/giveback/trailing geometry  \n  ExitMechanism (Enum)  L158  exit taxonomy  \n  PositionState (Enum)  L172  11 in-trade lifecycles  \n  PositionEvaluationStep  L190  trajectory step record  \n  LSFTicketState  L209  LSF per-ticket state  \n  PositionProtectionState  L226  per-ticket protection facts (dataclass)  \n  SmartPositionMetrics  L281  57 derived metrics (dataclass)  \n  OrderLifecycleManager  L348-6372  81 methods, 99 distinct  self.*  state attrs  \n "}, {"u": "/de/architecture/overview/", "t": "Architecture Overview [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Architektur  /  Überblick  \n NSE ist  hexagonal (Ports-and-Adapters) und ereignisgesteuert : Broker-Plattformen, Modelle und Netzwerkadapter liegen hinter Port-Verträgen ( IMT5Port ,  IGatewayPort ); die Domain weiß nie, welcher Broker angeschlossen ist. \n  ⧉   Marktdaten (MT5 / ZMQ / paper)\n  → Kausale Features — 50D-Basis (scalp_v1) · gesteuerte 70D-Assemblierung\n  → Inferenz-Validator — Schema-Hash · Scaler-Dim · Grenzen (lautablehnend)\n  → ScalpNet (TCN + Self-Attention) — 4 Logits → Confidence-Gate\n  → Regime-Wächter → SMC-Policy-Matrix (~30 Regeln)\n  → Risikomotor (Kelly-Sizing · Marge ≤20% · Tier-Kappen · HARD_MAX_LOTS=10)\n  → OrderManager (60-Szenario-Router · 11 Positionsstände · atomares Teardown)\n  → IMT5Port-Adapter → MT5 / paper / shadow (null Order-Autorität)\n  → Buchhaltung (unveränderliches SQLite-WAL) → Erfahrung &amp; Autopsie\n  → Observability (Logs · Incidents · For"}, {"u": "/de/architecture/qa-assurance-contract/", "t": "QA ASSURANCE CONTRACT — Deep Assurance Layer (CHG-0045) [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Architektur  /  qa assurance contract  \n QA ASSURANCE CONTRACT — Deep Assurance Layer (CHG-0045) \n  Owner: Nexus-Main (TASK-QA-DEEP-ASSURANCE). This document is the contract  for the OSS-grade adversarial QA layer: lanes, markers, budgets, the JSON  result schema, and the governance rules for flaky/open-defect tests.  \n 1. Position in the gate hierarchy \n  \n   Lane  Command  When  Budget    \n  Pre-push critical gate (existing, NOT replaced)   beforePush.sh  /  check_local.py   every push  ~2.5 min  \n   Deep assurance — fast    python scripts/qa/deep_assurance.py --fast   PR / push lane in CI  &lt; 60 s  \n   Deep assurance — full    python scripts/qa/deep_assurance.py   main / scheduled / dispatch  &lt; 5 min  \n  Mutation proof   python scripts/qa/run_mutations.py   scheduled / dispatch (weekly)  &lt; 15 min  \n   \n The deep-assurance layer NEVER replaces the runtime gate; it adds \n inde"}, {"u": "/de/architecture/QA_BLIND_SPOT_MATRIX/", "t": "QA BLIND-SPOT MATRIX — Nexus Scalp Engine [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Architektur  /  QA BLIND SPOT MATRIX  \n QA BLIND-SPOT MATRIX — Nexus Scalp Engine \n  CHG-0045 / TASK-QA-DEEP-ASSURANCE (Nexus-Main, 2026-09-02).  Required first milestone of the OSS-grade adversarial QA brief: prove which  gaps matter BEFORE building test mass. Derived from  agents/bugs.md   (BUG-001..BUG-208) and  agents/change_control.md  (CHG-0001..CHG-0050).  \n 1. Method \n \n  Defect-history mining  — every BUG/CHG row classified by subsystem, \n \n severity (P0 money/execution · P1 decision-path/trust · P2 operator \n trust/diagnostics · P3 robustness), and named regression test. \n \n  Detection-quality audit  — does the named regression test the ROOT \n \n CAUSE or only the incident's symptom path? \n \n  Re-entry analysis  — can the same class return through another door? \n  Verdict  — KEEP / IMPROVE / MERGE / DELETE / MISSING per test family. \n \n 2. Matrix — defect history → detection →"}, {"u": "/de/architecture/repository-hygiene/", "t": "Repository Hygiene Audit — Nexus Scalp Engine [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Architektur  /  repository hygiene  \n Repository Hygiene Audit — Nexus Scalp Engine \n   Date:  2026-08-31 ·  HEAD:   1f60832  (main) ·  Working tree:  UNCHANGED (0 modifications)   Mode:  READ-ONLY forensic librarian pass. Nothing was fixed, moved, deleted, or refactored.   Machine-readable twin:   artifacts/forensics/repository-hygiene-audit.json    2026-08-31 repair pass:  CLEANUP-001/002/003/004/005/006 repaired — networkx declared as runtime dep, psycopg declared via new  postgres  extra, requirements ranges reconciled to pyproject, skill.md runner path fixed, tick_storage.py removed, 32 e2e_cc files archived to  scratch/e2e_cc_archive/ , .pyproj.bak removed.   Scope guard:  excludes all active-agent work (BUG-166..174, anti-crash, decomposition, release).  \n 1. What was analyzed \n \n 1,621 tracked files (724 py / 625 md / 80 json / 22 js / 16 mjs / 15 ps1 / 10 yml) \n 351 Python sou"}, {"u": "/de/architecture/research-stack/", "t": "Research Stack [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Architektur  /  Forschungsstack  \n Research Stack \n The research side answers one question with evidence: **is this candidate good \n enough to trust — and can we prove it on data it never saw?** \n Pipeline \n  ⧉   DATA (canonical tick/bar datasets, provenance-fingerprinted)\n  → FEATURES (same causal contract as live: 50D base, governed 70D assembly)\n  → LABELING (triple-barrier, purged + embargoed)\n  → TRAINING (deterministic seeds, walk-forward)\n  → BACKTEST (friction-aware: spread / slippage / latency)\n  → WALK-FORWARD VALIDATION\n  → OOS GATE (hard: failure ⇒ REJECTED)\n  → ROBUSTNESS STRESS\n  → COUNTERFACTUAL / STRATIFICATION EVIDENCE\n  → CANDIDATE REGISTRY (content-addressed)\n  → SHADOW COMPARISON (zero order authority)\n  → OPERATOR-GATED PROMOTION   \n Key guarantees \n \n  Leakage prevention (INV-008):  purged + embargoed walk-forward \n \n (Lopez de Prado); broker history REPLACE+ALIGN"}, {"u": "/de/architecture/runtime-certification-gate/", "t": "Runtime Certification Gate — canonical pre-push contract [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Architektur  /  runtime certification gate  \n Runtime Certification Gate — canonical pre-push contract \n   CHANGE-ID:  CHG-0051 ·  TASK-ID:  TASK-RUNTIME-GATE ·  Status:  ACTIVE   One command. One answer.   python scripts/ci/runtime_gate.py   \n 1. Purpose \n The repository has many test families (runtime, features, 50D/70D, models, \n database, execution, providers, research, CLI, observability, installer, \n integration). The problem was never test count — it was the absence of ONE \n strong, trustworthy, repeatable command answering: \n  \"Is the composed runtime safe, coherent, loadable, and operational enough  for an agent to push its change?\"  \n The Runtime Certification Gate is that command. It is a **curated, layered \n certification of the REAL composed runtime** — not \"run all pytest\". It \n exercises the actual boot path (config → adapter →  LiveEngine  service \n graph → decision pip"}, {"u": "/de/architecture/runtime/", "t": "Runtime — the LiveEngine Loop [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Architektur  /  Laufzeit  \n Runtime — the LiveEngine loop \n  application/live_engine.py  is the orchestrator: a single async event loop \n that drives the tick pipeline and coordinates background workers. \n Startup sequence \n \n Launcher binds an adapter ( DirectMT5Adapter  /  RemoteMT5GatewayAdapter  / \n \n paper) behind  IMT5Port . \n \n Pre-flight  doctor gate : MT5 terminal present? config valid? platform \n \n supported? — otherwise the engine refuses to start. \n \n Migration gate: canonical DB migration engine runs (additive, checksummed). \n Model load: Champion bundle validated by the  10-gate load gate  (manifest \n \n hash, scaler dim, schema family, width contract…). \n \n Mode select:  PAPER (default)  / SHADOW / LIVE (interactive confirmation). \n Web server: FastAPI Control Center + SSE + WebSocket. \n Workers start (audit writer, research, hygiene, incidents, Telegram). \n \n Tick pipeli"}, {"u": "/de/architecture/system-map/", "t": "System Map [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Architektur  /  Systemkarte  \n System Map \n Package inventory ( src/nexus_scalp/ ) \n  ⧉   nexus_scalp/\n├── domain/            frozen Pydantic contracts (TickData, TradeProposal, …)\n├── ports/             IMT5Port · IGatewayPort        ← the hexagon seam\n├── adapters/          mt5/ (Win32 IPC) · gateway (ZMQ) · paper/ · database/ (AuditRepository, WAL)\n├── features/          scalp_features (50D) · schema registry · schema_contract (70D SSoT)\n│                      liquidity_engine · regime_classifier · temporal (research)\n├── models/            ScalpNet (dual-path TCN + self-attention)\n├── training/          walk_forward_trainer · labeling/ (triple-barrier)\n├── signals/           policy · rule matrix (~30 SMC rules)\n├── strategies/        factory (+ provider_gate for LLM/AI services)\n├── risk/              RiskEngine (Kelly sizing, clamps, kill switch)\n├── execution/         order_manag"}, {"u": "/de/contributing/add-language/", "t": "Adding a Language [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Mitwirken  /  Sprache hinzufügen  \n Adding a Language \n The multilingual architecture is data-driven: adding Turkish, French, Russian, \n Chinese or Japanese is a directory + registry entry — no code changes. \n Recipe \n \n  Create the language tree  \n \n  ⧉      site/content/&lt;lang&gt;/            # translated site content (mirror of en tree)\n   docs/&lt;lang&gt;/index.md            # optional docs-root landing page   \n \n  Register the language  in  scripts/docs/site_config.py : \n \n  ⧉      LANGUAGES = {\n       &quot;en&quot;: {&quot;name&quot;: &quot;English&quot;, &quot;dir&quot;: &quot;ltr&quot;},\n       &quot;fa&quot;: {&quot;name&quot;: &quot;فارسی&quot;,   &quot;dir&quot;: &quot;rtl&quot;},\n       ...\n       &quot;tr&quot;: {&quot;name&quot;: &quot;Türkçe&quot;,  &quot;dir&quot;: &quot;ltr&quot;},   # ← new\n   }   \n \n  Translate core pages first  (in priority order): \n \n  index  →"}, {"u": "/de/contributing/contribution-guide/", "t": "Contribution Guide [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Mitwirken  /  Beitragsleitfaden  \n Das Repository wird von koordinierten Agenten unter einem strengen Ingenieursvertrag entwickelt; menschliche Beitragende profitieren von derselben Disziplin. \n Bootstrap \n  ⧉   git clone https://github.com/Opselon/NexusTradingForexBot.git\ncd NexusTradingForexBot\npython -m venv .venv &amp;&amp; .\\.venv\\Scripts\\Activate.ps1\npip install -e .[dev]\npytest tests/unit -q   \n Änderungsdiziplin \n \n  Lies zuerst das Engineering-Gedächtnis :  \">https://github.com/Opselon/NexusTradingForexBot/blob/main/agents/skill.md\">  agents/skill.md   (Architekturkarte),  \">https://github.com/Opselon/NexusTradingForexBot/blob/main/agents/runtime_invariants.md\">  agents/runtime_invariants.md  ,  \">https://github.com/Opselon/NexusTradingForexBot/blob/main/agents/bugs.md\">  agents/bugs.md  . \n  Beanspruche, bevor du programmierst  — füge eine Zeile zu  agents/taskboard.md  hinzu"}, {"u": "/de/contributing/documentation/", "t": "Documentation Workflow [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Mitwirken  /  Dokumentations-Workflow  \n Documentation Workflow \n Ownership \n Documentation is owned by the  Nexus-Docs  role \n (registry:  docs/agent_handoffs/DOCS_REGISTRY.md ). The boundary is hard: \n docs changes never touch runtime code, and code owners never need to fix docs \n tooling. If documentation exposes a suspected code defect, it is recorded in \n the registry with subsystem attribution — the implementation stays untouched. \n Information architecture \n  ⧉   docs/            engineering documentation (markdown, this IA tree)\nsite/            GitHub Pages source (builds docs/ + translations into a static site)\nscripts/docs/    validation tooling (check_docs.py, check_translations.py, build_site.py)\n.github/workflows/docs.yml    docs CI + Pages deploy   \n Source of truth \n \n  English  is the source language; every other language is a translation \n \n with status metadata ( com"}, {"u": "/de/engineering/ci/", "t": "CI Architecture [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Engineering  /  CI-Architektur  \n CI Architecture \n Workflows \n  \n   Workflow  Trigger  Purpose    \n   ci.yml   push (main/develop/ci-tests), PR, weekly drift scan  ruff · format · mypy · pytest (critical; matrix arms for integration/e2e/research/model on demand)  \n   tests-os.yml   matrix OS runs  cross-platform unit sanity  \n   security.yml   PR + weekly schedule  CodeQL + Trivy  \n   osv-scanner.yml   schedule  dependency vulnerabilities  \n   lockfile-diff.yml   dependency file changes  lockfile drift  \n   js-tests.yml   Web/ changes   node --check  + JS tests  \n   release.yml    v*  tags  only   build + verify + publish release artifacts  \n   docker.yml   Docker surface changes  image build gates  \n   docs.yml   docs/site/README changes  documentation validation + Pages deploy (this platform)  \n   \n Trigger policy (CI_TRIGGER_POLICY v1): tags never fire CI (release-only), main \n pus"}, {"u": "/de/engineering/quality/", "t": "Quality & Testing [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Engineering  /  Qualität &amp; Tests  \n Quality &amp; Testing \n The quality gate \n Every push passes  beforePush.sh  /  beforePush.ps1  (5 stages): \n \n  ruff check  (lint) \n  ruff format  check \n  mypy src  \n  CRITICAL suite  pytest run ( tests/critical_suite.txt , ~779 tests, \n \n RAM-aware xdist workers, coverage) \n \n Forensic  deploy gate  writing  artifacts/forensics/deploy_gate_result.json  \n \n  -FullSuite  runs the whole ~1931-test unit corpus. CI mirrors the gate \n ( .github/workflows/ci.yml ) and adds CodeQL, Trivy, OSV, lockfile-diff and JS \n tests on separate workflows. \n Test architecture \n  \n   Suite  Location  Character    \n  Unit   tests/unit/   ~1900 tests; critical subset in  critical_suite.txt   \n  Integration   tests/integration/   API + engine-level, run standalone/sequential in CI  \n  Golden   tests/golden/  +  test_*_golden.py   byte/behavior-identical extraction ga"}, {"u": "/de/engineering/release-process/", "t": "Release Process [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Engineering  /  Release-Prozess  \n Release Process \n Versioning \n Semver, single canonical source:  pyproject.toml  ( version = \"9.0.6\" ) \n stamped into every build artifact. The README never hard-codes a conflicting \n version — it defers to  nexus version  / the release metadata. \n Pipeline ( .github/workflows/release.yml ) \n Tag-triggered  only  ( v* ). Stages: \n \n Validate tag vs version metadata \n Run the critical test suite (a release run that fails the suite does not \n \n publish — see the v9.0.6 re-cut history in the taskboard) \n \n Build Windows x64 artifacts:  NexusScalpEngine-&lt;version&gt;-win-x64-setup.exe  \n \n + portable  .zip  (PyInstaller) \n \n Generate SHA-256 digests, release manifest, SBOM; embed manifest in the \n \n portable bundle \n \n Publish GitHub Release \n  Post-publish verification  ( release/verify.py ): checksums, manifest \n \n paths, embedded layout (BUG-160 line"}, {"u": "/de/engineering/security/", "t": "Security [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Engineering  /  Sicherheit  \n Security \n Secrets \n \n Secrets live in the  settings DB  / secret store — never in  live.yaml , \n \n never committed (INV-010). Provider URLs/keys are redacted in health \n endpoints and logs ( [REDACTED_SECRET] ). \n \n  scripts/ci/scan_secrets.py  fails CI on secret-shaped strings in \n \n source/config/docs. \n \n Diagnostics export ( nexus export-diagnostics ) is sanitized by contract — \n \n never contains secrets. \n Scanning (CI) \n CodeQL (SAST), Trivy (containers/FS), OSV dependency scanning, lockfile-diff, \n secret scan — see  CI architecture . \n Trust boundaries \n  \n   Boundary  Rule    \n  broker ↔ engine   IMT5Port  adapters only; account-identity fail-safe at connect  \n  research/learning ↔ execution  zero order authority (INV-002); shadow never mutates execution  \n  observability ↔ trading  incidents/forensics are diagnostic-only  \n  Telegram  read-only "}, {"u": "/de/getting-started/configuration/", "t": "Configuration [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Einstieg  /  Konfiguration  \n Configuration \n Configuration has three layers with different authorities. Mixing them up is a \n classic failure mode — read this page before editing YAML by hand. \n 1.  AppConfig  (bootstrap / import / export) \n  src/nexus_scalp/configuration/config.py  — loads the YAML contract \n ( configs/base.yaml  is the canonical base;  configs/live.yaml.example  is the \n live-shaped example). Used for bootstrap/import/export only. \n 2. Runtime configuration (authoritative live state) \n  RuntimeConfiguration  via  RuntimeConfigStore.get_snapshot()  is the \n  authoritative live state  — versioned, hot-reloadable. Consumers must read \n through  get_snapshot() , never cached constructor values. Scope tags decide \n when a change applies ( LIVE_IMMEDIATE  vs  NEXT_DECISION ). \n 3. Settings DB (secrets + user intent) \n Credentials (e.g. Telegram) live in the settings datab"}, {"u": "/de/getting-started/first-run/", "t": "First-Run Safety [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Einstieg  /  Erster Lauf  \n First-Run Safety (Demo → Shadow → Live) \n This engine executes on a real broker. The repository's own first-run guidance \n is a strict ladder — do not skip steps. \n  \n   Step  Action  Why    \n  1️⃣  Log into a  DEMO account  in MT5 ( File → Open an Account → Practice/Demo ), confirm the account number/label before touching the bot  LIVE and demo accounts can look identical in MT5's login window  \n  2️⃣  MT5:  Tools → Options → Expert Advisors → tick \"Allow Algo Trading\"   Without this, orders are rejected  \n  3️⃣  Copy  configs/live.yaml  →  configs/demo.yaml ; set demo credentials; confirm  risk.max_concurrent_positions: 1 ,  risk.risk_per_trade_pct  (e.g. 0.5),  risk.max_account_drawdown_pct   Never touch a live config while real money can be reached  \n  4️⃣  Run  SHADOW  first ( nexus start --mode shadow ) for days; review the dashboard + Telegram reports"}, {"u": "/de/getting-started/installation/", "t": "Installation [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Einstieg  /  Installation  \n Nexus Scalp Engine ist eine  forschungsgetriebene quantitative Handelsplattform : eine hexagonale, ereignisgesteuerte Scalping-Runtime für MetaTrader 5 (Hauptmarkt: XAUUSD M1), die Marktdaten, kausale Feature-Technik, Modellinferenz, Strategie-Policy, Risikokontrolle, Replay, Ausführung, Observability und reproduzierbare Validierung zu einer prüfbaren Pipeline verbindet. \n &lt;div class=\"callout\"&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kein Gewinnversprechen.&lt;/strong&gt; Das ist eine Forschungs- und Ingenieursplattform. Statusangaben sind evidenzbasiert graduiert, und negative Ergebnisse werden veröffentlicht — einschließlich der Ablehnung unseres eigenen 70D-Forschungskandidaten auf Basis von Out-of-Sample-Evidenz. Leveraged Scalping birgt extremes finanzielles Risiko.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt; \n Was es anders macht \n \n  Evidenz vor Behauptungen  — Metriken ohne Evidenz "}, {"u": "/de/getting-started/quickstart/", "t": "Quickstart [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Einstieg  /  Quickstart  \n Schnellstart \n  ⧉   # 1. Installation (Entwickler, aus dem Quellcode)\ngit clone https://github.com/Opselon/NexusTradingForexBot.git\ncd NexusTradingForexBot\npython -m venv .venv &amp;&amp; .\\.venv\\Scripts\\Activate.ps1   # Linux: source .venv/bin/activate\npip install -e .[dev]\n\n# 2. System prüfen\nnexus doctor          # Diagnose (nur Lesen), 19 Kategorien + Lösungsvorschläge\nnexus health          # READY / DEGRADED / NOT READY\n\n# 3. Starten — PAPER als Standard, niemals stillschweigend LIVE\nnexus start           # Paper-Simulation, Control Center unter http://127.0.0.1:8080\n\n# 4. Mit echten Daten evaluieren, null Order-Autorität\nnexus start --mode shadow\n\n# 5. Stoppen\nnexus stop            # für --daemon; Strg+C im Vordergrund   \n Modi \n  \n   Modus  Daten  Orders  Verwendung    \n   paper  (Standard)  simuliert  simuliert  erster Start, UI, Entwicklung  \n   shad"}, {"u": "/de/guides/api/", "t": "API Reference [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Anleitungen  /  API-Referenz  \n API Reference \n The Control Center backend is a FastAPI application exposing * 203  /api/   \n endpoints across 22 groups** (verified by scanning the route modules in \n  src/nexus_scalp/web/ ), plus Server-Sent Events for ticks and WebSocket for \n the dashboard. Everything the UI does, the API does — the UI is a consumer of \n the same surface. \n  HINWEIS  Endpoint counts are generated from the repository's actual route decorators —  they drift with the code, and the docs doctor flags stale counts.  \n Discovery \n \n  Health / readiness:   GET /health  →  200  with  READY / DEGRADED ,  503  when NOT READY. \n  Engine state:   GET /api/status  and  GET /api/live/state  (the dashboard heart, includes the effective serving contract). \n  OpenAPI:  the FastAPI app serves its schema at  /openapi.json  and Swagger UI at  /docs  on the same port as the UI (  http://1"}, {"u": "/de/guides/cli/", "t": "CLI Guide [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Anleitungen  /  CLI-Anleitung  \n CLI Guide \n  nexus  is the application command (installation lifecycle lives in \n  install.ps1 ; everything you  operate  lives in  nexus ). From source: \n  python -m nexus_scalp.cli.main  (alias  nse ). \n Commands \n  ⧉   nexus help            # same authoritative surface as --help (+ &#x27;nexus help start&#x27;)\nnexus version         # build identity (--json / --plain)\nnexus doctor          # read-only diagnostics (19 categories) + suggested fixes\nnexus status          # health + environment + version\nnexus health          # quick health summary (READY / DEGRADED / NOT READY)\nnexus config          # inspect/validate active configuration (secrets masked)\nnexus start           # PAPER mode by default — never LIVE silently\nnexus stop / restart  # control the background engine (honest dead-pid reporting)\nnexus logs [--tail N] [--errors]\nnexus test --mode "}, {"u": "/de/guides/common-workflows/", "t": "Common Workflows [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Anleitungen  /  Typische Workflows  \n Common Workflows \n 1. Daily development loop \n  ⧉   git pull &amp;&amp; .venv/Scripts/Activate.ps1        # Windows dev\nnexus test --mode quick                        # fast sanity\n# ... edit ...\npytest tests/unit -q -k &quot;70 or schema&quot;         # targeted suite\n./beforePush.ps1 -SkipPush                     # full gate before pushing   \n 2. Evaluate the engine on real data (risk-free) \n  ⧉   nexus start --mode shadow      # live feed, zero order authority\n# observe Control Center → SHADOW section: disagreement analysis, drift, health\nnexus stop   \n 3. Research a candidate \n  ⧉   nexus model-dataset-build      # canonical dataset (fingerprinted)\nnexus model-experiment-create  # fair A/B/C protocol\nnexus model-train              # deterministic, seeded\nnexus model-validate           # walk-forward + OOS gate + robustness\nnexus model-replay   "}, {"u": "/de/guides/troubleshooting/", "t": "Troubleshooting [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Anleitungen  /  Fehlerbehebung  \n Troubleshooting \n  Rule of thumb:  nexus doctor  first — it reports 19 diagnostic categories  with suggested fixes and is the same gate the engine runs pre-launch.  \n Engine refuses to start \n  \n   Symptom  Likely cause  Action    \n  \"MT5 terminal missing/not running\"  terminal closed / not installed  start MT5, log in (demo first), retry  \n  config validation error  YAML contract violation   nexus config --validate &lt;path&gt; ; fix the named key  \n  environment blocked (exit 3)  Windows ARM64  unsupported by dependency stack; use x64  \n  migration gate failure  schema drift   nexus db migrate ; check  nexus db hygiene status   \n   \n UI / dashboard \n  \n   Symptom  Likely cause  Action    \n  dashboard unreachable  port drift (dev UI/API ports can move)  check  nexus status  output / launcher log for the bound port  \n  \"Cannot GET /\" on some port  wron"}, {"u": "/de/docs-hub/", "t": "Nexus Scalp Engine — Documentation [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Doku-Hub  \n Nexus Scalp Engine — Documentation \n  Research-driven quantitative trading platform  — a hexagonal, event-driven \n scalping engine for MetaTrader 5 (primary market: XAUUSD M1), built around \n causal feature engineering, artifact-first model governance, deterministic \n research tooling, and forensic observability. \n  WICHTIG  This documentation describes a  research and engineering platform . It is  not investment advice, and nothing here is a promise of profitability.  Leveraged scalping carries extreme financial risk. See   Project Status  for what is certified vs experimental.  \n Start here \n  \n   Question  Page    \n  What is Nexus and why does it exist?   Vision   \n  How do I run it?   Quickstart   \n  How is the architecture structured?   Architecture Overview   \n  How does data become a decision?   Data Flow   \n  How is research validated?   Research Methodology   \n  Wh"}, {"u": "/de/project/capabilities/", "t": "Capability Matrix [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Projekt  /  Fähigkeitsmatrix  \n Capability Matrix \n Legend: ✅ Certified · 🟢 Implemented · 🟡 Experimental · 🔵 Research · 🚧 In \n progress · 📌 Planned · ⚪ Not verified \n  \n   Capability  Status  Evidence (repository)  Notes    \n  Causal 50D feature engine ( scalp_v1 )  ✅ Certified   features/scalp_features.py , schema registry, golden/parity tests  live contract; NaN/Inf deterministic fallback  \n  70D canonical contract ( scalp_v3 )  🟢 Implemented (research)   features/schema_contract.py  SSoT, hash, inference validator (10 rejection codes)  candidate-only; negative OOS evidence so far  \n  Liquidity intelligence (10D block)  🟡 Experimental   features/liquidity_engine.py , INV-019 causality rules  research series; governed by  liquidity_features_enabled   \n  News intelligence 10D + bounded gate  🟡 Experimental   news/ , gate bounds boost ≤0.05 / penalty ≤0.10  opt-in, disabled by default; "}, {"u": "/de/project/milestones/", "t": "Milestones & Project Story [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Projekt  /  Meilensteine  \n Milestones — the project story \n This is a factual history reconstructed from the repository's own records \n (taskboard, decision records, forensic reports). No invented narrative. \n Phase I — Engine core (single-agent era) \n The original engine: hexagonal architecture, MT5 adapters, 50D causal features, \n ScalpNet, policy matrix, risk engine, order manager, SQLite WAL ledger, \n FastAPI Control Center. Foundation invariants established: no sync DB on the \n tick path, no order authority for learning components. \n Phase II — Multi-agent forensic era \n Development moved to a  multi-agent model  (up to 56+ parallel AI agents) with \n a strict engineering contract: taskboard, locks, bug ledger, runtime invariants, \n change control. The bug ledger (BUG-001…) and forensic acceptance reports date \n from this era. Key products: database hygiene, migrations, incident r"}, {"u": "/de/project/roadmap/", "t": "Roadmap [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Projekt  /  Roadmap  \n Formulierungsdiziplin: Punkte sind  Geplant ,  In Bewertung ,  Forschungsrichtung  oder  Abgeschlossen  — niemals „bald\", niemals garantiert. \n JETZT (aktiv) \n  \n   Strom  Punkt  Status    \n  VALIDIERUNG  Wiederaufbau der 70D-Kandidaten-Evidenz (korrigierte Confidence-Semantik, CHG-0042)  In Bewertung  \n  FORSCHUNG  Vertiefung der kontrafaktischen Evidenz (CHG-0041)  In Arbeit  \n  ARCHITEKTUR  Aufteilung großer Dateien mit Golden-Tests (CHG-0032-A1)  In Arbeit  \n  RUNTIME  Härtung des Record-Builder-Vertrags (BUG-185)  Abgeschlossen  \n   \n ALS NÄCHSTES \n  \n   Strom  Punkt  Abhängigkeiten    \n  ML  70D-Promotionsentscheidung — operator-gesteuert oder ehrliche Einstellung  validierter Kandidat + 14-Gate-Verifikation  \n  VALIDIERUNG  Kontrafaktisch-getriebenes Policy-Review  kontrafaktische Ergebnisse  \n  DOCS  100% Übersetzungsabdeckung der Kernseiten  Übersetzungs"}, {"u": "/de/project/scope/", "t": "Scope [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Projekt  /  Umfang  \n Scope \n In scope \n \n A complete quantitative trading  pipeline : data adapters (MT5/paper/gateway), \n \n causal feature engineering (50D active contract; 60D/70D research family), \n deep model inference (ScalpNet TCN + self-attention), SMC policy matrix, \n invariant risk engine, execution with 60-scenario router, SQLite WAL \n accounting ledger, experience/autopsy intelligence, research &amp; validation \n (walk-forward, OOS gate, robustness), replay and shadow runtimes, model \n governance, observability (structured logs, incidents, forensics, Telegram), \n FastAPI Control Center UI, packaged Windows release + installer + update/rollback. \n \n  Multi-agent engineering memory : architecture map, bug ledger, runtime \n \n invariants, contracts, taskboard, decision records — treated as first-class \n repository artifacts. \n Out of scope (by design) \n \n Multi-broker support b"}, {"u": "/de/project/status/", "t": "Project Status [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Projekt  /  Projektstatus  \n Projektstatus \n  WICHTIG  Status-Labels sind evidenzbasiert. „Implementiert\" = im Code vorhanden und  von Tests abgedeckt. „Zertifiziert\" = zusätzlich mit formaler forensischer  Abnahme. Hier wird keine Rentabilität versprochen.  \n Überblick \n  \n   Dimension  Status  Belege    \n  Version   9.0.6  (Semver, einzelne Quelle  pyproject.toml )  Release-Pipeline  \n  Releases   Veröffentlicht  (v9.0.0 → v9.0.6; SHA-256, Manifeste, SBOM)  GitHub Releases  \n  Runtime  Gehärtet; PAPER als Standard; LIVE nur mit Bestätigung  CLI-Vertrag + Pre-Flight-Doctor  \n  Live-Ausführung  Funktional (MT5 Win32 IPC + ZMQ-Gateway) mit Account-Fail-Safe  BUG-142-Regressionsuite  \n  Forschungsschleife  Ende-zu-Ende (Datensätze → Walk-Forward → OOS-Gate)  research/-Suites  \n  Live-Vertrag 50D ( scalp_v1 )   AKTIV    features/schema.py   \n  70D-Vertrag ( scalp_v3 )  Forschungs-SSoT;  n"}, {"u": "/de/project/vision/", "t": "Vision & Why [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Projekt  /  Vision &amp; Warum  \n Vision — warum Nexus? \n Das Problem \n Algorithmische Handelsprojekte scheitern meist auf eine von zwei Arten: \n \n  Sie verstecken die Wahrheit.  Metriken sind fabriziert oder optimistisch, \n \n Fehler passieren still, und die Lücke zwischen Backtest und Runtime wird nie \n gemessen. \n \n  Sie leaken die Zukunft.  Features oder Labels verwenden Informationen, \n \n die zum Entscheidungszeitpunkt nicht verfügbar waren — Ergebnisse sind \n strukturell ungültig, egal wie gut sie aussehen. \n Der Nexus Scalp Engine wurde gezielt gegen beide Fehlermodi gebaut: eine \n  vollständige, prüfbare Pipeline  — Marktdaten → Features → Modell → \n Policy → Risiko → Ausführung → Buchhaltung → Forschung — in der jede Stufe \n beobachtbar, jede Identität mit Fingerabdruck versehen und jede Aussage \n falsifizierbar ist. \n Philosophie (im Repository verankert) \n \n  Belege vor Behau"}, {"u": "/de/reference/cli-reference/", "t": "CLI Reference [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Referenz  /  CLI-Referenz  \n CLI Reference \n The authoritative surface is always  nexus help  /  nexus &lt;command&gt; --help  \n (this page documents the verified contract; the CLI is golden-tested by 66 \n end-to-end tests). \n Global flags \n  \n   Flag  Effect    \n   --json   machine-readable output (parity-tested keys)  \n   --plain   no color, no formatting  \n   --no-color   disable color only  \n   \n Command groups \n  \n   Command  Purpose  Notes    \n  `nexus start [--mode paper\\  shadow\\  live] [--port N] [--daemon]`  run engine  paper default; live needs interactive  --yes /confirmation; port default 8080  \n   nexus stop  /  nexus restart   daemon control  pidfile-based; dead-pid reported honestly (BUG-172)  \n   nexus doctor   19-category diagnostics + suggested fixes   --json  for tooling  \n   nexus status  /  nexus health   environment + health  READY / DEGRADED / NOT READY  \n   nex"}, {"u": "/de/reference/faq/", "t": "FAQ [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Referenz  /  FAQ  \n FAQ \n  Was ist Nexus?  \n Eine forschungsgetriebene quantitative Handelsplattform: hexagonale, ereignisgesteuerte Scalping-Engine für MetaTrader 5 (XAUUSD M1) mit kausalen Features, tiefen Modellen, invariantem Risiko, deterministischer Forschung und forensischer Observability. \n  Ist das ein Live-Trading-Bot?  \n Er  kann  Live-Trades ausführen — aber PAPER ist der Standardmodus, SHADOW hat null Order-Autorität, LIVE erfordert explizite interaktive Bestätigung, und das Repository veröffentlicht abgelehnte Kandidaten. Das ist eine Forschungsplattform mit einer Runtime, keine Geldmaschine. \n  Kann ich es ohne MT5 ausführen?  \n Ja — PAPER-Modus und die gesamte Testsuite laufen ohne Broker; Docker funktioniert ab Werk im PAPER-Modus. \n  Was ist 70D?  \n Der kanonische Forschungs-Feature-Vertrag (50 Basis + 10 News + 10 Liquidität). Nicht live — der Live-Vertrag ist 50D. D"}, {"u": "/de/reference/glossary/", "t": "Glossary [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Referenz  /  Glossar  \n Glossary \n Project-specific terms. Product/module names (Nexus, ScalpNet, OrderManager, \n MT5, 70D, 50D) are canonical and never translated in code; each language's \n  terminology file  defines how they are presented. \n  \n   Term  Meaning in NSE    \n   50D / scalp_v1   the 50-dimensional causal base feature contract — the ACTIVE live feature schema  \n   70D / scalp_v3   the canonical research feature contract: Base 50 (0..49) + News 10 (50..59) + Liquidity 10 (60..69); candidate-only, not live  \n   scalp_v4   a candidate 70D-family contract (integration-era); classified LEGACY/semantically-different vs v3  \n   Schema hash   SHA-256 over canonical JSON of feature (index, name, family) — reordering invalidates models  \n   ScalpNet   dual-path model: 2D MLP for single-tick snapshots, 3D TCN + self-attention for sequences; 4-logit head  \n   Champion / Challenger   p"}, {"u": "/de/reference/terminology/", "t": "Terminology & Translations [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Referenz  /  Terminologie &amp; Übersetzungen  \n Terminology &amp; Translations \n Untranslatable canon \n These stay in English/Latin script in every language (identifiers, contracts, \n product names): \n `Nexus · ScalpNet · OrderManager · RiskEngine · LiveEngine · IMT5Port · \n AuditRepository · MT5 · ZMQ · SQLite · FastAPI · 50D · 70D · scalp_v1 · \n scalp_v3 · NO_TRADE · BUY · SELL · WAIT · Champion · Challenger · Shadow · \n OOS · walk-forward · O(1) · MFE · MAE` \n Canonical term translations \n The authoritative per-language table lives in \n  site/terminology/&lt;lang&gt;.json  (consumed by the translation audit). Core \n entries: \n  \n   EN  FA (فارسی)  ES  AR (العربية)  DE    \n  Feature Vector  بردار ویژگی  Vector de características  متجه السمات  Merkmalsvektor  \n  Feature Contract  قرارداد ویژگی  Contrato de características  عقد السمات  Merkmalsvertrag  \n  Model Registry  ثبت مدل  Regi"}, {"u": "/de/research/backtesting/", "t": "Backtesting [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Forschung  /  Backtesting  \n Backtesting \n Determinism \n Backtests ( research/backtest.py ) are deterministic: fixed seeds, frozen \n datasets, no wall-clock dependence. Same inputs ⇒ same results. \n Friction model \n Spread, slippage and latency are modeled, not ignored: \n \n fills on historical bid/ask (direction-aware), \n tick-level SL/TP first-touch resolution, \n logical latency applied to the decision path, \n robustness stress re-runs under degraded friction (spread/slippage/latency \n \n shocks) — a strategy that only works under ideal fills does not pass. \n Boundary honesty \n \n Backtests produce evidence, not promises. Results feed the validation \n \n pipeline; they never bypass the OOS gate. \n \n Fees/commissions follow the configured friction profile; metrics without the \n \n underlying evidence render  n/a  — never fabricated zeros. \n \n Streaming replay ( research/streaming_replay.py"}, {"u": "/de/research/counterfactuals/", "t": "Counterfactuals [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Forschung  /  Kontrafaktische  \n Counterfactuals (CHG-0041) \n The question \n Backtests score trades that happened. The counterfactual engine asks the \n other question: **what would have happened on the decisions the engine did NOT \n take?** If the engine abstains (NO_TRADE), was the abstention valuable? \n How it works \n  research/counterfactual.py : \n \n Loads canonical tick datasets (fingerprinted, offline) and decision \n \n snapshots from  audit_signals . \n \n Joins each NO_TRADE decision to the tick window at decision time. \n Applies  certified fill semantics  hypothetically at time T. \n Walks ticks forward to compute MFE / MAE / R / cost / time-to-target. \n Classifies each abstention using  documented rules  (never ad-hoc). \n Stratifies evidence by gate, regime, confidence, session, direction. \n \n First evidence run (2026-09-01) \n 2095 NO_TRADE decisions (2026-08-24 → 09-01) walked ov"}, {"u": "/de/research/datasets/", "t": "Datasets [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Forschung  /  Datensätze  \n Datasets \n Bar datasets \n Built by  research/dataset.py  +  model_generation/  with quality gates \n (coverage, ordering, duplicates, horizon boundaries). Each dataset is a \n versioned artifact with a fingerprint ( ds_*  id) used in manifests and run \n snapshots. \n Tick datasets (CHG-0041 / TICK_DATASET_META v2) \n  research/mt5_tick_dataset.py  acquires ticks from the **certified adapter \n surface** ( copy_ticks_range ,  COPY_TICKS_ALL ), with: \n \n bounded, deduplicated acquisition (post BUG-188 semantics), \n immutable parquet store with  content fingerprints , \n provenance metadata v2 (symbol, window, source, acquisition identity), \n cache-hit idempotence — re-running acquisition never duplicates. \n \n After acquisition the dataset is fully  offline : research needs no broker. \n Rules \n \n A dataset is immutable once fingerprinted — corrections produce a new \n"}, {"u": "/de/research/methodology/", "t": "Research Methodology [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Forschung  /  Methodik  \n Forschung existiert, um  falsifizierbare Evidenz  zu erzeugen. Ein Kandidat, der nicht falsifiziert werden kann (kein OOS, keine Replay-Parität, keine Provenienz), berührt den Live-Pfad nie. \n Die Kette \n  ⧉   DATEN (fingerprintierte Datensätze) → FEATURES (kausaler Vertrag) → LABELING (Triple-Barrier)\n→ TRAINING (seeded, deterministisch) → BACKTEST (reibungsbewusst)\n→ WALK-FORWARD (gepurgt + Embargo) → OOS-GATE (Fehlschlag ⇒ REJECTED)\n→ ROBUSTHEITS-STRESS → KONTRAFAKTISCH → REGISTRY → SHADOW → OPERATOR-PROMOTION   \n Komponenten \n \n  Datensätze  — unveränderlich, fingerprintiert, Provenienz getrackt; Tick-Datensätze werden über die zertifizierte Adapterfläche bezogen und sind danach offline. \n  Backtests  — deterministisch; Spread/Slippage/Latenz modelliert. \n  Replay  — bit-exakt vs. Datensatz (Anti-Leakage-Tests); Streaming-Replay führt die geteilte Engine ü"}, {"u": "/de/research/out-of-sample/", "t": "Out-of-Sample Gate [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Forschung  /  OOS-Gate  \n Out-of-Sample (OOS) Gate \n Contract \n  research/oos.py  is a  hard gate : out-of-sample failure ⇒ candidate \n REJECTED, regardless of in-sample performance. There is no override path in \n the pipeline. \n Floors (model lifecycle validation) \n  \n   Metric  Floor    \n  macro-F1 (OOS)  ≥ 0.34  \n  balanced accuracy  ≥ 0.34  \n  calibration error (ECE)  ≤ 0.15  \n  minimum evidence  ≥ 100 rows  \n   \n Evidence the gate bites \n The 70D liquidity candidate — the most heavily engineered research series in \n the repository — was rejected by this exact gate (OOS NOT_ELIGIBLE) after \n real-data walk-forward and shadow benchmarks came back negative/inconclusive. \n A gate that rejects nothing is decoration; this one has a public rejection on \n its record. See  Project Status  and \n  docs/TASK-05-70D-SHADOW-FINAL.md . \n Temporal OOS protocol \n Temporal splits only ( timestamp -"}, {"u": "/de/research/replay/", "t": "Replay [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Forschung  /  Replay  \n Replay \n What replay is \n Replay re-runs the engine's decision logic over historical data and proves it \n produces  the same decisions  the live/training pipeline produced on that \n data. It is the execution-fidelity check between research and runtime. \n Two engines \n  \n   Engine  Module  Character    \n  Dataset replay   model_generation/replay.py  +  replay_70d_vector    bit-exact : replay vector must equal the dataset's stored vector (anti-leakage tests)  \n  Streaming replay   research/streaming_replay.py  (CHG-0035)  shared  LiveEngine  over a logical clock (zero sleeps): incremental bar aggregation, causal 50D + news + liquidity at time T, frozen policy + RiskEngine, direction-aware simulated fills on historical bid/ask, tick SL/TP first-touch, ledger MFE/MAE —  NO  order_send  (test-enforced)   \n   \n Anti-leakage \n Features at time T may consume only inform"}, {"u": "/de/research/reproducibility/", "t": "Reproducibility [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Forschung  /  Reproduzierbarkeit  \n Reproducibility \n Identity chain \n Every research artifact carries the chain that produced it: \n  ⧉   dataset fingerprint → feature schema hash → model manifest (scaler, weights)\n→ git commit → effective config (seeds, splits, purge/embargo)   \n Run snapshots ( research_run_snapshots ) store these at run time; provenance \n fields may be  NOT_RECORDED  (honest) but are never invented or backfilled. \n Determinism sources \n \n seeded training (seed-before-model construction — BUG-101 regression), \n frozen datasets (immutable, fingerprinted), \n logical-clock streaming replay (zero sleeps), \n freeze capture at forward-test cutoff +  post-run re-verification  of the \n \n freeze ( research/forward_test.py ). \n What breaks reproducibility (and is therefore guarded) \n  \n   Threat  Guard    \n  dataset mutation  immutable fingerprinted artifacts  \n  feature reord"}, {"u": "/de/research/validation/", "t": "Validation [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Forschung  /  Validierung  \n Validierung ist der Grund, warum die Plattform existiert. Ein Fehlschlag an irgendeinem Gate ist für diesen Kandidaten terminal — keine Mittelwerte, keine Ausnahmen. \n Die Gate-Kette \n  \n   Ebene  Gates    \n  Datensatz  Qualitäts-Gates · Fingerprint · Provenienz  \n  Features  Schema-Hash · Dimension · Grenzen · Ordnung  \n  Modell  10-Gate-Load-Gate · Kalibrierung · Mindest-Evidenz  \n  Forschung  gepurgtes/embargo Walk-Forward · OOS-Untergrenzen · Robustheit  \n  Governance  14-Gate-Verifikation · Promotion-Transaktion  \n  Runtime  forensisches Deploy-Gate vor jedem Release  \n  Release  SHA-256 · Manifeste · SBOM · Verifikation nach Veröffentlichung  \n   \n OOS-Untergrenzen (Modell-Lebenszyklus) \n macro-F1 ≥ 0.34 · balancierte Genauigkeit ≥ 0.34 · ECE ≤ 0.15 · Evidenz ≥ 100 Zeilen. \n Das Gate beißt — öffentlicher Beweis \n Der 70D-Liquiditätskandidat — die am s"}, {"u": "/de/research/walk-forward/", "t": "Walk-Forward [de]", "l": "de", "x": "  Forschung  /  Walk-Forward  \n Walk-Forward \n Method \n  training/walk_forward_trainer.py  +  research/walkforward.py  implement \n  purged, embargoed walk-forward  (Lopez de Prado): training folds are \n separated from test folds by a purge gap (label horizon) and an embargo gap \n (serial-correlation buffer), evaluated across temporally ordered folds. \n Defaults that matter (BUG-183) \n The production research path once ran with purge/embargo silently disabled — \n the constants existed but weren't wired. This is recorded as BUG-183 and fixed \n with regression tests:  DEFAULT_PURGE_SECONDS = 300 , `DEFAULT_EMBARGO_SECONDS \n = 60  are now wired into  ResearchPipeline.validate_candidate`, \n  OOSGate.evaluate ,  WalkForwardEngine.validate  and  BacktestEngine.run , and \n the  effective  purge/embargo values are recorded in every run's config. \n Why it is non-negotiable \n A walk-forward without"}, {"u": "/de/getting-started/", "t": "Einstieg [de]", "l": "de", "x": "Install, run and configure the engine. PAPER mode is the default; SHADOW gives you live data with zero order authority."}, {"u": "/de/project/", "t": "Projekt [de]", "l": "de", "x": "What Nexus is, what is certified vs experimental, where it is going — all evidence-graded."}, {"u": "/de/architecture/", "t": "Architektur [de]", "l": "de", "x": "How the engine is built: hexagonal layers, the tick-to-decision path, model governance, and the intelligence loop."}, {"u": "/de/research/", "t": "Forschung [de]", "l": "de", "x": "How historical data becomes falsifiable evidence — datasets, backtests, walk-forward, OOS, replay, counterfactuals."}, {"u": "/de/engineering/", "t": "Engineering [de]", "l": "de", "x": "Quality gates, CI architecture, the release process, and the security posture."}, {"u": "/de/guides/", "t": "Anleitungen [de]", "l": "de", "x": "Operating the engine day to day: CLI, REST API, troubleshooting, common workflows."}, {"u": "/de/contributing/", "t": "Mitwirken [de]", "l": "de", "x": "The engineering contract, documentation ownership, and how to add a language."}, {"u": "/de/reference/", "t": "Referenz [de]", "l": "de", "x": "CLI reference, glossary, terminology, and honest answers in the FAQ."}]
